B.aMf=s(["Step 1: Multiply the corresponding X components (u_x * v_x).","Step 2: Multiply the corresponding Y components (u_y * v_y).","Step 3: Sum the two products together and select the choice."],t.s)
B.aQI=s(["Pay attention to negative signs (e.g. (-2) * 3 = -6).","Perpendicular orthogonal vectors always produce a dot product of 0."],t.s)
B.aj0=new A.a8("Vector Dot Product","MATH","Calculate the algebraic inner product of two 2D vectors: u \u2022 v = (u_x * v_x) + (u_y * v_y).","Tap the correct scalar dot product answer.",B.aMf,B.aQI)
B.aX8=s(["Step 1: Read the prompt instruction banner (NUMERICAL vs PHYSICAL SIZE).","Step 2: Inhibit the irrelevant dimension (e.g. ignore large font when comparing numbers).","Step 3: Tap the corresponding side button."],t.s)
B.aCk=s(["Lock your attention onto the active dimension before looking at the stimuli.","Watch out for incongruent trials (e.g. number 9 printed small vs number 2 printed huge)."],t.s)
B.alk=new A.a8("Size-Congruity Stroop","ATTENTION","Rapidly select which number is larger, focusing strictly on either its numerical value or physical font size as instructed.","Tap LEFT or RIGHT.",B.aX8,B.aCk)
B.aO9=s(["Step 1: Compare start and end words to see which letters differ.","Step 2: Look for an intermediate valid word that differs by 1 letter from both.","Step 3: Tap the matching middle word."],t.s)
B.aDa=s(["Verify that the chosen middle word is a valid English dictionary word.","Check letter substitutions position by position."],t.s)
B.ajm=new A.a8("Word Ladder","WORD","Find the bridge word that transitions between start and end words changing only 1 letter at each step.","Tap the valid transition word from the choices.",B.aO9,B.aDa)
B.aLB=s(["Step 1: Watch the illuminated blocks in sequential order.","Step 2: Mentally reverse the visuospatial trajectory.","Step 3: Tap the blocks starting from the last block illuminated back to the first."],t.s)
B.aDW=s(["Anchor the final illuminated block strongly in visual memory as your starting point.","Trace the spatial path backwards across the board."],t.s)
B.aiX=new A.a8("Corsi Backward Span","MEMORY","Observe a sequence of spatial block flashes and tap the blocks in exact reverse (backward) order.","Tap the spatial blocks on screen in reverse sequence.",B.aLB,B.aDW)
B.azw=s(["Step 1: Check the active target rule banner at the top.","Step 2: Observe the presented visual shape (Square vs Circle).","Step 3: Press TARGET if it matches the current rule, else NON-TARGET."],t.s)
B.aOb=s(["Stay alert for rule change notifications.","Inhibit your prior motor reflex as soon as the rule shifts."],t.s)
B.aiV=new A.a8("A-B Rule Reversal","ATTENTION","Respond to target stimuli and switch response rules immediately when the target reverses.","Tap TARGET or NON-TARGET.",B.azw,B.aOb)
B.aJe=s(["Step 1: Scan the scrambled 9-letter pool.","Step 2: Look for common prefixes (DIS-, UN-) and suffixes (-ING, -TION, -FUL).","Step 3: Spell out the complete 9-letter word."],t.s)
B.aJq=s(["Group consonants with matching vowel sounds.","Try constructing the ending first to reveal the root stem."],t.s)
B.aiE=new A.a8("9-Letter Conundrum","WORD","Unscramble all 9 letter tiles into a single valid English word.","Tap letter tiles in order to spell the word; tap BACKSPACE to undo.",B.aJe,B.aJq)
B.axt=s(["Step 1: Inspect the row vectors of the 3x3 binary matrix.","Step 2: Check for identical rows or rows formed by the XOR sum of the other two rows.","Step 3: Tap the corresponding rank."],t.s)
B.aFz=s(["If all three rows are distinct and no row is the XOR sum of others, rank is 3.","If two rows are identical or all rows are multiples, rank is 1 or 2."],t.s)
B.ald=new A.a8("Matrix Rank (GF2)","MATH","Determine the linear algebraic rank (1, 2, or 3) of a 3x3 binary matrix modulo 2.","Tap RANK 1, RANK 2, or RANK 3.",B.axt,B.aFz)
B.aVQ=s(["Step 1: Focus your attention strictly on the center Landolt ring.","Step 2: Filter out the interference from the adjacent flanking rings.","Step 3: Tap the corresponding arrow direction."],t.s)
B.avj=s(["Narrow your attentional spotlight to the central ring boundary.","Don't look at the outer flankers; identify the break in the primary ring."],t.s)
B.agB=new A.a8("Visual Crowding","ATTENTION","Discriminate the gap orientation of the central Landolt ring in the presence of flanking distractor rings.","Tap the directional arrow matching the center gap orientation (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).",B.aVQ,B.avj)
B.aMG=s(["Step 1: Attend carefully to the sequential number stream.","Step 2: When the probe number is shown, search your short-term memory for its immediate successor.","Step 3: Enter the digit on the numpad."],t.s)
B.aR4=s(["Encode digits in rapid pairs (e.g. '3-8', '5-2') to quickly recall successor links.","Maintain a running audio-phonological loop in working memory."],t.s)
B.aj9=new A.a8("Probe Digit Recall","MEMORY","Observe a rapid stream of random digits and recall the number that immediately followed the probe digit.","Tap the digit on the on-screen keypad.",B.aMG,B.aR4)
B.aKA=s(["Step 1: Identify given legs (a, b) and hypotenuse (c).","Step 2: Apply the Pythagorean formula: c = \u221a(a\xb2 + b\xb2) or a = \u221a(c\xb2 - b\xb2).","Step 3: Select the matching integer result."],t.s)
B.aKn=s(["Memorize common primitive triples like (3, 4, 5), (5, 12, 13), (8, 15, 17).","Multiples of triples (e.g. 6, 8, 10) follow the same base ratio."],t.s)
B.aj8=new A.a8("Pythagorean Triples","MATH","Calculate the missing side length in integer right triangles using a\xb2 + b\xb2 = c\xb2.","Tap the correct missing integer value from the options.",B.aKA,B.aKn)
B.aBN=s(["Step 1: Keep both feature dimensions (Red + Square) in mind.","Step 2: Scan the display quickly for the unique combination.","Step 3: Press PRESENT if the Red Square is found, otherwise ABSENT."],t.s)
B.ate=s(["Filter distractors by color first (scan only red items for square contours).","Scan in structured horizontal swaths across the display."],t.s)
B.ahf=new A.a8("Conjunction Search","ATTENTION","Determine whether the target shape (Red Square) is present among color/shape conjunction distractors.","Tap PRESENT or ABSENT.",B.aBN,B.ate)
B.aV_=s(["Step 1: Observe the original 3D wireframe orientation.","Step 2: Mentally rotate the model around its vertical Y-axis by the indicated degrees.","Step 3: Tap the option showing the matching perspective."],t.s)
B.aH7=s(["Track the front-most apex or prominent vertex during rotation.","Eliminate options where base edges reverse depth incorrectly."],t.s)
B.alm=new A.a8("3D Wireframe Rotation","SPATIAL","Identify the correctly rotated 3D wireframe geometric solid after a yaw angular rotation.","Tap the matching rotated wireframe option.",B.aV_,B.aH7)
B.aQp=s(["Step 1: Memorize pairs during the countdown (e.g. 'DOCTOR - HOSPITAL').","Step 2: When presented with 'DOCTOR', locate 'HOSPITAL'.","Step 3: Tap the correct option button."],t.s)
B.aUS=s(["Create vivid semantic connections between pair concepts.","Review the pairs sequentially during the study phase."],t.s)
B.ags=new A.a8("Word Pair Memory","MEMORY","Study paired associations and pick the exact partner word when prompted with a cue.","Tap the matching target word among choices.",B.aQp,B.aUS)
B.azn=s(["Step 1: Locate rows and columns with duplicate numbers.","Step 2: Shade duplicates so only one instance remains visible.","Step 3: Ensure shaded cells are never orthogonally adjacent."],t.s)
B.aMy=s(["If a cell is shaded black, all four orthogonal neighbors must be unshaded (circle them).","Between two identical numbers with one cell in between, the middle cell must be unshaded."],t.s)
B.alj=new A.a8("Hitori","LOGIC","Shade duplicate numbers in the grid such that no row or column contains repeats among unshaded cells, black cells don't touch orthogonally, and unshaded cells remain connected.","Tap a cell once to shade (black), tap twice to circle (safe).",B.azn,B.aMy)
B.au0=s(["Step 1: Check the starting time on the analog clock.","Step 2: Add the given number of hours and reduce modulo 12.","Step 3: Tap the matching hour button."],t.s)
B.aHY=s(["Every 12 or 24 hours returns to the exact same position.","Subtract the largest multiple of 12 first to compute rapidly."],t.s)
B.ajk=new A.a8("Clock Modulo 12","MATH","Calculate cyclical time increments under modulo 12 modular arithmetic.","Tap the button corresponding to the future hour.",B.au0,B.aHY)
B.avH=s(["Step 1: Focus on the center '+' crosshair.","Step 2: Observe the two rapid asynchronous circle flashes.","Step 3: Choose which side flashed first."],t.s)
B.aBz=s(["Do not track eyes side to side; keep your central gaze fixed.","Trust your immediate perceptual intuition."],t.s)
B.aj3=new A.a8("Temporal Order","ATTENTION","Judge which of two brief peripheral circle flashes occurred first.","Tap LEFT FIRST or RIGHT FIRST.",B.avH,B.aBz)
B.aJm=s(["Step 1: Select a piece from the tray.","Step 2: Rotate if necessary to fit the empty board space.","Step 3: Tap the board square to place it."],t.s)
B.aRn=s(["Place awkward pieces (like L and J shapes) first.","Leave square-friendly holes for the O piece."],t.s)
B.agv=new A.a8("Polyomino Tiling","SPATIAL","Arrange and rotate tetromino pieces to tile the 4x4 board completely without overlaps.","Tap a piece to select, tap ROTATE, then tap a grid cell to place.",B.aJm,B.aRn)
B.aNM=s(["Step 1: Check arrow clues indicating the exact number of black cells in that direction.",u.gp,"Step 3: Draw a continuous single loop visiting all remaining empty white cells."],t.s)
B.ax5=s(["Clue cells cannot be visited by the loop and cannot be shaded black.","If a cell is shaded black, the loop must travel around it."],t.s)
B.agr=new A.a8("Yajilin","LOGIC","Draw a single closed loop through unshaded cells and shade cells black according to directional arrow clue counts without adjacent black cells.","Tap cells to draw loop segments; double tap to toggle black shading.",B.aNM,B.ax5)
B.azV=s(["Step 1: Inspect the algebraic expression (e.g. 3x + 5 < 17).","Step 2: Subtract constant terms and divide by the coefficient of x.","Step 3: Select the matching solution (e.g. x < 4)."],t.s)
B.aEt=s(["Perform reverse order of operations (subtract/add first, then divide/multiply).","Keep track of the inequality direction (<, >, \u2264, \u2265)."],t.s)
B.aik=new A.a8("Inequality Solver","MATH","Rapidly isolate the variable and solve linear single-step and two-step inequalities.","Tap the correct simplified inequality expression from the choices.",B.azV,B.aEt)
B.azr=s(["Step 1: Focus on the fast-flashing stream of alphanumeric items.","Step 2: Identify the primary target (green letter) and look for a subsequent 'X'.","Step 3: Report whether the letter 'X' appeared in the stream."],t.s)
B.aKx=s(["Avoid dwelling on the first target so your visual buffer reopens quickly.","Maintain relaxed, steady central gaze focus."],t.s)
B.ajB=new A.a8("Attentional Blink","ATTENTION","Detect whether a second probe letter ('X') appeared during rapid serial visual presentation after the primary target.","Tap YES or NO after the stream finishes.",B.azr,B.aKx)
B.aJl=s(["Step 1: Check pearl positions; white pearls require a straight pass-through, black pearls require an immediate 90\xb0 corner.","Step 2: Connect adjacent nodes by tapping to build the path.","Step 3: Close the loop without branches or dead ends."],t.s)
B.aWF=s(["Black pearls near edges must turn inward.","White pearls along a wall must travel parallel to the border."],t.s)
B.aih=new A.a8("Masyu","LOGIC","Draw a single non-intersecting loop passing through every circle. Pass straight through white circles and turn in adjacent cells; turn at 90\xb0 on black circles and go straight through adjacent cells.","Tap and drag or tap adjacent dots to draw/erase loop segments.",B.aJl,B.aWF)
B.aMP=s(["Step 1: Inspect the two consecutive prime numbers displayed on the cards.","Step 2: Mentally subtract the smaller prime from the larger prime.","Step 3: Select the matching numerical difference from the grid."],t.s)
B.aOh=s(["Twin primes always have a gap of 2 (e.g. 11 & 13, 17 & 19, 41 & 43).","Cousin primes have a gap of 4, and sexy primes have a gap of 6."],t.s)
B.akZ=new A.a8("Prime Gap Hunt","MATH","Calculate the exact arithmetic difference between pairs of consecutive prime numbers.","Tap the correct prime gap number button.",B.aMP,B.aOh)
B.aWD=s(["Step 1: Check rooms with numbers; each specifies the exact count of black cells inside that room.",u.gp,"Step 3: Keep all unshaded white cells connected into a single open path."],t.s)
B.aJg=s(["A room with '0' must have all white cells.","White corridors cannot span across more than two consecutive rooms in a straight line."],t.s)
B.agN=new A.a8("Heyawake","LOGIC","Paint cells black or white in rectangular rooms according to numeric room constraints.","Tap an empty cell once to paint black, tap twice to mark with a green dot.",B.aWD,B.aJg)
B.aXe=s(["Step 1: Read the set expression (e.g., A \u2229 B, A \u222a B, A \\ B, (A \u222a B)').","Step 2: Identify whether the formula targets only A, only B, the intersection, or the outer universe.","Step 3: Toggle the appropriate region cards and submit your answer."],t.s)
B.aWn=s(["Intersection (\u2229) means only the overlapping region.","Union (\u222a) combines all interior parts of both sets.","Complement (') refers to everything outside the specified set."],t.s)
B.akr=new A.a8("Set Theory Venn","MATH","Select the correct regions of the Venn diagram matching the given set theory formula.","Tap regions of the Venn diagram or the outside space to select them, then tap SUBMIT.",B.aXe,B.aWn)
B.aUo=s(["Step 1: Check the prompt rule: Global (Large shape) or Local (Small elements).","Step 2: Inspect the composite figure.","Step 3: Tap the letter corresponding to the active prompt instruction."],t.s)
B.aLY=s(["Do not look at the whole letter if local is requested; zoom into a single pixel letter.","Defocus your gaze slightly to immediately perceive the global shape."],t.s)
B.ahB=new A.a8("Navon Hierarchical","ATTENTION","Identify the requested letter level (Global large letter vs Local small constituent letters) under rapid rule changes.","Tap the matching letter button from the choices.",B.aUo,B.aLY)
B.azQ=s(["Step 1: Check numbered cells; each number indicates the length of consecutive shaded blocks surrounding it.","Step 2: Ensure all black wall cells form a single connected network.","Step 3: Never allow a 2x2 solid block of black wall cells."],t.s)
B.atq=s(["Clue cells can never be shaded black.","A cell with '8' must be surrounded by 8 black cells.","Diagonal blocks separated by unshaded spaces fulfill multiple-number clues like (1, 1) or (1, 2)."],t.s)
B.ah6=new A.a8("Tapa","LOGIC","Paint a continuous black wall such that all clue numbers indicate consecutive wall blocks around each cell, with no 2x2 black squares.","Tap an empty cell once to mark as wall, tap twice to mark with a red dot.",B.azQ,B.atq)
B.aXS=s(["Step 1: Calculate the numerical value of each base raised to its exponent.","Step 2: Tap the smallest power first to form the base of the tower.","Step 3: Stack subsequent powers upward in strict ascending numerical order."],t.s)
B.aVF=s(["Remember key powers of 2 (e.g. 2^5 = 32, 2^6 = 64) and 3 (3^3 = 27, 3^4 = 81).","Compare same bases by their exponents directly."],t.s)
B.agy=new A.a8("Exponent Tower","MATH","Calculate powers and stack exponential expressions in ascending order from smallest to largest.","Tap available power blocks to add them to your tower; tap placed blocks to remove them.",B.aXS,B.aVF)
B.aQ3=s(["Step 1: Keep your focus locked on the central '+' fixation cross.","Step 2: Note the flashing box highlight cue (warning: cues may sometimes be invalid distractors).","Step 3: When the target circle appears, immediately tap the corresponding side button."],t.s)
B.aL0=s(["Do not guess before the target circle actually renders.","Maintain central gaze fixation for the fastest peripheral reaction time."],t.s)
B.agu=new A.a8("Spatial Cueing","ATTENTION","React as quickly and accurately as possible when a target appears on the left or right side of the screen.","Tap LEFT or RIGHT button matching the target position.",B.aQ3,B.aL0)
B.aK0=s(["Step 1: Observe the driving gear rotation direction indicated by the animated arrow.","Step 2: Trace the connection to adjacent gears (meshed gears reverse direction, open belts keep direction, crossed belts reverse direction).","Step 3: Follow the transmission chain to the final gear and submit your answer."],t.s)
B.aE0=s(["Alternate directions for every meshed contact point.","Belts preserve rotation direction unless they cross over in an 'X'."],t.s)
B.akM=new A.a8("Gear Train","SPATIAL","Determine whether the target '?' gear will rotate clockwise or counter-clockwise.","Tap CLOCKWISE or COUNTER-CW.",B.aK0,B.aE0)
B.aWH=s(["Step 1: Study the symbol associations during the countdown study phase.","Step 2: Create a mental mnemonic connecting each cue symbol to its partner.","Step 3: When probed with a cue, tap the matching target from the tray."],t.s)
B.ay4=s(["Invent visual stories linking the two symbols (e.g., 'star fuels the rocket').","Pay attention to the matching color highlights."],t.s)
B.ak9=new A.a8("Paired Associate","MEMORY","Learn pairs of abstract symbols and select the correct matching partner when queried.","Tap the symbol button that was paired with the prompt symbol.",B.aWH,B.ay4)
B.aL3=s(["Step 1: A number counts the white cells in an unbroken line through it, across plus down, with the cell itself counted once.","Step 2: Start with a clue whose number is larger than the room around it. The cells it must reach have to be white.","Step 3: When a clue already sees its number, the cells just past the line on both sides have to be black.","Step 4: Blacken a cell and its four neighbours are white. Keep the white cells in one connected group and the board falls."],t.s)
B.aDg=s(["A clue of 1 on a cell with neighbours means every neighbour is black.","Two black cells can never share an edge, so a black cell settles four cells at once.","If blackening a cell would cut the white cells into two groups, that cell has to be white.","When nothing else moves, try a cell one way and follow the consequences. If it contradicts, the other way is forced."],t.s)
B.aj1=new A.a8("Kurodoko","LOGIC","Blacken cells until every numbered cell sees exactly as many white cells as its number says, counting across and down through itself.","Tap a cell to blacken it, tap it again to mark it white, and a third time to clear it. Numbers cannot be changed.",B.aL3,B.aDg)
B.axY=s(["Step 1: Focus your gaze on the center of the canvas.","Step 2: When the dots flash, capture the pattern as a holistic visual group.","Step 3: Select the exact number of dots you observed."],t.s)
B.axh=s(["Group dots mentally into small clusters of 2, 3, or 4.","Do not count one-by-one; rely on quick visual perception."],t.s)
B.ak1=new A.a8("Subitizing Rush","ATTENTION","Instantly identify the quantity of briefly flashed dots without sequential counting.","Tap the matching number button.",B.axY,B.axh)
B.aEY=s(["Observe: Watch the character execute a sequence of animation gestures (e.g. waving, jumping, bowing).","Memorize: Mentally log each gesture as it happens, creating verbal shorthand names for each (e.g. 'W-J-B').","Interact: When the sequence finishes and inputs unlock, tap the action buttons in the exact same order."],t.s)
B.aUp=s(["Say the actions out loud or repeat them in a rhythm in your head.","Assign simple visual shorthand tags to each movement.","Don't click prematurely; wait for the full sequence to complete before starting input."],t.s)
B.agz=new A.a8("Action Recall","MEMORY","Observe a sequence of character gesture animations and repeat them in the exact order they were shown.","Tap the corresponding action buttons to replay the sequence.",B.aEY,B.aUp)
B.aHK=s(["Step 1: Read the base word displayed in the center of the screen.","Step 2: Look at the multiple-choice affix options (e.g., 'un-', '-ly', 're-').","Step 3: Determine which affix can be legally attached to the base word.","Step 4: Tap the correct affix to build the new word and progress to the next puzzle."],t.s)
B.aU8=s(["Try saying the combined word out loud in your head to see if it sounds like a real word.","Pay attention to the hyphen position to know if you are choosing a prefix (before) or suffix (after).","Eliminate obviously incorrect affixes that break standard English spelling rules."],t.s)
B.ahJ=new A.a8("Affix Factory","WORD","Select the correct prefix or suffix that attaches to a given base word to form a new valid word.","Tap the correct affix button from the multiple-choice options provided.",B.aHK,B.aU8)
B.aKW=s(["Step 1: Look for black cells with numbers. The number indicates exactly how many lightbulbs must be placed adjacent (top, bottom, left, right) to that cell.","Step 2: Place lightbulbs around numbered cells where the placement is forced (e.g., a '4' needs a bulb on all four sides).","Step 3: Lightbulbs illuminate their entire row and column up to the grid edge or a black cell block.","Step 4: Ensure no two lightbulbs illuminate each other.","Step 5: Continue placing bulbs until every empty white cell is illuminated."],t.s)
B.aBw=s(["Start with the highest numbers ('4' or '3') as they often have limited or forced placement options.","If a '0' block is on the grid, you know no bulbs can be placed adjacent to it.","Look for isolated cells that can only be illuminated by a bulb placed in that exact spot or row/column."],t.s)
B.ahg=new A.a8("Akari","LOGIC","Place lightbulbs to illuminate every empty cell in the grid without any two lightbulbs shining on each other.","Tap an empty cell to place a lightbulb. Tap a placed lightbulb to remove it.",B.aKW,B.aBw)
B.aHG=s(["Step 1: Examine the balance scales showing different shapes balancing out a target weight or each other.","Step 2: Treat the scales as algebraic equations (e.g., 2 Triangles + 1 Circle = 15).","Step 3: Solve for the individual values of the shapes using substitution or elimination.","Step 4: Identify the value of the specific target shape marked with a question mark.","Step 5: Enter the correct numerical value using the number pad."],t.s)
B.aKJ=s(["Look for the simplest scale first, especially one that isolates a single type of shape (e.g., 3 Squares = 12 means Square = 4).","Substitute known values into more complex scales to find the remaining unknown values.","Double-check your math by mentally plugging your final answers back into the scales to see if they balance."],t.s)
B.ajd=new A.a8("Algebraic Balance","MATH","Deduce the numerical value of a specific target shape by analyzing visual balance scale equations.","Use the virtual number pad to enter your calculated value, then tap the submit button.",B.aHG,B.aKJ)
B.aWv=s(["Step 1: Analyze the partially filled 4x4 grid and the set of four target letters.","Step 2: Look for a row, column, or 2x2 block that is only missing one letter and fill it in.","Step 3: Use the process of elimination to find cells where only one specific letter can be placed without violating Sudoku rules.","Step 4: Continue filling cells until the entire grid is complete and valid."],t.s)
B.aUP=s(["Focus on the 2x2 subgrids, as they are often the easiest place to spot missing letters.","Cross-reference empty cells by checking both their horizontal row and vertical column constraints.","If you get stuck, look for a specific letter and see which cells in the grid it is blocked from entering."],t.s)
B.aiR=new A.a8("Alphabet Sudoku","LOGIC","Fill a 4x4 grid with four distinct letters such that no letter repeats in any row, column, or 2x2 subgrid.","Tap an empty grid cell, then tap a letter from the selection bar below to fill the cell.",B.aWv,B.aUP)
B.aDt=s(["Step 1: Read the provided definition carefully to understand the target word's meaning.","Step 2: Look at the scrambled letter tiles below the definition.","Step 3: Mentally rearrange the letters to find a word that fits the definition.","Step 4: Tap the letter tiles in order to spell the answer.","Step 5: If incorrect, clear your input and try a different arrangement."],t.s)
B.aLO=s(["Look for common word prefixes (like 'un-', 're-') or suffixes (like '-ing', '-ed', '-tion') among the scrambled letters.","If you're stuck on the letters, focus entirely on the definition and think of synonyms.","Identify the vowels first and try placing them in typical patterns."],t.s)
B.ajJ=new A.a8("Anagram Definition","WORD","Unscramble a given set of letters to form a word that matches the provided dictionary definition.","Tap the scrambled letters in the correct order to spell the word. Tap entered letters to remove them, or use the clear button.",B.aDt,B.aLO)
B.aMh=s(["Step 1: Look at the target angle value (e.g., 45\xb0, 120\xb0) displayed on the screen.","Step 2: Visualize what that angle looks like relative to a 90\xb0 right angle or 180\xb0 straight line.","Step 3: Drag the slider to rotate the dynamic arm until the visual angle matches your estimate.","Step 4: Tap the 'Submit' button to lock in your guess.","Step 5: Aim for high precision to maximize your score over multiple rounds."],t.s)
B.awk=s(["Use benchmark angles: 90\xb0 is a perfect L-shape, 180\xb0 is flat, 45\xb0 is exactly halfway between 0 and 90.","If the target is 135\xb0, think of it as 90\xb0 plus another 45\xb0.","Make small, fine adjustments using the slider before submitting your final answer."],t.s)
B.akh=new A.a8("Angle Finder","SPATIAL","Estimate and recreate a target angle by adjusting a movable protractor arm.","Drag the slider at the bottom of the screen to adjust the angle of the movable arm.",B.aMh,B.awk)
B.auO=s(["Step 1: Note the Target Area (Width \xd7 Height) and Target Perimeter (2 \xd7 (Width + Height)).","Step 2: Observe the current dimensions of the rectangle on the screen.","Step 3: Use the '+' and '-' controls to change the width and height.","Step 4: Find the specific pair of factors that multiply to the target area AND add up to half the target perimeter.","Step 5: The game completes the round automatically when the correct dimensions are reached."],t.s)
B.awI=s(["Focus on the Area first by finding factor pairs (e.g., if Area is 24, pairs are 1x24, 2x12, 3x8, 4x6).","Once you have a factor pair, check if its perimeter matches the target.","A square (or near-square) minimizes perimeter for a given area, while a long, thin rectangle maximizes it."],t.s)
B.agZ=new A.a8("Area Perimeter Match","MATH","Adjust the dimensions of a rectangle until its area and perimeter match the given target values.","Tap the '+' and '-' buttons on the sides of the rectangle to increase or decrease its width and height.",B.auO,B.awI)
B.aIM=s(["Step 1: Memorize the starting number shown on the screen.","Step 2: Watch as a sequence of mathematical operations (e.g., '+ 3', '\xd7 2', '- 4') appears.","Step 3: Perform each calculation mentally on your running total as it appears.","Step 4: Once the chain ends, enter your final calculated value using the number pad."],t.s)
B.aXd=s(["Don't worry about memorizing the individual steps, just focus purely on updating your current running total.","Stay calm during multiplication or division steps, as they usually result in clean integers.","Double-check your final mental calculation before pressing submit."],t.s)
B.ak5=new A.a8("Arithmetic Chain","MATH","Keep a running total in your head as a sequence of arithmetic operations is displayed, and calculate the final result.","Use the virtual number pad to enter your final calculated answer, then tap submit.",B.aIM,B.aXd)
B.aXa=s(["Step 1: Watch the screen as pairs of colors and shapes are presented one by one during the memorization phase.","Step 2: Create a mental link between the shape and the color (e.g., 'Teal Square').","Step 3: After the presentation ends, a recall question will appear asking which color was associated with a specific shape.","Step 4: Select the correct color from the available options to score points."],t.s)
B.aXb=s(["Create a quick story or visualization for each pair (e.g., visualizing a bright 'Amber Circle' as the sun).","Repeat the pairings out loud or in your head as they appear on screen.","Don't let similar colors (like Teal and Blue) confuse you; focus on distinct mental tags."],t.s)
B.ahi=new A.a8("Associative Pairs","MEMORY","Memorize the associations between specific colors and shapes, and accurately recall them when tested.","Tap the correct answer from the multiple-choice options provided during the recall phase.",B.aXa,B.aXb)
B.aXR=s(["Step 1: Fixate your eyes on the center of the screen as a rapid stream of letters flashes by.","Step 2: Stay alert and look for the first number (Target 1) hidden among the letters.","Step 3: Immediately prepare to spot the second number (Target 2), which will appear shortly after.","Step 4: Once the sequence ends, type both numbers in the order you saw them."],t.s)
B.aG3=s(["Do not move your eyes. Keep a soft focus on the exact spot where the characters appear.","Beware of the 'attentional blink'\u2014a split second after spotting the first number, your brain might miss the second one if it appears too quickly. Force yourself to stay alert.","Say the first number out loud the moment you see it to free up your visual attention for the second number."],t.s)
B.ajD=new A.a8("Attentional Blink","ATTENTION","Identify the two numbers that briefly appear within a rapid, continuous sequence of letters.","Use the keyboard to type the first and second target numbers you spotted, then submit.",B.aXR,B.aG3)
B.aLh=s(["Step 1: Review the balance scales displayed on the screen. Each scale represents a mathematical equation.","Step 2: Identify the known weight values (usually represented by standard numbers or shapes you can calculate).","Step 3: Use substitution to find the weight of the unknown items on the scales.","Step 4: Determine the weight of the final target item marked with a question mark.","Step 5: Enter your deduced answer using the number pad."],t.s)
B.aUC=s(["Find a scale where identical items balance a known number to quickly establish a base value.","Treat the scales exactly like algebraic equations. If 2 items balance 10, then 1 item is 5.","Work methodically from the simplest scale to the most complex one."],t.s)
B.agK=new A.a8("Balance Scale","MATH","Deduce the numerical weight of a target item based on visual balance scale equations.","Use the virtual number pad to type your calculated answer, then tap the checkmark submit button.",B.aLh,B.aUC)
B.aUr=s(["Step 1: Look at the top card to see the starting number and its base (e.g., Binary, Octal, Decimal, Hexadecimal).","Step 2: Note the target base you need to convert the number into.","Step 3: Perform the base conversion mentally or using scratch paper.","Step 4: Tap the correct converted value from the options at the bottom of the screen to score a point."],t.s)
B.aTk=s(["When converting to or from Binary, remember the powers of 2 (1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32).","For Hexadecimal, remember that letters A-F represent values 10-15.","If you're stuck, try converting the starting number to Decimal (Base 10) first, as an intermediate step."],t.s)
B.agL=new A.a8("Base Conversion Run","MATH","Convert a given number from its starting numeral base (e.g., Binary, Hex) into a target base.","Tap the correct converted number from the four multiple-choice options.",B.aUr,B.aTk)
B.aIR=s(["Step 1: Read the arithmetic expression provided on the screen.","Step 2: The expression will involve numbers in various bases (indicated by prefixes like '0x' for Hex or '0b' for Binary).","Step 3: Convert the numbers to standard decimal (base 10).","Step 4: Perform the requested arithmetic operation.","Step 5: Enter the final decimal result and submit."],t.s)
B.avN=s(["Memorize basic Hexadecimal values (0xA = 10, 0xF = 15) to speed up conversions.","For Binary, quickly add up the active bits (e.g., 0b1011 = 8 + 0 + 2 + 1 = 11).","Always convert to decimal before attempting the addition or subtraction."],t.s)
B.aib=new A.a8("Base Shift","MATH","Solve an arithmetic expression involving numbers in different bases and input the correct decimal result.","Tap the text field to open the keyboard, type your calculated numerical answer, and tap the submit button.",B.aIR,B.avN)
B.axU=s(["Step 1: Look at the 4-bit binary string (e.g., '1011') displayed in the center of the screen.","Step 2: Calculate the decimal value by summing the powers of 2 (8, 4, 2, 1) where a '1' is present.","Step 3: Find the matching decimal value in the option grid below.","Step 4: Tap the correct option as quickly as possible before the timer runs out."],t.s)
B.at0=s(["Memorize the standard 4-bit values: the first digit is 8, the second is 4, the third is 2, the fourth is 1.","For '1111', know instantly that it equals 15. For '1000', know it equals 8.","Speed is key in this sprint game; trust your quick mental math and tap immediately."],t.s)
B.ahl=new A.a8("Binary Code","MATH","Rapidly translate 4-bit binary strings into their standard decimal integer values.","Tap the correct decimal number from the 2x2 grid of multiple-choice options.",B.axU,B.at0)
B.avo=s(["Step 1: Examine the grid for fixed starting numbers.","Step 2: Look for pairs of identical numbers (e.g., '1-1'). The cells on either side must be the opposite number (e.g., '0-1-1-0').","Step 3: Look for identical numbers separated by one empty cell (e.g., '1-_-1'). The empty cell must be the opposite number ('1-0-1').","Step 4: Ensure every row and column contains exactly half 0s and half 1s.","Step 5: Ensure no two rows are identical and no two columns are identical.","Step 6: Continue deducing cell values until the grid is filled correctly."],t.s)
B.aN4=s(["If a row or column has reached its maximum quota of 1s, fill the remaining empty cells with 0s.","Compare nearly completed rows or columns with existing ones to avoid creating duplicate rows or columns.","Always apply the 'no three in a row' rule first, as it provides the most immediate deductions."],t.s)
B.aln=new A.a8("Binary Puzzle","LOGIC","Fill the grid with 0s and 1s such that no three identical numbers are adjacent, each row and column has an equal number of 0s and 1s, and all rows and columns are unique.","Tap an empty or modifiable cell to toggle its value between empty, 0, and 1.",B.avo,B.aN4)
B.aG2=s(["Step 1: Check the Target weight required to balance the scale.","Step 2: Look at the available binary weight blocks.","Step 3: Tap blocks to add their values to your Current weight.","Step 4: Adjust your selection until the Current weight exactly matches the Target weight.","Step 5: Tap the 'BALANCED?' submit button to verify your answer and move to the next round."],t.s)
B.aKm=s(["Use a greedy approach: always select the largest available block that is smaller than or equal to the remaining target weight.","If the target weight is odd, you must select the '1' block.","This game is essentially converting a decimal number to binary; each selected block represents a '1' bit."],t.s)
B.ali=new A.a8("Binary Scale Balance","MATH","Select the correct combination of binary weight blocks to perfectly match the target weight on the scale.","Tap the binary weight blocks (32, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1) to toggle them on or off, then tap the 'BALANCED?' button to submit.",B.aG2,B.aKm)
B.aRB=s(["Step 1: Look at the expanded quadratic expression (e.g., x\xb2 + 5x + 6) displayed in the center.","Step 2: Determine which two numbers multiply to equal the constant term (c) and add to equal the coefficient of the middle term (b).","Step 3: Review the multiple-choice options of factored binomials.","Step 4: Tap the option that contains the correct pair of numbers (e.g., (x + 2)(x + 3))."],t.s)
B.aTF=s(["Pay close attention to the signs. If the constant term is positive, both numbers have the same sign. If it's negative, they have opposite signs.","If the middle term is negative but the constant is positive, both factored numbers must be negative.","Eliminate options quickly by just checking the multiplication of the two constants in the binomials."],t.s)
B.akY=new A.a8("Binomial Match","MATH","Identify the correct factored form of a given quadratic expression.","Tap the correct factored binomial pair from the multiple-choice list.",B.aRB,B.aTF)
B.aEQ=s(["Step 1: Watch the grid of faces carefully.","Step 2: Various faces will randomly blink once to distract you.","Step 3: Keep your eyes scanning for a specific face that rapidly blinks twice in succession.","Step 4: Once you identify the double-blinking face, tap it to score a point.","Step 5: Repeat this process until you reach the target score."],t.s)
B.aFy=s(["Keep your gaze relaxed and centered on the grid rather than staring intensely at one specific face.","Use your peripheral vision to detect movement, then focus in to verify if it was a single or double blink.","Don't rush your tap; wait to be certain you saw the double blink pattern."],t.s)
B.ak_=new A.a8("Blink Detector","ATTENTION","Identify the target face in a grid that blinks twice, while ignoring distractor faces that blink only once.","Observe the grid, then tap the face that exhibited the double-blink behavior.",B.aEQ,B.aFy)
B.avM=s(["Step 1: Examine the 3D block structure displayed on the screen.","Step 2: Drag to rotate the model and view it from different angles to ensure you don'''t miss hidden blocks.","Step 3: Count the blocks, remembering that any block on a higher tier must be supported by blocks beneath it.","Step 4: Type the total number of blocks using the virtual numpad.","Step 5: Tap the submit button to check your answer."],t.s)
B.aVI=s(["Count column by column. A column that is 3 blocks high contributes 3 to your total.","Rotate the view to look straight down from the top to easily count the base footprint.","Ensure you account for blocks completely hidden in the center of a larger structure."],t.s)
B.al9=new A.a8("Block Count 3D","SPATIAL","Determine the total number of individual cubes that make up a complex 3D block structure.","Drag your finger across the 3D viewport to rotate the structure. Use the virtual numpad to enter your count and tap submit.",B.avM,B.aVI)
B.aQd=s(["Step 1: Identify the distinct target block (usually colored differently) that needs to reach the exit on the right.","Step 2: Locate the blocks obstructing the target block's path to the exit.","Step 3: Drag the obstructing vertical and horizontal blocks out of the way to create a clear lane.","Step 4: Slide the target block through the exit to solve the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aA8=s(["Work backwards: look at the exit and determine which block is directly blocking it, then figure out how to move that specific block.","Horizontal blocks can only move left/right, and vertical blocks can only move up/down.","Sometimes you have to move a block into the target's path temporarily to shuffle other blocks around."],t.s)
B.ahc=new A.a8("Block Escape","LOGIC","Clear a path to slide the target block out of the exit on the right side of the board.","Drag blocks along their horizontal or vertical axis to move them into empty spaces.",B.aQd,B.aA8)
B.atc=s(["Step 1: Watch the active block slide back and forth across the top of the stack.","Step 2: Time your tap so the active block aligns perfectly with the block below it.","Step 3: When you tap, the block drops. Any overhanging portion is sliced off, making your next block smaller.","Step 4: Continue stacking until you reach the target height to win.","Step 5: If you miss the stack entirely, the tower falls and the game is over."],t.s)
B.au6=s(["Focus your eyes on the edges of the stationary block below, and tap exactly when the moving block's edge aligns with it.","As the blocks get smaller, the game gets harder; prioritize perfect alignment early on.","Get into a rhythm, as the block speed increases slightly with each successful drop."],t.s)
B.aka=new A.a8("Stacking Physics","SPATIAL","Stack moving blocks on top of each other as high as possible by timing your drops perfectly.","Tap anywhere on the screen to drop the currently moving active block.",B.atc,B.au6)
B.aVZ=s(["Step 1: Analyze the 2D cross-shaped net containing numbers on its faces.","Step 2: Mentally fold the net into a 3D cube in your mind.","Step 3: Pay attention to the relative orientation of the numbers when folded.","Step 4: Look at the multiple-choice 3D cube options.","Step 5: Select the cube that matches your mental model of the folded net."],t.s)
B.aXL=s(["Find opposing faces on the net (faces separated by exactly one square). These can never be adjacent on the final cube.","Pick a 'front' face on the net and visualize what numbers fold into the top, bottom, left, and right positions.","Use process of elimination to discard cubes showing impossible adjacent faces."],t.s)
B.ahj=new A.a8("Box Completion","SPATIAL","Determine which 3D cube is formed by folding a given 2D net with numbers on it.","Tap the correct 3D cube from the multiple-choice options provided.",B.aVZ,B.aXL)
B.aJk=s(["Step 1: Review the numbered islands on the grid.","Step 2: Tap an island to select it, then tap an orthogonal (up, down, left, right) island to connect them with a bridge.","Step 3: Bridges cannot cross other bridges or islands.","Step 4: Each island must have a total number of connected bridges equal to its number.","Step 5: All islands must be connected together in one single group to solve the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aJ8=s(["Look for corners with '4', edges with '6', or center islands with '8'. These require double bridges in all available directions.","If a '1' island is connected, no other bridges can attach to it.","Ensure you don'''t create an isolated closed loop of islands; the network must be fully connected."],t.s)
B.ahH=new A.a8("Bridges","LOGIC","Connect all islands into a single continuous network with bridges, ensuring each island has exactly the number of bridges indicated by its number.","Tap an island to select it, then tap an adjacent island to draw a bridge. Tap again to upgrade to a double bridge, or tap a third time to remove the connection.",B.aJk,B.aJ8)
B.aM6=s(["Step 1: Tap start to begin the countdown timer.","Step 2: Read the math equation presented in the center of the screen.","Step 3: Quickly calculate the answer.","Step 4: Tap the matching option from the choices below.","Step 5: Answer correctly to increase your score and reach the target goal before time expires."],t.s)
B.aQx=s(["Don'''t overthink; rely on your quick mental math reflexes.","Use estimation or look at the last digit of the numbers to quickly eliminate wrong multiple-choice options.","Maintain a steady rhythm and don'''t panic if you make a mistake."],t.s)
B.ahF=new A.a8("Calculation Sprint","MATH","Solve as many math equations as possible before the time runs out.","Tap the correct answer from the 2x2 grid of multiple-choice options.",B.aM6,B.aQx)
B.aSp=s(["Step 1: Tap start to begin dealing.","Step 2: Watch closely as 5 playing cards are dealt sequentially onto the screen.","Step 3: Keep track of the suits (Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs, Spades) of the cards.","Step 4: After dealing finishes, a question will ask how many cards of a specific suit were shown.","Step 5: Tap the correct number to answer the question and score."],t.s)
B.avW=s(["Instead of memorizing the whole card, keep a mental tally (e.g., '''2 Hearts, 1 Spade, 2 Clubs''') as they are dealt.","Assign fingers on your hand to different suits and tap them to keep count.","Ignore the card ranks (numbers/letters) completely; focus only on the shapes and colors of the suits."],t.s)
B.agq=new A.a8("Card Counting","MEMORY","Memorize a sequence of dealt playing cards and accurately recall how many cards of a specific suit appeared.","Tap the correct numerical count from the multiple-choice options during the recall phase.",B.aSp,B.avW)
B.awS=s(["Step 1: Read the category prompt (e.g., '''Animals''', '''Fruits''') at the top of the screen.","Step 2: Tap the text input field to open your keyboard.","Step 3: Think of a word that fits the category, type it, and submit it.","Step 4: Valid words will be accepted and added to your list as chips.","Step 5: Reach the target word count before the timer hits zero to win."],t.s)
B.aDO=s(["Think in sub-categories (e.g., for '''Animals''', think of pets, then farm animals, then zoo animals) to jog your memory.","Type quickly and don'''t worry about entering complex words; simple, common words score just the same.","If you get stuck, look around your immediate environment or think through the alphabet for inspiration."],t.s)
B.ahI=new A.a8("Category Fluency","WORD","Type as many words as possible that fit the given category before the time runs out.","Use the keyboard to type a word into the text field, then tap the send icon or press submit on the keyboard.",B.awS,B.aDO)
B.aLV=s(["Step 1: Look at the last word currently at the bottom of the chain.","Step 2: Identify the last two letters of that word, which are highlighted.","Step 3: Think of a new valid English word that begins with those exact two letters.","Step 4: Type the word into the input field and submit it to grow the chain.","Step 5: Keep the chain going as long as possible before the time expires."],t.s)
B.aQV=s(["Keep words relatively short to save typing time, as the score is based on the chain length, not word complexity.","Avoid using words that end in rare two-letter combinations (like '''ix''' or '''uz''') which will make your next turn very difficult.","If you are stuck, try adding common suffixes like '''er''', '''ed''', or '''ing''' to a base word if it helps set up an easier ending."],t.s)
B.ahG=new A.a8("Chain Reaction","WORD","Build the longest word chain possible by entering words that start with the last two letters of the previous word.","Use the keyboard to type a word into the text field, then tap the add icon or press submit on the keyboard.",B.aLV,B.aQV)
B.aA3=s(["Step 1: The game presents a '''heard''' voice word and a visual distractor word on the chalkboard.","Step 2: Ignore the visual word.","Step 3: Type the word you heard into the input field.","Step 4: Complete this for 5 rounds to finish the game."],t.s)
B.asT=s(["Focus entirely on the audio cue rather than the chalkboard.","Read the '''YOU HEAR''' text carefully if audio is off.","Type accurately to avoid losing points from incorrect submissions."],t.s)
B.aiG=new A.a8("Chalk and Talk","ATTENTION","Listen to the spoken word and type it correctly, ignoring the visually distracting word written on the chalkboard.","Tap the text field to open the keyboard and type the heard word. Tap '''Submit''' to confirm.",B.aA3,B.asT)
B.aRA=s(["Step 1: The screen flashes between two nearly identical images.","Step 2: Carefully scan the images to spot what appears or disappears.","Step 3: Tap the changed region.","Step 4: Find the changes across multiple rounds to win."],t.s)
B.aM3=s(["Keep your eyes focused on one section of the image at a time.","Look for objects that suddenly appear or disappear.","Do not tap randomly, as incorrect taps may penalize you."],t.s)
B.ahC=new A.a8("Change Blindness","ATTENTION","Identify the single difference between two alternating images before the time runs out.","Tap the area on the image where you spot the change.",B.aRA,B.aM3)
B.aNg=s(["Step 1: A grid of numbers is briefly displayed on the screen.","Step 2: Memorize their locations.","Step 3: Tap the '''1''' to begin; the other numbers will hide.","Step 4: Tap the remaining blank squares in sequential order."],t.s)
B.aPF=s(["Group numbers into patterns or shapes in your mind.","Focus intensely during the brief memorization phase.","Take your time when recalling, as a single mistake ends the round."],t.s)
B.aha=new A.a8("Chimp Test","MEMORY","Memorize the positions of numbers and tap them in sequential order after they are hidden.","Tap the hidden squares in the correct numerical order.",B.aNg,B.aPF)
B.aOl=s(["Step 1: Wait for a shape or directional cue to appear on screen.","Step 2: Instantly identify which side or button it corresponds to.","Step 3: Tap the correct button.","Step 4: Repeat for several trials to get an average reaction time."],t.s)
B.aV1=s(["Keep your fingers hovering over the buttons.","Focus on the center of the screen so you can see the stimulus immediately.","Prioritize accuracy, as incorrect taps hurt your score more than being slightly slow."],t.s)
B.akW=new A.a8("Choice Reaction Time","SPEED","React as quickly as possible to a visual stimulus by selecting the correct corresponding option.","Tap the correct button (e.g., left or right) that matches the stimulus shown.",B.aOl,B.aV1)
B.aBX=s(["Step 1: Locate your starting point and the end goal.","Step 2: Swipe up, down, left, or right to move.","Step 3: Find the open path without hitting dead ends.","Step 4: Reach the goal to complete the maze."],t.s)
B.aSC=s(["Trace the path backwards from the goal with your eyes before moving.","Look ahead at intersections to avoid long dead ends.","Move efficiently to complete the maze in fewer moves or less time."],t.s)
B.ak4=new A.a8("Classic Maze","LOGIC","Navigate from the starting position to the goal through a complex maze.","Swipe in the direction you want to move the character, or use directional buttons.",B.aBX,B.aSC)
B.atz=s(["Step 1: A list of word pairs is presented.","Step 2: Determine which pairs share both root and meaning.","Step 3: Select the true cognates.","Step 4: Avoid false friends (words that look similar but mean different things)."],t.s)
B.atJ=s(["Look for common prefixes or suffixes.","Watch out for known '''false friends''' between the languages.","Sound out the words in your head to find phonetic similarities."],t.s)
B.ahd=new A.a8("Cognate Catch","WORD","Identify words that are cognates (share a similar origin and meaning) across different languages.","Tap the word pairs that are true cognates.",B.atz,B.atJ)
B.aVT=s(["Step 1: You are given a starting integer.","Step 2: If it's even, divide it by 2.","Step 3: If it's odd, multiply by 3 and add 1.","Step 4: Continue until the number becomes 1."],t.s)
B.avz=s(["Remember the rules: Even -> half, Odd -> 3n+1.","Calculate carefully to avoid unnecessary steps.","Look for powers of 2, as they lead straight down to 1."],t.s)
B.akF=new A.a8("Collatz","MATH","Apply the Collatz conjecture rules to reach the number 1 from a given starting number.","Tap the corresponding math operation button (e.g., '''n/2''' or '''3n+1''').",B.aVT,B.avz)
B.atG=s(["Step 1: Start from the top-left corner tile.","Step 2: Choose a color that matches adjacent tiles to absorb them.","Step 3: Continue changing colors to expand your area.","Step 4: Fill the entire board with one color before running out of moves."],t.s)
B.aC6=s(["Always pick the color that absorbs the maximum number of new tiles.","Look ahead to see which color will open up large sections.","Work towards the edges of the board."],t.s)
B.ajq=new A.a8("Color Flood","LOGIC","Flood the entire grid with a single color within the allowed number of moves.","Tap the color buttons at the bottom to change the color of your growing cluster.",B.atG,B.aC6)
B.aWw=s(["Step 1: A word describing a color appears on screen.","Step 2: Look at the actual color of the text.","Step 3: Decide if the word text matches the color.","Step 4: Answer quickly and accurately across multiple trials."],t.s)
B.aHI=s(["Focus primarily on the visual color first, then read the word.","Try to disconnect your reading brain from your visual processing.","Don'''t rush too fast, as errors cost points."],t.s)
B.akn=new A.a8("Color Match","ATTENTION","Determine if the meaning of the word matches the ink color it is written in.","Tap '''Yes''' if it matches, or '''No''' if it doesn'''t.",B.aWw,B.aHI)
B.aWT=s(["Step 1: Observe the required color sequence shown at the top.","Step 2: Move from the start tile to the next adjacent tile in the sequence.","Step 3: Continue looping through the sequence as you move.","Step 4: Reach the exit without breaking the pattern."],t.s)
B.aSu=s(["Always double-check what the next required color is.","Plan your path a few steps ahead to avoid dead ends.","If you get stuck, retrace your steps carefully."],t.s)
B.aiK=new A.a8("Color Maze Nav","LOGIC","Navigate the maze by following a specific sequence of colored tiles.","Swipe to move your character to an adjacent valid tile.",B.aWT,B.aSu)
B.atj=s(["Step 1: Two words are displayed on the screen.","Step 2: Identify the ink color of the top word.","Step 3: Identify the text meaning of the bottom word.","Step 4: Tap Match if they are the same, otherwise tap Mismatch."],t.s)
B.aVC=s(["Mentally separate the two tasks: color for top, reading for bottom.","Ignore the text of the top word completely.","Ignore the ink color of the bottom word completely."],t.s)
B.ain=new A.a8("Color Word Match Up","ATTENTION","Match the ink color of the top word with the meaning of the bottom word.","Tap '''Match''' or '''Mismatch''' based on the conditions.",B.atj,B.aVC)
B.aGa=s(["Step 1: A set of fractions is displayed.","Step 2: Identify the denominators of all fractions.","Step 3: Calculate the lowest common multiple of these numbers.","Step 4: Enter your answer to complete the round."],t.s)
B.aS7=s(["Check if the largest denominator is already a multiple of the others.","Use prime factorization for larger numbers.","Practice your multiplication tables to speed up calculation."],t.s)
B.akx=new A.a8("Common Denominator","MATH","Find the lowest common denominator (LCD) for a given set of fractions.","Type or select the correct number and submit.",B.aGa,B.aS7)
B.aCO=s(["Step 1: Look at the compass arrows on your current tile.","Step 2: Move to an adjacent tile that aligns with one of those arrows.","Step 3: Repeat to find a path to the goal.","Step 4: Reach the goal tile to win."],t.s)
B.aO8=s(["Work backwards from the goal to see which tiles point to it.","Avoid tiles with arrows that point to dead ends or boundaries.","Look for loops and avoid getting trapped."],t.s)
B.agG=new A.a8("Compass Maze","LOGIC","Navigate a grid where you can only move in the directions indicated by the current tile's compass.","Tap an adjacent tile in a valid direction to move.",B.aCO,B.aO8)
B.aBV=s(["Step 1: Analyze the unfolded 2D shape (net).","Step 2: Mentally fold the faces together along the edges.","Step 3: Compare your mental model to the multiple-choice 3D shapes.","Step 4: Select the matching shape."],t.s)
B.aNR=s(["Focus on a single distinctive face and track its adjacent sides.","Use process of elimination for shapes that are clearly impossible.","Pay attention to the orientation of patterns on the faces."],t.s)
B.akI=new A.a8("Complex Folding Nets","SPATIAL","Determine which 3D shape can be formed by folding the provided 2D net.","Tap the correct 3D shape option.",B.aBV,B.aNR)
B.aSc=s(["Step 1: Look at the provided word fragments.","Step 2: Identify pairs that combine to make a real compound word.","Step 3: Select the first half, then the second half.","Step 4: Clear all words from the board."],t.s)
B.aTc=s(["Start with the most obvious pairs first.","If a word doesn't fit, think about alternative meanings.","Read the remaining words aloud to see if they sound right together."],t.s)
B.akR=new A.a8("Compound Connect","WORD","Connect two words to form a valid compound word.","Tap a word from the first list, then tap a word from the second list.",B.aSc,B.aTc)
B.aQT=s(["Step 1: The game tells you what to find (e.g., '''Red Square''').","Step 2: Scan the grid of distractors (e.g., red circles, blue squares).","Step 3: Locate the exact item that matches both features.","Step 4: Tap it quickly to earn points."],t.s)
B.atd=s(["Scan systematically (left to right, top to bottom).","Focus on finding one feature first, then filter by the second.","Don'''t get distracted by items that share only one feature."],t.s)
B.agO=new A.a8("Conjunction Search","ATTENTION","Find the specific target item that combines two distinct features among distractors.","Tap the correct target item on the screen.",B.aQT,B.atd)
B.avq=s(["Step 1: A word is displayed with its vowels missing.","Step 2: Use the remaining consonants as clues.","Step 3: Fill in the correct vowels to reconstruct the word.","Step 4: Submit your answer."],t.s)
B.aFb=s(["Look for common prefixes and suffixes.","Try inserting common vowels like E or A first.","Think about word patterns and syllable structures."],t.s)
B.ajZ=new A.a8("Consonant Reconstruct","WORD","Guess the hidden word using only its provided consonants.","Type the complete word into the input field.",B.avq,B.aFb)
B.at6=s(["Step 1: Read the sentence with the blank space.","Step 2: Analyze the context and tone of the sentence.","Step 3: Review the options.","Step 4: Tap the word that best completes the thought."],t.s)
B.aM0=s(["Look for signal words (like '''however''' or '''because''').","Eliminate options that are grammatically incorrect.","Read the completed sentence to see if it makes logical sense."],t.s)
B.akb=new A.a8("Context Clues","WORD","Determine the meaning of a missing word based on the surrounding sentence context.","Select the best word from the multiple-choice options.",B.at6,B.aM0)
B.aDU=s(["Step 1: Images will appear on screen one by one.","Step 2: For each image, decide if it's a new item or a repeat.","Step 3: Tap the corresponding New or Old button.","Step 4: Keep track as the sequence gets longer."],t.s)
B.axZ=s(["Focus on unique details of each image to remember it better.","Trust your gut reaction; overthinking can lead to mistakes.","Stay highly focused, as a momentary lapse can ruin your streak."],t.s)
B.aiO=new A.a8("Continuous Recognition","MEMORY","Determine if the currently shown image has appeared before in the sequence.","Tap '''New''' if it's the first time seeing it, or '''Old''' if you've seen it before.",B.aDU,B.axZ)
B.aXV=s(["Step 1: Watch the blocks carefully as they light up one by one.","Step 2: Remember the pattern and order.","Step 3: Wait for the sequence to finish.","Step 4: Tap the blocks in the exact same order."],t.s)
B.aE_=s(["Trace the pattern with your eyes or finger in the air.","Chunk the sequence into smaller groups of 3 or 4 blocks.","Focus on the geometric shape the sequence forms."],t.s)
B.akD=new A.a8("Corsi Blocks","MEMORY","Memorize and reproduce a sequence of tapped blocks in the exact order.","Tap the blocks in the sequence they lit up.",B.aXV,B.aE_)
B.aC9=s(["Step 1: You are given a target number and a set of starting numbers.","Step 2: Select a number, then an operator, then another number.","Step 3: The result becomes a new available number.","Step 4: Continue combining until you reach the exact target."],t.s)
B.aDC=s(["Work backwards from the target number if possible.","Save small numbers for fine-tuning at the end.","Don'''t be afraid to clear and start over if you get stuck."],t.s)
B.ahR=new A.a8("Countdown Math","MATH","Use the provided numbers and basic arithmetic operators to reach a target number before time runs out.","Tap numbers and operators to build your equation.",B.aC9,B.aDC)
B.aLd=s(["Step 1: Analyze the colored regions on the grid.","Step 2: Place one crown in each region, row, and column.","Step 3: Ensure crowns do not touch even diagonally.","Step 4: Fill the necessary spots to solve the puzzle."],t.s)
B.auG=s(["Start with small regions where placement options are limited.","Use the X marker to cross out invalid cells.","Remember that corners diagonally adjacent to a crown are invalid."],t.s)
B.agT=new A.a8("Crown","LOGIC","Place crowns on the grid so that no two share the same row, column, or colored region, and they don't touch diagonally.","Tap empty cells to place or remove a crown. Long press to mark with an X.",B.aLd,B.auG)
B.aSd=s(["Step 1: Look at the letter-based equation (e.g., AB + A = BCC).","Step 2: Use logic to figure out value constraints (e.g., C must be 1).","Step 3: Assign numbers to letters.","Step 4: Complete the puzzle so the math adds up perfectly."],t.s)
B.aX2=s(["Look for carrying operations to find 1s or 0s.","Identify the most restricted letters first.","Use trial and error for the final few digits if needed."],t.s)
B.aky=new A.a8("Crypto Arithmetic","LOGIC","Deduce which digit corresponds to each letter to make the math equation true.","Tap a letter and use the number pad to assign it a digit.",B.aSd,B.aX2)
B.aRJ=s(["Step 1: Analyze the coded phrase and letter frequencies.","Step 2: Guess common letters like E, T, or A.","Step 3: Fill in short words like '''THE''' or '''AND'''.","Step 4: Reveal the entire hidden message."],t.s)
B.aQf=s(["Look for single-letter words which are usually '''A''' or '''I'''.","Find common two-letter words (OF, TO, IN, IS).","Check apostrophes for common endings like '''S''', '''T''', or '''LL'''."],t.s)
B.ahE=new A.a8("Cryptogram","WORD","Decode the encrypted message by substituting letters.","Tap a coded letter and assign it a real letter from the keyboard.",B.aRJ,B.aQf)
B.aF0=s(["Step 1: Observe the colors on the unfolded 2D cross-shaped net.","Step 2: Visualize how the net folds into a 3D cube.","Step 3: Examine the three 3D cube options provided.","Step 4: Select the cube that represents a valid rotation of the folded net and submit your choice."],t.s)
B.aDS=s(["Look for opposite faces on the net (they will have one square between them) - they can never touch on the folded cube.","Track the relative orientation of three adjacent faces.","Eliminate options that show impossible color combinations."],t.s)
B.aip=new A.a8("Cube Net Fold","SPATIAL","Identify which 3D cube configuration matches the unfolded 2D net shown.","Tap on the correct 3D cube option (A, B, or C) at the bottom of the screen, then tap SUBMIT CHOICE.",B.aF0,B.aDS)
B.ay3=s(["Step 1: Scan the 4x4 grid of letters ('d' and 'p').","Step 2: Identify the letter 'd's that have exactly two dashes (either 2 above, 2 below, or 1 above and 1 below).","Step 3: Tap all matching 'd's to highlight them.","Step 4: Ignore all 'p's and 'd's with 1, 3, or 4 dashes.","Step 5: Tap SUBMIT BOARD to check your answers and advance."],t.s)
B.aT_=s(["Scan row by row or column by column systematically to avoid missing targets.","Quickly skip over any 'p' letters without counting their dashes.","Count the total dashes on 'd's carefully; do not be distracted by the position of the dashes."],t.s)
B.all=new A.a8("D2 Attention","ATTENTION","Find and select all instances of the letter 'd' that have exactly two dashes.","Tap the tiles to select or deselect them, then tap SUBMIT BOARD when you have found all targets.",B.ay3,B.aT_)
B.atS=s(["Step 1: Read the target word shown in the large colored box.","Step 2: Read through the four definition options provided below.","Step 3: Select the definition that correctly matches the word.","Step 4: If correct, you will advance; if incorrect, the game ends."],t.s)
B.aMB=s(["Use root words and prefixes to deduce the meaning of unfamiliar words.","Eliminate obviously incorrect definitions first to narrow down your choices.","Pay attention to the part of speech (noun, verb, adjective) to match the definition style."],t.s)
B.agm=new A.a8("Definition Dash","WORD","Match the displayed vocabulary word with its correct definition.","Tap on the definition button that corresponds to the meaning of the given word.",B.atS,B.aMB)
B.aHO=s(["Step 1: A sample image or pattern will be shown briefly on the screen.","Step 2: The screen will go blank or show a distraction for a delay period.","Step 3: Several options will appear.","Step 4: Tap the option that perfectly matches the original sample."],t.s)
B.aXQ=s(["Focus on specific unique features or colors in the sample rather than the whole image.","Mentally repeat the visual features during the delay period.","Do not let the blank screen break your concentration."],t.s)
B.aja=new A.a8("Delayed Match Sample","MEMORY","Remember a target pattern or image, wait through a delay, and then identify it among distractors.","Observe the sample, wait for the delay to end, and tap the matching option.",B.aHO,B.aXQ)
B.auK=s(["Step 1: Watch the sequence of digits shown one by one.","Step 2: Wait for the sequence to complete.","Step 3: Use the keypad to input the digits in exactly the reverse order.","Step 4: Submit your answer to see if you are correct and proceed to longer sequences."],t.s)
B.aUm=s(["Group the digits into pairs or triplets as they appear to aid memory.","Mentally rehearse the sequence backwards as it is being shown.","Focus intensely on the last digit shown, as it will be your first input."],t.s)
B.ahx=new A.a8("Reverse Digit Span","MEMORY","Remember a sequence of digits and enter them in reverse order.","Watch the digits appear, then use the on-screen keypad to enter them backwards.",B.auK,B.aUm)
B.aVM=s(["Step 1: Examine the incorrect equation presented.","Step 2: Calculate the current results of the left and right sides.","Step 3: Identify which two digits, when swapped, will balance the equation.","Step 4: Tap the first digit, then tap the second digit to execute the swap."],t.s)
B.aSv=s(["Look for the difference between the two sides to estimate what needs to change.","Focus on digits that have the largest impact (e.g., tens place vs ones place).","Check the operations; swapping numbers in a multiplication part changes the value drastically."],t.s)
B.alg=new A.a8("Digit Swap Equation","MATH","Fix an incorrect mathematical equation by swapping two digits.","Tap two digits to swap their positions and make the equation true.",B.aVM,B.aSv)
B.aXo=s(["Step 1: Observe the sequence of arrows (Up, Down, Left, Right) shown on screen.","Step 2: Wait for the sequence to finish displaying.","Step 3: Tap the directional buttons to input the exact sequence from memory.","Step 4: Complete the sequence correctly to advance to longer rounds."],t.s)
B.aFx=s(["Assign words (e.g., North, South, East, West) to the arrows if verbal memory is easier.","Visualize the sequence as a path moving through space.","Chunk the arrows into groups of 3 or 4."],t.s)
B.aiU=new A.a8("Directions Recall","MEMORY","Memorize a sequence of directional arrows and reproduce the sequence.","Watch the arrows appear, then tap the corresponding directional buttons in the correct order.",B.aXo,B.aFx)
B.aFD=s(["Step 1: Note the target symbol shown at the start of the round.","Step 2: Scan the dense grid of symbols.","Step 3: Tap every instance of the target symbol.","Step 4: Avoid tapping the distractors, then submit your answer."],t.s)
B.aQR=s(["Look for the defining feature that differentiates the target from the distractors.","Scan the grid methodically, row by row.","Take your time; accuracy is more important than speed to avoid penalties."],t.s)
B.air=new A.a8("Distractor Matrix","ATTENTION","Locate specific target shapes/symbols hidden among visually similar distractors.","Tap all the target symbols in the matrix.",B.aFD,B.aQR)
B.ato=s(["Step 1: Understand the requirements of Task A (e.g., sorting shapes).","Step 2: Understand the requirements of Task B (e.g., dodging obstacles).","Step 3: Monitor both sides of the screen continuously.","Step 4: React to stimuli on both sides to keep the game going."],t.s)
B.aM8=s(["Do not fixate on one side of the screen; keep your eyes moving back and forth.","Prioritize the task that has an immediate impending failure condition.","Rely on peripheral vision to detect movement or changes."],t.s)
B.ai5=new A.a8("Divided Attention","ATTENTION","Perform two different tasks simultaneously without letting either fail.","Use left-side controls for one task and right-side controls for the other.",B.ato,B.aM8)
B.aPV=s(["Step 1: Note the target divisor shown at the top of the screen.","Step 2: Watch numbers appear on the board.","Step 3: Quickly perform mental division.","Step 4: Tap only the numbers that divide evenly by the target."],t.s)
B.aUn=s(["Memorize divisibility rules (e.g., ends in 0/5 for 5, sum of digits for 3 and 9).","Ignore obvious wrong answers (e.g., odd numbers for an even divisor).","Focus on accuracy first, speed will follow."],t.s)
B.agI=new A.a8("Divisibility Dash","MATH","Identify numbers that are divisible by a given target number within a time limit.","Tap the falling or appearing numbers that are cleanly divisible by the target.",B.aPV,B.aUn)
B.aQ_=s(["Step 1: Look at the sample object presented on screen.","Step 2: Wait for the screen to clear during the delay period.","Step 3: Multiple objects will appear. Only ONE is the novel object.","Step 4: Tap the novel object that differs in both icon and color from the sample."],t.s)
B.aS1=s(["Firmly lock both the icon and color of the sample object in your mind.","The correct card is the one that is completely different (different icon AND different color).","Cards that share the same icon or same color as the sample are decoys.","Difficulty increases with correct streaks: more decoys appear as you succeed."],t.s)
B.al5=new A.a8("Delayed Non-Match to Sample","MEMORY","Choose the novel object that was NOT shown in the previous sample. Score 12 or more to win.","Observe the sample, wait, and then tap the new/different object.",B.aQ_,B.aS1)
B.aIK=s(["Step 1: Look at the grid of numbers.","Step 2: Identify pairs of adjacent numbers that make up valid domino tiles.","Step 3: Tap and drag to group two numbers together.","Step 4: Cover the entire grid exactly once with no overlapping dominoes."],t.s)
B.aLD=s(["Look for pairs that can only be formed in one specific location.","Work from the edges and corners inward.","Keep track of which dominoes (e.g., 2-3, 4-4) you have already placed."],t.s)
B.agt=new A.a8("Dominosa","LOGIC","Reconstruct a set of dominoes by pairing adjacent numbers on a grid.","Tap and drag between adjacent numbers to form a domino.",B.aIK,B.aLD)
B.aLX=s(["Step 1: Note the current N level (e.g., N=2 means comparing to 2 steps ago).","Step 2: A sequence of squares will appear in different grid positions while letters are spoken.","Step 3: If the square is in the same position as N steps ago, tap Position Match.","Step 4: If the letter heard is the same as N steps ago, tap Audio Match."],t.s)
B.aD9=s(["Do not try to remember the sequence as a whole; constantly update your memory buffer.","Say the letters out loud while visualizing the grid positions.","Practice single N-back tasks if dual tracking is too difficult."],t.s)
B.agV=new A.a8("Double N-Back","MEMORY","Simultaneously track auditory and visual stimuli, indicating when the current stimulus matches the one from 'N' steps back.","Tap the 'Position Match' or 'Audio Match' buttons when appropriate.",B.aLX,B.aD9)
B.aSV=s(["Step 1: On the left side, tap falling green apples to score points before they reach the bottom.","Step 2: Avoid tapping red apples, as they deduct points.","Step 3: On the right side, tap the blue bubble before it grows too large and bursts.","Step 4: Reach the target number of taps across both sides to complete the game."],t.s)
B.aXJ=s(["Keep your eyes moving between both sides to avoid missing targets.","Prioritize catching green apples quickly, as missing them also costs points.","Pop bubbles early before they get too close to bursting on their own."],t.s)
B.ahm=new A.a8("Double Trouble","FLEXIBILITY","Manage two simultaneous mini-games by tapping targets on both sides of the screen.","Tap the falling apples on the left and the growing bubbles on the right.",B.aSV,B.aXJ)
B.aBP=s(["Step 1: A sequence of image-word pairs will be presented.","Step 2: Focus on creating a mental link between the image and the word.","Step 3: During the test phase, an image or a word will be shown.","Step 4: Select the corresponding pair from the given options."],t.s)
B.aQM=s(["Create vivid, bizarre, or funny mental stories combining the word and the image.","Focus on specific features of the image and relate them to the syllables of the word.","Rehearse the associations as they appear."],t.s)
B.ah7=new A.a8("Dual Coding","MEMORY","Memorize pairs of distinct visual images and descriptive words.","Study the pairs, then select the correct matching word or image during the test phase.",B.aBP,B.aQM)
B.aN_=s(["Step 1: Identify your primary cursor and the mirrored cursor.","Step 2: Identify the two target zones.","Step 3: Drag the primary cursor. The mirrored cursor will move in the opposite direction.","Step 4: Navigate around obstacles to place both cursors in their target zones simultaneously."],t.s)
B.aUg=s(["Focus primarily on the cursor that is closest to obstacles or walls.","Move slowly; fast movements can cause the mirrored cursor to crash.","Use walls to 're-align' the cursors by deliberately bumping one into a wall while the other moves."],t.s)
B.ahb=new A.a8("Dual Mirror","SPATIAL","Control two objects moving in opposite directions to reach their respective targets.","Swipe or drag to move. One object follows your finger, the other moves inversely.",B.aN_,B.aUg)
B.aQi=s(["Step 1: Memorize the sequence or set of target items shown.","Step 2: Complete the active distractor task (e.g., solving simple math or tapping moving objects).","Step 3: Once the distractor task ends, recall and input the original target items.","Step 4: Submit your answers to proceed."],t.s)
B.aCt=s(["Solidify the memory targets quickly before the distractor task begins.","Mentally rehearse the target items in the background while performing the distractor task.","Do not get overly invested in the distractor task; allocate just enough attention to pass it."],t.s)
B.akU=new A.a8("Dual Task Memory","MEMORY","Memorize a set of items while simultaneously performing a secondary distracting task.","Study items, interact with the distractor task via tapping, then recall the initial items.",B.aQi,B.aCt)
B.avC=s(["Step 1: At the start, several items will briefly flash or highlight as your targets.","Step 2: All items will become identical and begin moving around the screen.","Step 3: Visually track the movement of your specific targets.","Step 4: When the movement stops, tap the items you tracked."],t.s)
B.aAH=s(["Try to view the targets as a single moving geometric shape (e.g., a triangle if there are 3 targets).","Do not look directly at one target; keep your eyes focused on the center of the group.","Avoid blinking while the items are in motion."],t.s)
B.aiz=new A.a8("Dynamic Salience","ATTENTION","Track specific targets as they move among visually similar distractors.","Watch the targets move, then tap them once they stop.",B.avC,B.aAH)
B.aJh=s(["Step 1: Read the list of available logical clues.","Step 2: Cross-reference attributes on the logic grid.","Step 3: Tap a cell to mark an intersection as true (which auto-crosses out the rest of the row/column).",u.cX],t.s)
B.at2=s(["Start with the most direct clues that explicitly link two items.","Use negative clues to eliminate possibilities immediately.","Look for chain reactions where placing one checkmark forces another."],t.s)
B.aiJ=new A.a8("Einstein's Riddle","LOGIC","Use a set of clues to deduce the attributes belonging to different subjects on a grid.","Tap grid cells to mark them as true (check) or false (cross) based on the clues.",B.aJh,B.at2)
B.atQ=s(["Step 1: Read the target vocabulary word.","Step 2: Review the multiple-choice language origin options.","Step 3: Tap the origin you believe the word derives from.","Step 4: Complete the round to see your score."],t.s)
B.av7=s(["Look for common prefixes and suffixes (e.g., 'anti-', 'ology' often point to Greek; 'tion', 'pre' to Latin).","Short, basic everyday words often come from Old English/Germanic roots.","Scientific or abstract concepts frequently have Latin or Greek origins."],t.s)
B.aiy=new A.a8("Etymology Origin","WORD","Determine the correct historical language origin (e.g., Latin, Greek, Old English) of the given word.","Tap the button corresponding to the correct language origin.",B.atQ,B.av7)
B.aSs=s(["Step 1: Examine the list of provided words.","Step 2: Identify the common root or prefix shared by most of the words.","Step 3: Find the word that looks similar but derives from a completely different root meaning.","Step 4: Tap the oddball word to submit your answer."],t.s)
B.aAN=s(["Focus on the meaning of the words, not just the spelling.","Watch out for words that have homophonic roots (sound the same but mean different things).","If unsure, look for the word that doesn't fit the overall semantic theme of the group."],t.s)
B.akH=new A.a8("Etymon Oddball","WORD","Identify the word in a list that does not share the same etymological root as the others.","Tap the word that is the odd one out.",B.aSs,B.aAN)
B.aW4=s(["Step 1: Study the list of events and their corresponding dates or timestamps.","Step 2: Once the study phase ends, the events will be shuffled and dates hidden.","Step 3: Drag the events up and down to arrange them from earliest to latest.","Step 4: Submit your timeline to check your accuracy."],t.s)
B.aJ_=s(["Create a mental story connecting the events in the order they occurred.","Focus on anchoring the first and last events securely in your memory.","Look for logical cause-and-effect relationships between the events."],t.s)
B.ajl=new A.a8("Event Timeline Memory","MEMORY","Memorize a sequence of historical or fictitious events and their dates, then place them in chronological order.","Drag and drop the event cards into the correct chronological sequence.",B.aW4,B.aJ_)
B.awC=s(["Step 1: A series of faces will be shown, each paired with a name.","Step 2: Memorize the association between the facial features and the name.","Step 3: During the test phase, a face will be presented without the name.","Step 4: Select or input the correct name associated with that face."],t.s)
B.aBm=s(["Find a distinctive feature on the face (e.g., prominent nose, unique hair) and link it to the name.","If the name is 'Smith', imagine a blacksmith hammer hitting their most prominent facial feature.","Mentally repeat the name while staring at the face."],t.s)
B.agD=new A.a8("Face Name Association","MEMORY","Memorize the names associated with different faces and recall them during the test phase.","Study the faces and names, then type or select the correct name when shown a face.",B.awC,B.aBm)
B.aPA=s(["Step 1: Faces will appear alongside specific traits or facts.","Step 2: Memorize which trait belongs to which person.","Step 3: In the test phase, a face will appear with multiple trait options.","Step 4: Tap the correct trait that was originally paired with the face."],t.s)
B.aTp=s(["Visualize the person actively engaging in their trait or occupation.","Create a quick, memorable story about why that person has that trait based on how they look.","Group faces by similar traits if possible to reduce memory load."],t.s)
B.aia=new A.a8("Face Trait Association","MEMORY","Memorize personal traits (e.g., occupation, hobby) associated with different faces.","Study the faces and traits, then select the correct trait when tested.",B.aPA,B.aTp)
B.aCl=s(["Step 1: Study the presented information containing multiple facts linked to a central subject.","Step 2: Try to build a comprehensive mental model of the information.","Step 3: After the study phase, read the questions testing your recall.","Step 4: Select the correct answers based on the facts you memorized."],t.s)
B.aUZ=s(["Organize the facts into categories (e.g., dates, locations, names) in your mind.","Try to identify the logical connections between different facts.","Don't just read passively; actively quiz yourself while studying."],t.s)
B.ahw=new A.a8("Fact Binder","MEMORY","Memorize interconnected sets of facts about various subjects and answer questions about them.","Read the fact sheets, then tap the correct answers to multiple-choice questions.",B.aCl,B.aUZ)
B.aw0=s(["Step 1: Look at the large target number displayed on the screen.","Step 2: Review the floating or grid-based number options.","Step 3: Tap all the numbers that are valid factors (divide evenly into the target).","Step 4: Avoid tapping numbers that are not factors to prevent losing points."],t.s)
B.axB=s(["Start with the easiest factors: 2 (if even), 3 (if sum of digits is divisible by 3), and 5.","Remember that factors often come in pairs (e.g., if 2 is a factor of 24, so is 12).","Work systematically from smallest to largest."],t.s)
B.ahS=new A.a8("Factor Finder","MATH","Identify all the prime factors or regular factors of a given target number.","Tap the correct number bubbles that are factors of the target.",B.aw0,B.axB)
B.aKd=s(["Step 1: A matrix filled with complex symbols (varying in shape, color, and pattern) is shown.","Step 2: Memorize the exact position and features of each symbol.","Step 3: The matrix will clear, leaving empty cells.","Step 4: Reconstruct the matrix by placing the correct symbols back into their original cells."],t.s)
B.azu=s(["Look for patterns in the grid (e.g., all red items in one row, all circles in one column).","Chunk the matrix into smaller sections (e.g., 2x2 blocks) rather than memorizing individual cells.","Prioritize remembering one feature first (like shape) and mentally layer the colors on top."],t.s)
B.agE=new A.a8("Feature Matrix Recall","MEMORY","Memorize a grid containing symbols with specific features (color, shape, pattern) and reconstruct it.","Study the grid, then reconstruct it by selecting the correct features for each empty cell.",B.aKd,B.azu)
B.aX_=s(["Step 1: Swipe the grid to move all tiles in the chosen direction.","Step 2: When two consecutive Fibonacci numbers (e.g., 2 and 3, or 5 and 8) collide, they merge into the next Fibonacci number (e.g., 5, 13).","Step 3: Note that 1s can merge with other 1s to make 2.","Step 4: Keep merging tiles to free up space and build larger numbers before the grid fills up."],t.s)
B.aFA=s(["Keep your highest value tile in one specific corner of the grid.","Only swipe in two or three directions (e.g., Down and Right) to maintain organization.","Plan your moves ahead to bring consecutive numbers adjacent to each other."],t.s)
B.al0=new A.a8("Fibonacci Merge","MATH","Slide tiles on a grid to merge consecutive Fibonacci numbers and reach the highest possible number.","Swipe up, down, left, or right to move all tiles in that direction.",B.aX_,B.aFA)
B.aTH=s(["Step 1: Examine the starting numbers on the grid.","Step 2: Each number represents the size of the block (polyomino) it belongs to.","Step 3: Tap adjacent cells to assign them the same number to group them.","Step 4: Ensure no two blocks of the same size share a horizontal or vertical edge.","Step 5: Fill all grid cells to solve the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aWm=s(["Start with small numbers like 1, which are immediately isolated blocks.","Look for paths that are forced to extend because they cannot merge with adjacent groups of the same size.","Keep track of block sizes by counting cells with the same number."],t.s)
B.ahL=new A.a8("Fillomino","LOGIC","Divide the grid into polyominoes of matching sizes. Two polyominoes of the same size cannot touch share an edge.","Tap cells to cycle through numbers from 1 to 9.",B.aTH,B.aWm)
B.azm=s(["Step 1: Look at the target word shown at the top.","Step 2: Scan the grid for the starting letter of the word.","Step 3: Drag your finger across adjacent letters to highlight the full word.","Step 4: Release your finger to submit the selection."],t.s)
B.aWI=s(["Look for double letters or unique consonants first (like Z, K, X).","Search the grid systematically starting from the top-left.","Verify the direction of the word (forward, backward, diagonal) before dragging."],t.s)
B.ajn=new A.a8("Find Word","WORD","Locate the target word in a grid of scrambled letters.","Drag across letters horizontally, vertically, or diagonally to spell the word.",B.azm,B.aWI)
B.aDl=s(["Step 1: A row of arrows appears on screen (e.g., <<><<).","Step 2: Focus only on the central arrow (the middle one).","Step 3: Ignore the surrounding arrows (congruent or incongruent).","Step 4: Tap the correct direction button as fast as possible."],t.s)
B.aNb=s(["Fixate your eyes on the center of the screen ahead of time.","Breathe and react to only the visual direction of the middle arrow.","Do not let incongruent flankers trick you into clicking the wrong side."],t.s)
B.aig=new A.a8("Flanker Test","ATTENTION","Quickly identify the direction of the central arrow while ignoring the flanking arrows.","Tap the left or right button depending on the center arrow's direction.",B.aDl,B.aNb)
B.aNJ=s(["Step 1: Watch the target object highlighted at the start.","Step 2: Follow the object as it moves deeper into the tunnel.","Step 3: Steer or look in the direction the object is traveling.","Step 4: Keep tracking accurately to maintain your focus streak."],t.s)
B.aXi=s(["Relax your eyes to take in the wider path ahead.","Anticipate turns in the tunnel based on the object's trajectory.","Ignore visual distractions inside the tunnel."],t.s)
B.akm=new A.a8("Focus Tunnel","ATTENTION","Track and follow a target object as it moves through a complex visual tunnel.","Use the joystick or swipe to steer and track the object.",B.aNJ,B.aXi)
B.aR2=s(["Step 1: Look at the fraction representation shown (visual pie or numerical).","Step 2: Find the matching card with the equivalent value (e.g., 2/4 matches 1/2).","Step 3: Tap or drag to connect them.","Step 4: Match all cards correctly to complete the level."],t.s)
B.aRP=s(["Simplify fractions to their lowest terms immediately.","For visual pies, count the total segments first (denominator) and then shaded parts (numerator).","Practice common fraction conversions (halves, quarters, thirds)."],t.s)
B.ahA=new A.a8("Fraction Match","MATH","Match equivalent fractions or match fraction values to their visual representation.","Tap the matching fraction cards or drop them into matching slots.",B.aR2,B.aRP)
B.at1=s(["Step 1: Examine the cards containing numbers, shapes, or representations.","Step 2: Calculate the fraction value of each.","Step 3: Select pairs that represent the exact same value.","Step 4: Clear all cards to win."],t.s)
B.aND=s(["Look for easy visual matches first.","Mentally reduce all numbers to their simplified fraction forms.","Use process of elimination for trickier numbers."],t.s)
B.ajT=new A.a8("Fraction Matcher","MATH","Find matching equivalent representations of fractions.","Tap equivalent fraction cards to pair them up.",B.at1,B.aND)
B.awd=s(["Step 1: Read the order (e.g., '1/2 of an 8-slice pizza' or '3/4 of a 12-slice pizza').","Step 2: Calculate the exact number of slices required.","Step 3: Select or serve that number of slices.","Step 4: Submit the order to satisfy the customer."],t.s)
B.aRp=s(["Multiply the fraction by the total number of slices.","Visualize half or quarter sections of the pizza to estimate quickly.","Check your math before serving to avoid losing points."],t.s)
B.ajc=new A.a8("Fractional Pizza","MATH","Serve the correct amount of pizza slices based on fractional orders.","Tap to cut or select the requested number of pizza slices.",B.awd,B.aRp)
B.aBQ=s(["Step 1: Read the target frequency at the top of the screen.","Step 2: Observe the pulsing speeds of the 'A' and 'B' panels.","Step 3: Tap the panel that pulses at the target frequency.","Step 4: Answer correctly to increase your score before time runs out."],t.s)
B.aLc=s(["Use the reference frequency as a baseline (e.g., 1.0Hz is one pulse per second).","Higher frequencies pulse faster; lower frequencies pulse slower.","Rely on the visual rhythm rather than counting exact milliseconds."],t.s)
B.ajb=new A.a8("Frequency Tap","Math & Logic","Compare the pulse rates of two light panels and identify which one matches the target frequency (e.g., 1.5Hz).","Tap the left or right panel that corresponds to the correct frequency.",B.aBQ,B.aLc)
B.aLv=s(["Step 1: Look for inequality signs between adjacent cells.","Step 2: Find rows or columns with missing numbers and use the signs to deduce the values.","Step 3: Tap an empty cell and select the correct number from the bottom row.","Step 4: Complete the grid without violating any inequality constraints or row/column uniqueness."],t.s)
B.av0=s(["Look for chains of inequalities (e.g., A < B < C) which severely restrict possible numbers.","Identify the highest and lowest possible numbers in the grid to fill edges of inequalities.","Use the process of elimination in rows and columns as you would in Sudoku."],t.s)
B.akk=new A.a8("Futoshiki","Math & Logic","Fill the grid with numbers such that each row and column contains unique numbers, while respecting the inequality signs (<, >) between cells.","Tap a cell to select it, then use the numpad at the bottom to enter a number. Use the erase button to clear a cell.",B.aLv,B.av0)
B.aVq=s(["Step 1: Swipe to move all tiles in a single direction.","Step 2: When two tiles with the same number touch, they merge into one tile with double the value.","Step 3: After every swipe, a new 2 or 4 tile appears on the board.","Step 4: Keep merging tiles to free up space and build towards 2048."],t.s)
B.aXs=s(["Keep your highest value tile in one of the corners.","Restrict your swipes to primarily three directions to maintain your corner strategy.","Try to keep your tiles organized in a descending chain to allow for cascading merges."],t.s)
B.ai1=new A.a8("2048","Math & Logic","Combine tiles with the same numbers to reach the 2048 tile.","Swipe up, down, left, or right anywhere on the screen to slide all tiles in that direction.",B.aVq,B.aXs)
B.aA_=s(["Step 1: Observe the chain of interconnected gears.","Step 2: Note the rotation direction of the first gear (indicated by an arrow).","Step 3: Trace the rotation through the chain, remembering that adjacent gears rotate in opposite directions.","Step 4: Select the correct rotation direction for the final gear."],t.s)
B.azW=s(["Adjacent gears always rotate in opposite directions.","If there is an odd number of gears in the chain, the first and last gears rotate in the same direction.","If there is an even number of gears, the first and last gears rotate in opposite directions."],t.s)
B.aio=new A.a8("Gear Rotation","Visual Spatial","Determine the rotation direction of the final gear in a sequence, given the starting gear's direction.","Tap the 'CLOCKWISE' or 'COUNTER-CLOCKWISE' button.",B.aA_,B.azW)
B.aBy=s(["Step 1: Watch the pulsing circle expand and contract.","Step 2: Internalize the rhythm of the pulse over the first few cycles.","Step 3: When the pulse becomes invisible ('Ghost Mode'), continue tracking the rhythm in your head.","Step 4: Tap the screen precisely when the invisible pulse would reach its peak."],t.s)
B.aLP=s(["Count along with the visual pulses to establish a steady internal metronome.","Don't rush your tap; trust the rhythm you established during the visible phase.","If you are slightly off, adjust your timing for the next round based on the feedback."],t.s)
B.aii=new A.a8("Ghost Tap","Focus & Attention","Tap the screen at the exact moment an invisible pulsing radar peaks.","Tap anywhere on the screen.",B.aBy,B.aLP)
B.aUE=s(["Step 1: Look at the numbered circles at the grid intersections.","Step 2: A number indicates exactly how many diagonal lines must connect to that circle.","Step 3: Tap cells to draw diagonals, ensuring they satisfy all numbered intersections.","Step 4: Check that your lines do not create any closed loops."],t.s)
B.aS4=s(["Start with corners and edges; a '0' or '4' in the middle, or '0' or '2' on an edge, forces specific diagonals.","If a '1' is in a corner, only one line can connect to it.","Remember that loops are forbidden; if placing a line would close a loop, you must use the opposite diagonal."],t.s)
B.ahQ=new A.a8("Gokigen Naname","Math & Logic","Draw a diagonal line in every cell so that the lines meeting at each intersection match the number clue, without forming any closed loops.","Tap a cell to toggle the direction of its diagonal line (forward slash or backslash).",B.aUE,B.aS4)
B.aS9=s(["Step 1: Wait for a symbol to appear on the screen.","Step 2: If the symbol is a 'Go' (green/play icon), tap the screen as fast as possible.","Step 3: If the symbol is a 'No Go' (red/cross icon), do nothing and wait for it to disappear.","Step 4: Build your score by correctly reacting to a series of symbols."],t.s)
B.aXU=s(["Keep your finger hovering near the screen but avoid resting it to prevent accidental taps.","Focus primarily on the color or shape to make split-second decisions.","Stay relaxed; over-anticipating can cause false starts on 'No Go' symbols."],t.s)
B.aiw=new A.a8("Go No Go","Focus & Attention","Quickly tap the screen when a 'Go' symbol appears, and do NOT tap when a 'No Go' symbol appears.","Tap anywhere on the screen for 'Go'. Refrain from tapping for 'No Go'.",B.aS9,B.aXU)
B.aLq=s(["Step 1: Read the sentence presented on the screen carefully.","Step 2: Look for errors in tense, subject-verb agreement, or spelling.","Step 3: Tap 'CORRECT' if the sentence has no errors.","Step 4: Tap 'INCORRECT' if you spot a grammatical mistake."],t.s)
B.aJR=s(["Read the sentence aloud in your head; awkward phrasing often indicates an error.","Pay special attention to homophones (e.g., their/there/they're) and apostrophes.","Don't rush; ensure you evaluate the entire sentence before deciding."],t.s)
B.akl=new A.a8("Grammar Police","Language","Determine whether a displayed sentence is grammatically correct or incorrect.","Tap the 'CORRECT' or 'INCORRECT' button.",B.aLq,B.aJR)
B.aUz=s(["Step 1: Look at the word displayed in the center of the screen.","Step 2: Determine if it represents a person/place/thing (Noun), an action (Verb), or a description (Adjective).","Step 3: Tap the corresponding bucket button at the bottom.","Step 4: Quickly sort as many words as possible to build your score."],t.s)
B.aDv=s(["Try placing the word in a simple sentence (e.g., 'The [word]' for nouns, 'I [word]' for verbs, 'The [word] car' for adjectives).","Keep your fingers near all three buttons to minimize physical travel time.","Focus on accuracy over speed; consecutive correct answers often yield higher scores."],t.s)
B.ajp=new A.a8("Grammar Sort","Language","Categorize words into their correct parts of speech (Noun, Verb, or Adjective) before time runs out.","Tap the 'NOUN', 'VERB', or 'ADJECTIVE' button that corresponds to the displayed word.",B.aUz,B.aDv)
B.aCu=s(["Step 1: Read the equation (e.g., y = 2x - 1) and the target x-value.","Step 2: Calculate the corresponding y-value.","Step 3: Find the (x, y) coordinates on the graph and tap to place your point.","Step 4: Verify your selection and tap 'SUBMIT POINT'."],t.s)
B.avQ=s(["Double-check your mental math before submitting, especially with negative numbers.","Remember that the x-axis is horizontal and the y-axis is vertical.","Use the grid lines and labels to ensure you haven't misaligned your tap by one unit."],t.s)
B.akJ=new A.a8("Coordinate Plot","Math & Logic","Solve a linear equation for a given x-value and plot the resulting (x, y) point on the coordinate graph.","Tap a location on the grid to place a point, then tap 'SUBMIT POINT'.",B.aCu,B.avQ)
B.aLN=s(["Step 1: Study the 3x3 grid of icons during the memorization phase.","Step 2: When the grid goes blank, keep the image of the grid in your mind.","Step 3: When the icons reappear, spot the two icons that are in new positions.","Step 4: Tap both swapped icons to complete the round."],t.s)
B.aMd=s(["Focus on memorizing the corners or a specific row/column to anchor your memory.","Try creating a quick story or pattern connecting the icons in your head.","Look for icons that feel 'out of place' in your mental map when they reappear."],t.s)
B.aiM=new A.a8("Grid Displacement","Memory","Memorize the positions of icons in a 3x3 grid, and then identify which two icons swapped places after the grid was hidden.","Tap the two cells that contain the swapped icons.",B.aLN,B.aMd)
B.atb=s(["Step 1: Review the list of items and their categories during the memorization phase.","Step 2: Tap 'READY' when you have memorized the list.","Step 3: An item from the list will be displayed.","Step 4: Tap the category button that the item belongs to."],t.s)
B.aEs=s(["Group items by category in your mind (e.g., remember all the 'Produce' items together).","Visualize the items physically located in different aisles of a grocery store.","Use mnemonic devices or associations for items that are harder to categorize."],t.s)
B.al4=new A.a8("Grocery List","Memory","Memorize a list of grocery items and their categories, then correctly identify the category for a specific item during the testing phase.","Tap the correct category button from the options provided.",B.atb,B.aEs)
B.ax9=s(["Step 1: Read the sentence with the missing word.","Step 2: Review the multiple-choice options, which are homophones of each other.","Step 3: Determine which spelling fits the grammatical context and meaning of the sentence.","Step 4: Tap the correct option."],t.s)
B.aLa=s(["Use context clues; e.g., 'their' shows possession, 'there' indicates a place, 'they'''re' is 'they are'.","If unsure, mentally substitute each definition into the sentence to see which makes logical sense.","Take your time to double-check the spelling, as the words are visually similar."],t.s)
B.ai6=new A.a8("Homophone Hunt","Language","Select the correct homophone (words that sound the same but have different meanings/spellings) to complete the sentence.","Tap the button with the correctly spelled word.",B.ax9,B.aLa)
B.aKb=s(["Step 1: Identify the fixed tiles marked with a small dot; these cannot be moved.","Step 2: Look at the color difference between the fixed tiles to understand the direction of the gradient.","Step 3: Tap a movable tile, then tap another to swap them into the correct gradient order.","Step 4: Continue swapping until the colors transition smoothly across the entire grid."],t.s)
B.aKl=s(["Start by organizing the edges or corners connecting the fixed tiles.","Sort by one color dimension at a time (e.g., getting all the darkest tiles to one side).","If a tile looks slightly 'off', swap it with an immediate neighbor to see if the transition improves."],t.s)
B.aiu=new A.a8("Hue Sort","Visual Spatial","Rearrange the color tiles to form a perfect, seamless gradient, using the fixed tiles as anchors.","Tap one tile to select it, then tap another tile to swap their positions.",B.aKb,B.aKl)
B.aFp=s(["Step 1: Calculate the value of the mathematical expression on the left.","Step 2: Calculate the value of the expression on the right.","Step 3: Compare the two values.","Step 4: Tap '<' if left is less, '>' if left is greater, or '=' if they are equal."],t.s)
B.aHy=s(["Remember the order of operations (PEMDAS/BODMAS): multiply/divide before adding/subtracting.","Sometimes exact calculation isn't necessary; estimating can quickly reveal if one side is vastly larger.","Look for common terms on both sides that can be mentally canceled out to simplify the math."],t.s)
B.ajU=new A.a8("Inequality Balance Ops","Math & Logic","Evaluate two mathematical expressions and determine the correct inequality or equality relationship between them.","Tap the '<', '=', or '>' button.",B.aFp,B.aHy)
B.awo=s(["Step 1: Look at the 'LEFT' and 'RIGHT' formulas.","Step 2: Quickly solve both formulas in your head.","Step 3: Tap the appropriate inequality sign to compare them.","Step 4: Answer as many as you can before the timer runs out."],t.s)
B.axe=s(["Prioritize speed; use estimation techniques if the numbers are far apart.","Familiarize yourself with common addition and multiplication facts to reduce calculation time.","Keep a steady rhythm and try not to panic if the timer gets low."],t.s)
B.ajS=new A.a8("Inequality Dash","Math & Logic","Quickly determine the relationship (<, =, >) between two simple mathematical expressions before time runs out.","Tap the '<', '=', or '>' button.",B.awo,B.axe)
B.aww=s(["Step 1: Examine 'Shape A' and 'Shape B'.","Step 2: Drag your finger across the screen to rotate both shapes and view them from all angles.","Step 3: Mentally rotate one shape and try to slide it into the empty spaces of the other.","Step 4: Tap 'YES' if they interlock perfectly, or 'NO' if they do not."],t.s)
B.aHL=s(["Count the number of blocks in both shapes; their sum must equal the total volume of the target solid.","Look for prominent protrusions on one shape and find the corresponding indentations on the other.","Rotate the shapes to align their axes mentally, making it easier to visualize the fit."],t.s)
B.aj4=new A.a8("Interlock Puzzle","Visual Spatial","Determine if two 3D block shapes will fit together perfectly to form a solid cube/prism.","Drag on the screen to rotate the 3D shapes. Tap 'YES' or 'NO' to submit your answer.",B.aww,B.aHL)
B.aAk=s(["Step 1: Note the weights (1, 2, 3, 4...) located on the top and left edges of the grid.","Step 2: Check the target sums located on the right and bottom edges.","Step 3: Tap cells to shade them. A shaded cell in column 3 adds 3 to its row's sum.","Step 4: Continue shading until all row and column targets turn green."],t.s)
B.aRO=s(["Look for high target numbers that require almost all cells in a row/column to be shaded.","Look for low targets (like 1 or 2) where only one specific cell can be shaded.","Use cross-referencing: shading a cell affects both its row and column sum simultaneously."],t.s)
B.ajC=new A.a8("Kakurasu Sums","Math & Logic","Shade cells in a grid so that the sum of the weights of the shaded cells matches the target sums for each row and column.","Tap a cell to toggle its shaded state.",B.aAk,B.aRO)
B.aPM=s(["Step 1: Find a clue block (number with a diagonal line).","Step 2: The top-right number is the target sum for the horizontal block to its right. The bottom-left is for the vertical block below it.","Step 3: Tap a white cell and use the keypad to enter a digit from 1 to 9.","Step 4: Ensure no digits repeat within a single sum block."],t.s)
B.aXC=s(["Learn common Kakuro combinations (e.g., a 2-cell sum of 3 must be 1+2; a 2-cell sum of 4 must be 1+3).","Look for intersections of restrictive sums (e.g., a low horizontal sum crossing a low vertical sum).","Use pencil marks or mental notes to track possible candidates for each cell."],t.s)
B.aiL=new A.a8("Kakuro","Math & Logic","Fill the white cells with digits 1-9 so that the sum of each contiguous horizontal/vertical block matches its clue, without repeating any digit within a block.","Tap a white cell to select it, then tap a number on the keypad to enter it. Use the backspace button to clear a cell.",B.aPM,B.aXC)
B.aF_=s(["Step 1: Look at the cages (heavily outlined areas) and their target clues (e.g., '3+', '12x').","Step 2: Find single-cell cages, which require no math and give you free numbers.","Step 3: Tap empty cells and input numbers that satisfy the cage's math operation.","Step 4: Ensure no number repeats in any row or column."],t.s)
B.aDb=s(["Start with single-cell cages and cages with only one possible number combination (e.g., '3+' in a 2-cell cage must be 1 and 2).","Remember that subtraction and division cages can have numbers in any order (e.g., a '2\xf7' cage could be 4 and 2, or 2 and 4).","Use Sudoku-style row/column elimination to determine the exact placement of numbers within a cage."],t.s)
B.ajr=new A.a8("KenKen","Math & Logic","Fill the grid with numbers 1 to N (grid size) without repeating in any row or column, such that the numbers in each outlined 'cage' achieve the target value using the specified math operation.","Tap a cell to select it, then tap a number on the numpad. Use the backspace icon to clear.",B.aF_,B.aDb)
B.aOs=s(["Step 1: Identify the 2x2 HERO block.","Step 2: Move the smaller blocks around to clear a path downward.","Step 3: Continue sliding blocks into empty spaces without overlapping.","Step 4: Reach the green escape zone at the bottom middle with the HERO block to win."],t.s)
B.awD=s(["Focus on moving the smaller 1x1 blocks into empty spaces to free up larger ones.","Try to keep the empty spaces together to allow the large 2x2 block to move."],t.s)
B.akv=new A.a8("Klotski","SPATIAL","Move the 2x2 HERO block to the escape zone at the bottom middle of the board by sliding blocks out of the way.","Tap a block to select it, then tap the directional arrows that appear on it, or swipe the block to move it into an empty space.",B.aOs,B.awD)
B.aQr=s(["Step 1: Observe the laser source position and its initial direction.","Step 2: Note the target positions the laser must reach.","Step 3: Tap grid cells to place mirrors and reflect the laser path.","Step 4: Ensure the laser hits all targets to complete the level."],t.s)
B.aSA=s(["Trace the laser path backward from the targets to figure out where mirrors are needed.","Experiment with both mirror types to find the correct reflection angles."],t.s)
B.ah_=new A.a8("Laser Link","LOGIC","Place mirrors to reflect the laser from the source so that it hits all the target positions.","Tap on empty cells in the grid to cycle through mirror types (forward slash '/' or backslash '\\').",B.aQr,B.aSA)
B.aLL=s(["Step 1: Read the first word and the second word presented on screen.","Step 2: Think of a letter that can end the first word and start the second word.","Step 3: Input the letter to bridge the two words.","Step 4: If correct, both new words will be validated and you win."],t.s)
B.auP=s(["Test common vowels and consonants that frequently start or end words.","Focus on the shorter or more restrictive word first to narrow down options."],t.s)
B.aiq=new A.a8("Letter Bridge","WORD","Find the single letter that forms a valid word when added to the end of the first word, and also forms a valid word when added to the beginning of the second word.","Type or select the correct bridge letter to fill in the blank.",B.aLL,B.auP)
B.aLU=s(["Step 1: Identify the target letter you need to find at the start.","Step 2: Scan the grid carefully for the target letter.","Step 3: Tap each correct letter.","Step 4: Find all instances to complete the grid."],t.s)
B.aME=s(["Scan row by row or column by column systematically to ensure you don'''t miss any.","Ignore similar-looking letters that are placed as distractors."],t.s)
B.ajX=new A.a8("Letter Cancellation","ATTENTION","Find and select all instances of the target letter from the grid while ignoring distractions.","Tap on the tiles containing the target letter to select them.",B.aLU,B.aME)
B.aDw=s(["Step 1: Read the target letter you need to count.","Step 2: Scan through the paragraph and count every instance of the letter.","Step 3: Input your final count.","Step 4: Match the exact count to win."],t.s)
B.aKB=s(["Count word by word rather than skimming quickly.","Read the text aloud or trace with your finger to keep track."],t.s)
B.ajx=new A.a8("Letter Frequency Scan","ATTENTION","Count exactly how many times a specific target letter appears in the given paragraph of text.","Enter the correct count of the target letter using the number pad.",B.aDw,B.aKB)
B.aul=s(["Step 1: Look at the three TARGET WORDS displayed at the top.","Step 2: Find the letters for the first word and move them to the top row.","Step 3: Tap a tile, then tap an adjacent tile to swap them.","Step 4: Complete all three words horizontally to score a point and generate a new puzzle."],t.s)
B.aXN=s(["Focus on forming one word at a time, starting from the top row.","Be careful not to mix up the letters of already completed words."],t.s)
B.aiS=new A.a8("Letter Grid Swapper","WORD","Rearrange the letters in the 3x3 grid by swapping adjacent tiles to form the three target words horizontally.","Tap a tile to select it, then tap an adjacent tile to swap their positions.",B.aul,B.aXN)
B.aFr=s(["Step 1: Look at the numbers on each lighthouse.","Step 2: Place ships in the same row or column as the lighthouse to match its number.","Step 3: Ensure ships do not touch each other or the lighthouses, even diagonally.","Step 4: Satisfy all lighthouse conditions to win."],t.s)
B.aUT=s(["Start with lighthouses that have a count of 0 and mark their rows and columns as empty.","Look for overlapping paths between lighthouses with high numbers."],t.s)
B.akV=new A.a8("Lighthouses","LOGIC","Place ships in the grid so that each lighthouse points to the correct number of ships in its row and column.","Tap grid cells to place or remove ships.",B.aFr,B.aUT)
B.aTK=s(["Step 1: Observe the initial pattern of lit and unlit tiles.","Step 2: Tap a tile to turn it off, noting how it flips its neighbors.","Step 3: Work your way across the grid to systematically turn off lights.","Step 4: Achieve a completely dark board to win."],t.s)
B.aTo=s(["Try solving row by row, turning off all lights in the current row by clicking the row below it.","Use patterns to solve the final row if you get stuck."],t.s)
B.al_=new A.a8("Lights Out","LOGIC","Turn off all the lights on the grid. Tapping a light toggles its state and the state of adjacent lights.","Tap a tile to toggle it and its immediate neighbors (up, down, left, right).",B.aTK,B.aTo)
B.aTe=s(["Step 1: Watch the pattern being drawn on the grid.","Step 2: Memorize the exact sequence and direction.","Step 3: Swipe across the dots to recreate the sequence.","Step 4: Release your finger when the pattern is complete."],t.s)
B.aLr=s(["Break complex patterns down into simple geometric shapes.","Visualize a path or assign numbers to the dots to remember the order."],t.s)
B.ajw=new A.a8("Lock Pattern","MEMORY","Memorize and recreate the displayed lock pattern by connecting the dots in the correct order.","Drag your finger across the dots to draw the pattern.",B.aTe,B.aLr)
B.aL4=s(["Step 1: Read the provided statements carefully.","Step 2: Read the conclusion drawn from those statements.","Step 3: Decide if the conclusion is a guaranteed fact based ONLY on the statements.","Step 4: Tap the correct validity option."],t.s)
B.aW3=s(["Ignore real-world facts; base your answer only on the logic presented.","Draw Venn diagrams mentally to map out 'All', 'Some', or 'No' relationships."],t.s)
B.aiD=new A.a8("Logical Syllogisms","LOGIC","Determine if a conclusion logically follows from the given premises.","Tap 'Valid' or 'Invalid' based on your deduction.",B.aL4,B.aW3)
B.atR=s(["Step 1: Check the required target sum.","Step 2: Find a row, column, or diagonal with only one missing number.","Step 3: Calculate the missing value and place it.","Step 4: Repeat until the entire grid is filled correctly."],t.s)
B.aHX=s(["Always solve the lines with the most numbers filled in first.","The center cell is crucial; finding it early makes the rest easier."],t.s)
B.ala=new A.a8("Magic Squares","MATH","Fill the grid with numbers so that every row, column, and diagonal adds up to the same target sum.","Tap an empty cell and select a number to place it.",B.atR,B.aHX)
B.aRF=s(["Step 1: Check the numbers at the edges of the grid indicating how many + and - poles are in each row/column.","Step 2: Remember that + cannot touch + and - cannot touch - anywhere.","Step 3: Fill in the magnetic halves.","Step 4: Mark non-magnetic dominoes as blank to complete the grid."],t.s)
B.aG5=s(["Rows or columns with a count of 0 can immediately be filled with blanks.","If a domino must be magnetic, placing one pole forces the other."],t.s)
B.ai7=new A.a8("Magnets","LOGIC","Place domino-shaped magnets (with + and - poles) so they satisfy the row/column count constraints and identical poles do not touch.","Tap cells to toggle between +, -, and empty.",B.aRF,B.aG5)
B.aHA=s(["Step 1: Study the colored mandala carefully during the memorization phase.","Step 2: Once the colors disappear, select a color from the bottom palette.","Step 3: Tap the correct sections of the mandala to apply the color.","Step 4: Fill in all colored sections perfectly to win."],t.s)
B.aO6=s(["Focus on symmetry; if the left side is red, the right side might be too.","Memorize the colors layer by layer, starting from the center outward."],t.s)
B.aiN=new A.a8("Mandala Recall","MEMORY","Memorize the colors of the mandala pattern and recreate it from memory.","Tap a color from the palette, then tap the mandala sections to paint them.",B.aHA,B.aO6)
B.aQm=s(["Step 1: Enter a valid equation that equals the target number.","Step 2: Look at the color feedback (e.g., green for correct spot, yellow for wrong spot).","Step 3: Adjust your equation using the feedback.","Step 4: Find the exact hidden equation before you run out of tries."],t.s)
B.aKZ=s(["Start with an equation that uses diverse numbers and operations.","Remember order of operations (PEMDAS) applies to your guesses."],t.s)
B.ahD=new A.a8("Math Guess","MATH","Guess the hidden mathematical equation within the given number of tries, using color hints for correct numbers and operators.","Use the on-screen keyboard to type an equation and tap submit.",B.aQm,B.aKZ)
B.auY=s(["Step 1: Note the starting value and the mathematical rule for the maze.","Step 2: Calculate the results of moving to adjacent cells.","Step 3: Choose the path that keeps your value correct or matches the sequence.","Step 4: Reach the exit tile to complete the maze."],t.s)
B.aLJ=s(["Look a few steps ahead to avoid dead ends that break the math rule.","Work backwards from the exit if the forward path is confusing."],t.s)
B.akO=new A.a8("Math Maze","MATH","Navigate through the maze by moving to adjacent cells that satisfy the mathematical condition or target value.","Swipe or tap adjacent cells to move your character through the maze.",B.auY,B.aLJ)
B.aEN=s(["Step 1: Look at the target number you need to reach.",u.aq,"Step 3: Swipe through operators and numbers to build an equation.","Step 4: Release your finger when the equation equals the target."],t.s)
B.awJ=s(["If the target is large, look for multiplication tiles.","Keep track of the running total in your head as you map the path."],t.s)
B.akX=new A.a8("Math Path","MATH","Find a path of numbers and operators that evaluates to the target result.","Swipe across adjacent tiles to form a valid mathematical expression.",B.aEN,B.awJ)
B.aNf=s(["Step 1: Look at the two matrices to be multiplied.","Step 2: Multiply the rows of the first matrix by the columns of the second.","Step 3: Tap a cell in the result matrix.","Step 4: Enter the sum of the products to fill the matrix."],t.s)
B.aD5=s(["Write down intermediate steps mentally or use scratchpad if needed.","Double-check positive and negative signs carefully."],t.s)
B.aiI=new A.a8("Matrix Multiplier","MATH","Perform matrix multiplication to calculate the correct resulting matrix.","Tap the result cells and enter the calculated numbers.",B.aNf,B.aD5)
B.axV=s(["Step 1: View the list of matrix pairs and the list of results.","Step 2: Quickly estimate or calculate the multiplication of one pair.","Step 3: Tap the pair and tap the matching result.","Step 4: Clear all items from the screen to win."],t.s)
B.aMC=s(["Calculate just the top-left element of the result to quickly find matches.","Look for matrices with zeroes to speed up calculations."],t.s)
B.ajR=new A.a8("Matrix Multiplier Match","MATH","Match pairs of matrices with their correct multiplied result.","Tap a matrix expression and then tap its corresponding result to match them.",B.axV,B.aMC)
B.aNw=s(["Step 1: Observe the 3x3 grid of patterns with one missing piece.","Step 2: Find the logical rule governing the rows and columns (e.g., rotation, addition).","Step 3: Apply the rule to determine what the missing piece should look like.","Step 4: Tap the matching option to solve."],t.s)
B.aCw=s(["Test one feature at a time: first color, then shape, then rotation.","Verify your theory across both a row and a column to be sure."],t.s)
B.ale=new A.a8("Matrix Reasoning","LOGIC","Identify the missing pattern in the visual matrix from the given choices.","Tap the correct visual pattern from the options below the matrix.",B.aNw,B.aCw)
B.aJf=s(["Step 1: Look around to orient yourself in the 3D environment.","Step 2: Move forward through the corridors.","Step 3: Memorize intersections to avoid walking in circles.","Step 4: Find the exit door or portal to win."],t.s)
B.aPr=s(["Use the 'right-hand rule': always keep your right hand on the wall to eventually find the exit.","Look out for unique textures or landmarks to remember where you've been."],t.s)
B.ahr=new A.a8("3D Maze Navigation","SPATIAL","Navigate through a 3D maze to find the exit from a first-person perspective.","Use the on-screen directional buttons or swipe to move forward, backward, and turn.",B.aJf,B.aPr)
B.au3=s(["Step 1: Watch the grid as certain tiles light up.","Step 2: Memorize their exact positions.","Step 3: Wait for the tiles to flip back over.","Step 4: Tap all the previously lit tiles correctly."],t.s)
B.aCq=s(["Look for shapes or letters formed by the highlighted tiles.","Don't rush; tap systematically once you are sure of the pattern."],t.s)
B.aiA=new A.a8("Memory Matrix","MEMORY","Memorize the highlighted tiles and tap them after they are hidden.","Tap the tiles you remember were highlighted.",B.au3,B.aCq)
B.aO3=s(["Step 1: Observe the items placed at various locations in the room.","Step 2: Create a mental story linking the item to the location.","Step 3: Once the items are hidden, tap a location.","Step 4: Select the item that belongs there from the options."],t.s)
B.aDI=s(["Make your mental associations weird or funny\u2014they are easier to remember.","Visualize walking through the room in a specific path."],t.s)
B.ahp=new A.a8("Memory Palace","MEMORY","Associate items with specific locations in a room and recall them later.","Tap the locations in the room and select the correct item from the list.",B.aO3,B.aDI)
B.awQ=s(["Step 1: Read the sequence of numbers to add or subtract.","Step 2: Mentally move the beads on an imaginary abacus.","Step 3: Keep track of the final bead positions.","Step 4: Type in the final numeric result."],t.s)
B.aJi=s(["Familiarize yourself with the value of top (5) and bottom (1) beads.","Use your fingers to physically mimic moving the beads in the air."],t.s)
B.aij=new A.a8("Mental Abacus","MATH","Perform calculations by visualizing an abacus and moving its beads mentally.","Enter the final calculated number using the keypad.",B.awQ,B.aJi)
B.aLw=s(["Step 1: Look at the date presented on the screen.","Step 2: Apply the Doomsday rule or a similar mental math calendar algorithm.","Step 3: Calculate the anchor day and offset.","Step 4: Select the resulting day of the week."],t.s)
B.atk=s(["Memorize the month codes and century codes beforehand.","Practice finding the anchor day for the current year to speed up calculations."],t.s)
B.aiY=new A.a8("Mental Calendar","MATH","Calculate the day of the week for a given random date.","Tap the correct day of the week from the multiple choices.",B.aLw,B.atk)
B.aQJ=s(["Step 1: Note your starting position on the grid.","Step 2: Read or listen to the sequence of directional movements (e.g., North, East).","Step 3: Track the movements mentally without touching the screen.","Step 4: Tap the final cell where the path ends."],t.s)
B.aRG=s(["Cancel out opposing moves in your head (e.g., Up then Down means you didn't move).","Keep your eyes fixed on the starting point and move your focus exactly as instructed."],t.s)
B.aim=new A.a8("Mental Mapping","SPATIAL","Follow a series of directional instructions mentally and identify the final location on a map.","Tap the final destination cell on the grid.",B.aQJ,B.aRG)
B.aUM=s(["Step 1: Look at the primary 3D block structure.","Step 2: Look at the second 3D block structure.","Step 3: Mentally rotate the first structure to align with the second.","Step 4: Decide if they are the exact same shape or a mirrored version."],t.s)
B.aX9=s(["Focus on a single distinctive feature or 'arm' of the shape and track its rotation.","Try to identify the handedness (left/right) of asymmetric parts."],t.s)
B.akP=new A.a8("Mental Rotation","SPATIAL","Determine if two 3D shapes are identical but rotated, or mirror images.","Tap 'Match' or 'Different' based on your spatial visualization.",B.aUM,B.aX9)
B.aA6=s(["Step 1: Tap a random tile to open up a starting area.","Step 2: Look at the numbers; a '1' means exactly one mine is adjacent to it.","Step 3: Long-press to place a flag where you are certain a mine exists.","Step 4: Safely tap all non-mine tiles to complete the level."],t.s)
B.au2=s(["If a '1' touches only one unrevealed tile, that tile MUST be a mine.","Once you've flagged the correct number of mines around a number, all its other adjacent tiles are safe."],t.s)
B.ajO=new A.a8("Minesweeper","LOGIC","Clear the board without detonating any hidden mines, using numbered clues that indicate adjacent mines.","Tap a tile to reveal it. Long-press to flag a suspected mine.",B.aA6,B.au2)
B.aCF=s(["Step 1: Carefully observe the target image presented at the start.","Step 2: Examine the multiple-choice options presented.","Step 3: Mentally mirror the target image along the specified axis.","Step 4: Tap the option that matches your mental reflection to advance."],t.s)
B.aMl=s(["Focus on asymmetrical details like protrusions or colors.","Pick one specific point on the target and find where it should end up after the flip.","Eliminate clearly incorrect options first to improve your odds."],t.s)
B.aji=new A.a8("Mirror Image","SPATIAL","Identify the exact mirror reflection of the presented shape or image.","Tap the correct reflection from the list of multiple-choice options.",B.aCF,B.aMl)
B.aJn=s(["Step 1: Identify the starting point of the beam and the final target.","Step 2: Note the obstacles and empty spaces in the grid.","Step 3: Tap to place a mirror and tap again to rotate it.","Step 4: Align the mirrors so the beam reflects at 90-degree angles to reach the goal."],t.s)
B.aHC=s(["Work backwards from the target to figure out the required final reflection.","Count the number of available mirrors; you might need to use all of them.","Avoid placing mirrors where the beam will hit an obstacle."],t.s)
B.al3=new A.a8("Mirror Maze","SPATIAL","Navigate a laser or light beam through a maze to the target by placing mirrors.","Tap grid cells to place or rotate mirrors to deflect the path.",B.aJn,B.aHC)
B.ayF=s(["Step 1: Look at the dotted outline of the shape you need to trace.","Step 2: Place your finger on the starting point.","Step 3: Drag your finger to trace the shape, adjusting for the inverted movement.","Step 4: Complete the full outline with minimal deviation to achieve a high score."],t.s)
B.au5=s(["Move slowly and deliberately, especially around corners.","Focus your eyes on the drawing tip rather than your finger.","Anticipate the opposite direction before making a move."],t.s)
B.al1=new A.a8("Mirror Tracing","SPATIAL","Trace a given shape as accurately as possible while your input is mirrored.","Drag your finger across the screen to draw; your strokes will appear mirrored.",B.ayF,B.au5)
B.aRX=s(["Step 1: Analyze the given numbers and the target result of the equation.","Step 2: Estimate which operations will get you closer to the target.","Step 3: Tap the empty slots and insert operators.","Step 4: The game checks if your filled equation evaluates to the target result."],t.s)
B.att=s(["Remember the order of operations (multiplication/division before addition/subtraction).","If the target is much larger than the operands, you likely need multiplication.","If the target is small or fractional, look for division or subtraction."],t.s)
B.aiT=new A.a8("Missing Operator","MATH","Fill in the missing mathematical operators to make the given equation correct.","Tap an empty operator slot, then tap the desired operator (+, -, \xd7, \xf7).",B.aRX,B.att)
B.aDs=s(["Step 1: Read the consonant skeleton of the word and its accompanying clue.","Step 2: Try to sound out possible words that fit the consonants.","Step 3: Tap the vowel keys in the correct sequence.","Step 4: Complete the word to move on to the next challenge."],t.s)
B.asV=s(["Use the context clues heavily; they often give away the meaning.","Look for common prefixes and suffixes that might hint at the vowels.","If stuck, try plugging in 'E' or 'A' first, as they are the most common."],t.s)
B.ai8=new A.a8("Missing Vowels","WORD","Identify the correct word by filling in its missing vowels.","Tap the correct vowels from the keyboard to complete the word.",B.aDs,B.asV)
B.aTL=s(["Step 1: Read the base modulo (e.g., Modulo 12, like a standard clock).","Step 2: Look at the given arithmetic expression.","Step 3: Perform the calculation and find the remainder when divided by the base.","Step 4: Tap the correct answer."],t.s)
B.aCp=s(["For Modulo 12, just think of adding or subtracting hours on a clock face.","If a number is larger than the modulo, subtract the modulo until it's smaller.","Negative numbers mean counting backwards from the modulo base."],t.s)
B.akj=new A.a8("Modulo Clock","MATH","Solve arithmetic problems using modular (clock) arithmetic.","Tap the number buttons to input your calculated answer.",B.aTL,B.aCp)
B.aRi=s(["Step 1: Note the target modulo rule required for the path.","Step 2: Start at the highlighted beginning cell.","Step 3: Select an adjacent cell that fulfills the modulo condition relative to the current cell.","Step 4: Continue until you reach the target destination."],t.s)
B.aUL=s(["Look ahead one or two steps before committing to a move.","Quickly calculate the remainders of all surrounding cells to find candidates.","If you hit a dead end, backtrack and try an alternative route."],t.s)
B.aj5=new A.a8("Modulo Path","MATH","Find a continuous path through a grid where adjacent numbers satisfy a specific modulo rule.","Tap or drag across adjacent grid cells to form a valid path.",B.aRi,B.aUL)
B.awT=s(["Step 1: Memorize the items that are briefly highlighted at the start.","Step 2: Keep your eyes focused on those targets as all items begin to move.","Step 3: Maintain focus until all movement stops.","Step 4: Tap on the exact items that were originally highlighted."],t.s)
B.aUu=s(["Don't look directly at one object; use a soft, central gaze to track the whole group.","Group the targets mentally into a polygon and watch how the shape morphs.","Avoid getting distracted by items crossing paths."],t.s)
B.agP=new A.a8("Multiple Object Tracking","ATTENTION","Keep track of specific target objects as they move randomly among identical distractors.","Tap the objects you believe were the original targets after they stop moving.",B.awT,B.aUu)
B.aBO=s(["Step 1: Observe the different categories of objects you need to track.","Step 2: As objects appear and disappear, update your mental tally for each.","Step 3: When the sequence ends, input your final count for every category.","Step 4: Submit your answers to see if you tracked them all correctly."],t.s)
B.aH1=s(["Repeat the counts rhythmically in your head (e.g., 'two red, three blue').","Use your fingers to keep track of one category while mentally tracking the other.","Stay calm and don't panic if a lot of objects appear at once."],t.s)
B.aj_=new A.a8("Multi Track Counter","ATTENTION","Keep simultaneous counts of different types of objects appearing on screen.","Tap the respective plus/minus buttons or input the final counts for each category.",B.aBO,B.aH1)
B.atD=s(["Step 1: Read the provided narrative carefully within the given time limit.","Step 2: Try to memorize key details like names, numbers, colors, and sequence of events.","Step 3: Once the text disappears, read the comprehension questions.","Step 4: Select the correct answer based on what you remember."],t.s)
B.aUb=s(["Visualize the story in your mind to make details more memorable.","Pay special attention to proper nouns, dates, and numbers.","Don't just skim; try to understand the actual plot and context."],t.s)
B.ajP=new A.a8("Narrative Recall","MEMORY","Read a short story and correctly answer questions about specific details.","Tap the correct answer from the multiple-choice options provided.",B.atD,B.aUb)
B.aVJ=s(["Step 1: Note the 'N' level for the current game (e.g., 2-back means matching the item 2 steps ago).","Step 2: Observe the sequence of items (shapes, letters, or positions) appearing one by one.","Step 3: When the current item appears, compare it to the item 'N' steps back.","Step 4: Tap the corresponding button to register your answer before the next item appears."],t.s)
B.aKF=s(["Continuously update your mental 'buffer' by dropping the oldest item and adding the newest.","Say the sequence of the last 'N' items out loud in your head.","Stay focused; a single lapse in concentration can ruin your sequence."],t.s)
B.ak2=new A.a8("N-Back","MEMORY","Indicate whether the current item matches the item presented 'N' steps previously.","Tap 'Match' or 'No Match' as each item appears.",B.aVJ,B.aKF)
B.azo=s(["Step 1: Look at the complex image presented on the screen.","Step 2: Shift your focus from the solid objects to the empty background spaces.","Step 3: Identify the cohesive shape formed by that empty space.","Step 4: Select or input the correct answer."],t.s)
B.aQW=s(["Try squinting or relaxing your eyes to blur the foreground.","Look at the edges of the solid objects; they form the outline of the negative shape.","Mentally invert the colors (imagine the background is black and objects are white)."],t.s)
B.akT=new A.a8("Negative Space Detection","SPATIAL","Identify the hidden shape or letter formed by the negative space between objects.","Tap the correct answer from the options, or type the identified shape.",B.azo,B.aQW)
B.aNK=s(["Step 1: Look at the numbers at the beginning of each row and column. They indicate consecutive filled cells.","Step 2: Use intersecting clues to deduce which cells must be filled.","Step 3: Mark cells you know must be empty with an 'X' to narrow down possibilities.",u.cX],t.s)
B.aUj=s(["Start with the largest numbers, especially those that take up more than half the row/column.","Always mark empty spaces with an 'X' once you complete a clue block.","Never guess; every move should be based on pure logic."],t.s)
B.ak7=new A.a8("Nonogram","LOGIC","Fill in a grid based on numerical clues to reveal a hidden pixel art picture.","Tap a cell to fill it, tap again to mark it as empty (X), or long-press to drag.",B.aNK,B.aUj)
B.aMc=s(["Step 1: Look at the grid divided into boldly outlined regions.","Step 2: Shade exactly two cells per region.","Step 3: Ensure that every shaded cell shares exactly one edge with another shaded cell (forming dominos).","Step 4: Ensure no domino touches another domino, not even diagonally."],t.s)
B.aJv=s(["If a region has only two cells, they must both be shaded.","Once you place a domino, surround it with empty marks since no other domino can touch it.","Use corner logic to deduce where dominos are forced to go."],t.s)
B.ah9=new A.a8("Norinori","LOGIC","Shade exactly two cells in every defined region, ensuring no shaded cells touch diagonally or share borders in groups larger than two.","Tap cells to toggle their shaded state, or mark them as definitively empty.",B.aMc,B.aJv)
B.aBL=s(["Step 1: Look at the central 'whole' number and the connected 'part' numbers.","Step 2: Subtract the known parts from the whole to find the missing value.","Step 3: Input the correct number into the empty circle.","Step 4: Complete all bonds on the screen to progress."],t.s)
B.axI=s(["Use subtraction for finding a missing part, and addition for finding a missing whole.","Memorize combinations of 10 and 100 to speed up calculations.","Double-check your math before submitting the final answer."],t.s)
B.akp=new A.a8("Number Bonds","MATH","Complete the number bonds by finding the missing part that adds up to the given whole.","Tap the missing node and use the number pad to input the correct value.",B.aBL,B.axI)
B.aAI=s(["Step 1: A large group of items or a complex math problem appears briefly.","Step 2: Make a quick mental approximation of the quantity or answer.","Step 3: Select the option that is closest to your approximation.","Step 4: Score points based on how close your estimate was to the actual number."],t.s)
B.aRj=s(["Don't try to count every item individually; you won't have time.","Count a small sub-section (like one quadrant) and multiply by the total number of sections.","For math problems, round numbers to the nearest ten or hundred before calculating."],t.s)
B.al2=new A.a8("Numerical Estimation","MATH","Estimate the number of items or the result of a complex calculation without exact counting.","Select the closest estimate from a list, or adjust a slider to your guessed value.",B.aAI,B.aRj)
B.atF=s(["Step 1: Look at the grid containing numbers. Each number is part of exactly one island of that exact size.","Step 2: Ensure all black cells form a single connected network.","Step 3: Ensure there are no 2x2 squares of black cells anywhere.","Step 4: Complete the grid by correctly defining all islands and the river."],t.s)
B.aS5=s(["A cell containing a '1' is its own island, so surround it entirely with black cells.","When two islands get too close, separate them with a wall of black cells.","If a block of black cells is about to form a 2x2 square, leave one cell white."],t.s)
B.aic=new A.a8("Nurikabe","LOGIC","Create 'islands' of white cells containing exactly one number, surrounded by a continuous 'river' of black cells.","Tap cells to mark them as black (river) or white (island).",B.atF,B.aS5)
B.aPG=s(["Step 1: Memorize the layout and position of all objects on the screen.","Step 2: Wait for the screen to blink or for the objects to be briefly hidden.","Step 3: Observe the new layout and spot the discrepancy.","Step 4: Tap the object that is in a different place than before."],t.s)
B.aG0=s(["Group the objects mentally by their relative positions (e.g., 'apple next to banana').","Focus on the edges or corners of the layout first.","Don't try to memorize absolute coordinates; memorize spatial relationships."],t.s)
B.agp=new A.a8("Object Displacement","MEMORY","Identify which object was moved or swapped after the screen briefly goes blank.","Tap on the object that has changed its position.",B.aPG,B.aG0)
B.aPv=s(["Step 1: Watch carefully as the target object is placed under one of the containers.","Step 2: Keep your eyes fixed on that specific container as they all swap places.","Step 3: Wait for the shuffling animation to completely finish.","Step 4: Tap the container you believe holds the target."],t.s)
B.aPZ=s(["Do not take your eyes off the target container, even for a split second.","Do not try to track all containers, only the one with the target.","If you lose track, try to guess based on its last known trajectory."],t.s)
B.ai2=new A.a8("Object Shuffle","MEMORY","Track a hidden target object as it is shuffled rapidly among identical containers.","Tap the container holding the target after the shuffling stops.",B.aPv,B.aPZ)
B.atZ=s(["Step 1: Focus on the center of the screen.","Step 2: A number will appear for a fraction of a second.","Step 3: Determine if the number is odd or even.","Step 4: Tap the correct button as fast as possible to maximize your score."],t.s)
B.aQg=s(["Only look at the last digit of the number to determine if it's odd or even.","Keep your fingers hovering over both buttons to minimize reaction time.","Don't get distracted by the length of the number."],t.s)
B.ajW=new A.a8("Odd Even Flash","ATTENTION","Quickly categorize a rapidly flashed number as odd or even.","Tap the 'Odd' or 'Even' button corresponding to the number.",B.atZ,B.aQg)
B.aLF=s(["Step 1: Scan the array of shapes, symbols, or images.","Step 2: Identify the pattern or rule that most of them follow.","Step 3: Find the one item that breaks this rule.","Step 4: Tap the anomalous item before time runs out."],t.s)
B.aLQ=s(["Look for differences in color, shape, orientation, or size.","Scan systematically (e.g., row by row) rather than randomly.","If it's a grid of similar characters (like 'O' and '0'), unfocus your eyes slightly to make the odd one pop."],t.s)
B.ak6=new A.a8("Odd One Out","ATTENTION","Identify the single object that does not share the common characteristics of the rest.","Tap the odd object out from the given grid.",B.aLF,B.aLQ)
B.aXh=s(["Step 1: Observe the reference shape and the multiple choices.","Step 2: Mentally rotate each choice to align with the reference shape.","Step 3: Identify which shape requires a flip (mirroring) instead of just rotation.","Step 4: Tap that non-matching, mirrored shape."],t.s)
B.aLS=s(["Pick a specific 'pointer' or asymmetric feature on the shape and track its orientation.","Determine the 'handedness' (left or right-facing) of the objects.","Mentally rotate the shapes by 90-degree increments."],t.s)
B.ajz=new A.a8("Odd Rotation","SPATIAL","Find the object that is a mirrored version, not just a rotated version, of the others.","Tap the object that cannot be rotated to match the target shape.",B.aXh,B.aLS)
B.atf=s(["Step 1: Look at your starting word and the target final word.","Step 2: Identify a single letter you can change to form a new, valid dictionary word.","Step 3: Input the new word.","Step 4: Repeat the process until you successfully reach the target word."],t.s)
B.aR5=s(["Work from both ends; think of words that are one letter away from the target.","Vowels are usually the easiest to swap out to make new words.","Don't worry if your path isn't the shortest, as long as every step is a real word."],t.s)
B.ajY=new A.a8("One Letter Shift","WORD","Transform one word into another by changing exactly one letter at a time, creating valid words at each step.","Use the keyboard to type the next valid word in the sequence.",B.atf,B.aR5)
B.aXp=s(["Step 1: An equation will appear; determine if it is correct and tap True or False.","Step 2: Immediately after, a letter or word will appear briefly. Memorize it.","Step 3: Repeat this alternating process for several rounds.","Step 4: At the recall screen, type in all the letters/words you memorized in their exact order."],t.s)
B.aOk=s(["Solve the math as quickly as possible to give yourself more time to rehearse the memory sequence.","Use acronyms or make a story out of the letters/words to remember them.","Say the sequence aloud in your head constantly."],t.s)
B.aiH=new A.a8("Operation Span","MEMORY","Solve simple math problems while simultaneously remembering a sequence of letters or words.","Answer True/False for the math equation, then input the memorized sequence at the end.",B.aXp,B.aOk)
B.aLI=s(["Step 1: Watch the object traveling along its orbital path.","Step 2: Note the position of the stationary target zone.","Step 3: Anticipate the object's speed and trajectory.","Step 4: Tap the screen precisely when the object overlaps the target."],t.s)
B.aCA=s(["Focus your eyes on the target zone, not the moving object.","Learn the rhythm and speed of the orbit.","Account for your own reaction time by tapping slightly before perfect alignment."],t.s)
B.ahW=new A.a8("Orbit Tap","ATTENTION","Tap the screen exactly when a moving object aligns with a target zone on its orbit.","Tap anywhere on the screen to trigger the action.",B.aLI,B.aCA)
B.aWX=s(["Step 1: Read through all the provided phrases carefully.","Step 2: Look for phrases where two consecutive or closely placed words have opposite meanings.","Step 3: Discard normal descriptive phrases.","Step 4: Tap the contradictory phrase (e.g., 'deafening silence') to score."],t.s)
B.axa=s(["Look for extreme adjectives paired with extreme nouns.","Read the literal meaning of each word independently to spot the contradiction.","Familiarize yourself with common oxymorons like 'jumbo shrimp' or 'awfully good'."],t.s)
B.agU=new A.a8("Oxymoron Hunt","WORD","Identify the oxymoron (a phrase containing contradictory terms) from a list of phrases.","Tap the phrase that constitutes an oxymoron.",B.aWX,B.axa)
B.aJt=s(["Step 1: Review the available letter tiles.","Step 2: Identify pairs of identical letters, as they must mirror each other.","Step 3: Place the single, unpaired letter (if any) in the exact center.","Step 4: Arrange the remaining pairs symmetrically to spell a valid word."],t.s)
B.aMw=s(["Always find the center letter first if the word length is odd.","Work from the outside in, placing common prefixes and their mirrored suffixes.","Ensure the resulting string actually spells a real word in the dictionary."],t.s)
B.akd=new A.a8("Palindrome Builder","WORD","Construct a valid palindrome (a word that reads the same forwards and backwards) using given letter tiles.","Tap or drag letters into the correct slots to form the word.",B.aJt,B.aMw)
B.aCK=s(["Step 1: Read the incomplete sentence provided on screen.","Step 2: Determine which letters of the alphabet have not yet been used.","Step 3: Deduce the missing word that uses those exact remaining letters.","Step 4: Input the correct word to complete the pangram."],t.s)
B.aDn=s(["Keep a mental checklist of rare letters like Q, X, Z, and J.","Use grammar and context clues to figure out what type of word is missing.","Remember classic pangrams like 'The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog'."],t.s)
B.alh=new A.a8("Pangram Sprint","WORD","Identify missing letters or assemble a pangram (a sentence containing every letter of the alphabet).","Type the missing letters or drag words into order.",B.aCK,B.aDn)
B.aMU=s(["Step 1: Observe the folding sequence indicated by the arrows.","Step 2: Note where the hole punch is made on the folded paper.","Step 3: Mentally unfold the paper in reverse order.","Step 4: Select the option that matches your visualized hole pattern."],t.s)
B.aT4=s(["Track the reflections of the punch across each fold line.","Eliminate options that have holes in impossible locations.","Remember that diagonal folds swap the X and Y coordinates."],t.s)
B.aiP=new A.a8("Paper Folding","SPATIAL","Determine the final pattern of holes after a folded piece of paper is punched and unfolded.","Tap on the correct result grid out of the 4 options provided.",B.aMU,B.aT4)
B.atM=s(["Step 1: Identify the start (S) and exit (E) points on the grid.","Step 2: Note the required step length provided in the hint.","Step 3: Drag through the grid cells to create a path of the exact length.","Step 4: Connect the path to the exit point to complete the level."],t.s)
B.aKY=s(["If you reach the exit too early, you need to find a more winding route.","Keep track of the number of steps as you drag.","Work backwards from the exit to find valid path segments."],t.s)
B.ahz=new A.a8("Path Finder","LOGIC","Trace a continuous path of a specific length from the start point to the exit point without overlapping.","Drag your finger across the grid to draw the path from start to finish.",B.atM,B.aKY)
B.atU=s(["Step 1: Observe the two different colored paths drawn on the screen.","Step 2: Follow the trajectories of both paths visually.","Step 3: Locate the single cell where they overlap.","Step 4: Tap the intersection cell to verify your answer."],t.s)
B.aQY=s(["Focus on the general region where horizontal and vertical segments meet.","Trace one path with your eyes and look for the color break of the other.","Don't rush; confirm the grid square aligns with both path lines."],t.s)
B.ah3=new A.a8("Path Intersect","SPATIAL","Identify the exact grid coordinate where two overlapping colored paths intersect.","Tap the specific cell on the grid where the paths cross.",B.atU,B.aQY)
B.aMo=s(["Step 1: Watch carefully as a path is highlighted on the grid.","Step 2: Wait for the path to disappear and the grid to clear.","Step 3: Tap the starting cell of the remembered path.","Step 4: Continue tapping adjacent cells to complete the sequence."],t.s)
B.aOc=s(["Visualize the path as a distinct shape rather than individual steps.","Group the movements into chunks (e.g., 'two right, one up').","Keep your eyes on the grid even when it clears to maintain spatial memory."],t.s)
B.ai3=new A.a8("Path Recall","MEMORY","Remember a path shown briefly on a grid and recreate it exactly from memory.","Tap the grid cells in the correct sequence to reconstruct the path.",B.aMo,B.aOc)
B.aN1=s(["Step 1: Watch the nodes light up and lines connect in a specific order.","Step 2: Wait for the drawing phase to complete.","Step 3: Start at the first node and drag to recreate the connections.","Step 4: Release after the final connection to submit your pattern."],t.s)
B.aT5=s(["Focus on the geometric shape formed by the lines.","Trace the pattern in the air with your finger as it is shown.","Remember the start and end points as anchor references."],t.s)
B.aix=new A.a8("Pattern Sequence Draw","MEMORY","Observe a sequence of connected lines being drawn between nodes and replicate the exact pattern.","Drag your finger to connect the nodes in the correct order.",B.aN1,B.aT5)
B.aRh=s(["Step 1: Read the percentage expressions presented on the screen.","Step 2: Quickly estimate the absolute value of each expression.","Step 3: Compare the calculated values.","Step 4: Tap the box containing the highest value."],t.s)
B.aCz=s(["Use estimation (e.g., 50% is half, 10% is moving the decimal).","Look for obvious low outliers and ignore them.","Focus on the base number size if the percentages are similar."],t.s)
B.ajf=new A.a8("Percentage Peak","MATH","Calculate or estimate percentages to identify the highest resulting value among multiple options.","Tap the option that represents the largest calculated amount.",B.aRh,B.aCz)
B.aAL=s(["Step 1: Note the original price of the item and the discount percentage.","Step 2: Calculate the discount amount by applying the percentage.","Step 3: Subtract the discount from the original price.","Step 4: Tap the option matching your calculated final price."],t.s)
B.aN2=s(["For 20% off, calculate 10% and double it, then subtract.","Alternatively, calculate 80% of the original price directly.","Round numbers for quick estimation if options are far apart."],t.s)
B.akw=new A.a8("Percentage Shopping","MATH","Calculate the final price of items by correctly applying percentage discounts or markups.","Select the correct final price from the options provided.",B.aAL,B.aN2)
B.aFG=s(["Step 1: Fixate your eyes on the central fixation point.","Step 2: Wait for a target shape to briefly appear on the edges.","Step 3: Tap the corresponding area on the screen before the target vanishes.","Step 4: Continue maintaining central focus for the next target."],t.s)
B.aF3=s(["Do not move your eyes from the center; trust your peripheral vision.","Relax your focus slightly to widen your field of view.","React quickly as the presentation time decreases with higher levels."],t.s)
B.ah8=new A.a8("Peripheral Focus","ATTENTION","Keep your central focus steady while quickly identifying targets appearing in your peripheral vision.","Tap the screen in the quadrant where the target appears.",B.aFG,B.aF3)
B.awK=s(["Step 1: Examine the 3D block structure shown in the center.","Step 2: Note the requested viewing direction (e.g., Top, Left, Front).","Step 3: Mentally rotate the object to face that direction.","Step 4: Select the corresponding 2D silhouette from the options."],t.s)
B.aFF=s(["Count the maximum height or width of blocks to rule out incorrect options.","Look for distinct features like gaps or protruding blocks.","Visualize standing on the side of the object being requested."],t.s)
B.agM=new A.a8("Perspective Shift View","SPATIAL","Identify how a 3D block structure looks when viewed from a different specific angle.","Tap the 2D projection that matches the requested viewing angle.",B.awK,B.aFF)
B.avA=s(["Step 1: Observe the avatar's position and the direction they are facing.","Step 2: Note the target object in relation to the avatar.","Step 3: Mentally step into the avatar's shoes to determine left or right.","Step 4: Tap the correct answer option."],t.s)
B.aRC=s(["If the avatar is facing you, their left and right are opposite to yours.","Use physical cues like turning your body or head slightly to help visualize.","Focus on the avatar's hands or orientation markers."],t.s)
B.aiC=new A.a8("Perspective Taking","SPATIAL","Determine the left/right orientation or spatial layout from the viewpoint of an avatar in the scene.","Select the correct direction or object layout based on the avatar's perspective.",B.avA,B.aRC)
B.axy=s(["Step 1: Read the phonetic spelling provided on the screen.","Step 2: Sound the word out loud if necessary.","Step 3: Identify the standard English word it represents.","Step 4: Enter your answer to proceed."],t.s)
B.aKO=s(["Saying the word aloud quickly helps bypass visual spelling confusion.","Focus on the vowel sounds as they are often the biggest clues.","Don't overthink silent letters that are missing in phonetic spelling."],t.s)
B.ah0=new A.a8("Phonetic Guess","WORD","Decipher the correct English word based on its phonetic spelling or pronunciation text.","Type or select the correctly spelled word.",B.axy,B.aKO)
B.awp=s(["Step 1: Identify the start and end points of the pipeline.","Step 2: Tap pieces to align them towards adjacent tiles.","Step 3: Connect all segments ensuring there are no open, leaking ends.","Step 4: Complete the connection to let the fluid flow and finish the level."],t.s)
B.aRH=s(["Start from the edges or fixed points and work your way inwards.","Look for corners and straight pieces that can only fit in one logical way.","Avoid creating closed loops that don't connect to the main line."],t.s)
B.alc=new A.a8("Pipes","LOGIC","Rotate pipe segments to create a continuous, unbroken flow from the start point to the end point.","Tap on individual pipe tiles to rotate them 90 degrees clockwise.",B.awp,B.aRH)
B.aQc=s(["Step 1: Study the target pixel pattern shown at the top.","Step 2: Tap the corresponding cells on your empty grid below.","Step 3: Ensure every colored square matches the target exactly.","Step 4: Complete the pattern to trigger the win condition."],t.s)
B.aCC=s(["Work row by row or column by column to avoid missing pixels.","Use the edges and corners as reference points.","Count the empty spaces between pixels for accurate placement."],t.s)
B.alb=new A.a8("Pixel Mimic","SPATIAL","Recreate a specific pixel art pattern exactly on a blank grid.","Tap cells on your grid to toggle their color to match the target.",B.aQc,B.aCC)
B.aEA=s(["Step 1: Read the given portmanteau word (e.g., 'Brunch').","Step 2: Analyze the word to find the blended components.","Step 3: Select the first root word (e.g., 'Breakfast').","Step 4: Select the second root word (e.g., 'Lunch') to submit."],t.s)
B.awe=s(["Look at the beginning and end of the word for root fragments.","Think about the definition of the portmanteau to derive the roots.","Use a process of elimination if the options are tricky."],t.s)
B.ak3=new A.a8("Portmanteau Split","WORD","Identify the two original root words that were combined to form the given portmanteau word.","Select the two correct words from the provided list.",B.aEA,B.awe)
B.aJO=s(["Step 1: Look at the main number at the top of the tree.","Step 2: Find two numbers that multiply to make that number.","Step 3: Continue breaking down composite numbers until only primes remain.","Step 4: Fill in all nodes correctly to finish the tree."],t.s)
B.aLW=s(["Always check if a number is divisible by 2 or 3 first.","Remember that branches must multiply to equal the node above them.","Only prime numbers belong at the very bottom leaf nodes."],t.s)
B.ahh=new A.a8("Prime Factor Trees","MATH","Break down a composite number into its prime factors by completing a branching tree diagram.","Tap empty nodes and select the correct prime factors.",B.aJO,B.aLW)
B.avO=s(["Step 1: Scan the grid of numbers presented.","Step 2: Identify numbers that are only divisible by 1 and themselves.","Step 3: Tap them quickly to score points.","Step 4: Avoid tapping composite numbers, which will result in a penalty."],t.s)
B.awO=s(["Memorize the prime numbers up to 100 for speed.","Quickly eliminate even numbers (except 2) and numbers ending in 5.","Check divisibility by 3 (sum of digits) to quickly rule out composites."],t.s)
B.ajg=new A.a8("Prime Hunter","MATH","Identify and select all the prime numbers from a grid before the timer runs out.","Tap the numbers you believe are prime to collect them.",B.avO,B.awO)
B.aGz=s(["Step 1: An equation appears on the screen.","Step 2: Perform the calculation in your head rapidly.","Step 3: Input or select the correct answer.","Step 4: Move on immediately to the next equation to maximize your score."],t.s)
B.aWZ=s(["Rely on mental math shortcuts and rote memorization.","For multiple choice, use estimation to instantly eliminate wrong answers.","Maintain a steady rhythm; don't panic if you miss one."],t.s)
B.ajt=new A.a8("Quick Math","MATH","Solve a series of basic arithmetic equations as quickly as possible.","Tap the correct answer from the choices or use the keypad to type it.",B.aGz,B.aWZ)
B.aA1=s(["Step 1: Read the radical expression shown on screen.","Step 2: Determine the root value or simplify the expression.","Step 3: Compare your result with the provided options.","Step 4: Tap the correct option to advance."],t.s)
B.aII=s(["Memorize common perfect squares (1-144) and perfect cubes (1-125).","For simplifications, find the largest perfect square factor inside the root.","Use the last digit of the number to estimate the root."],t.s)
B.ago=new A.a8("Radical Roots","MATH","Calculate the square or cube roots of given numbers, or simplify radical expressions.","Select the correct numerical answer or simplified form from the options.",B.aA1,B.aII)
B.aPm=s(["Step 1: Read the sentence presented and tap True if it makes sense, False if it doesn't.","Step 2: Memorize the very last word of that sentence.","Step 3: Repeat this process for the whole sequence of sentences.","Step 4: At the end, select the memorized last words in the exact order they appeared."],t.s)
B.aFe=s(["Create a mental story or acronym using the last words to aid memory.","Don't let the True/False decision distract you from storing the word.","Rehearse the list of words internally between sentences."],t.s)
B.akB=new A.a8("Reading Span","MEMORY","Read sentences, determine their logical validity, and remember the final word of each sentence.","Tap True/False for sentences, then select the remembered words in order.",B.aPm,B.aFe)
B.aCx=s(["Step 1: Wait for the screen or indicator to change color/state.","Step 2: Keep your finger hovered closely over the screen.","Step 3: Tap immediately when the cue occurs.","Step 4: Avoid tapping early to prevent a false start penalty."],t.s)
B.aun=s(["Focus intensely on the center of the screen to minimize processing time.","Keep your tapping finger relaxed but ready to move.","Don't anticipate the timing; react only to the actual visual change."],t.s)
B.ahy=new A.a8("Reflex Tap","ATTENTION","Test your reaction time by tapping the screen the instant a specific visual cue appears.","Tap anywhere on the screen as fast as possible when prompted.",B.aCx,B.aun)
B.aTA=s(["Step 1: Observe a series of paired items (e.g., a specific object in a specific location).","Step 2: Focus on encoding the link between the two items.","Step 3: During the recall phase, one item of a pair will be shown.","Step 4: Select the corresponding matched item from the options."],t.s)
B.aDA=s(["Create vivid, bizarre mental images linking the two items together.","Say the pair out loud in a sentence to strengthen the memory.","Pay attention to unique details of similar-looking items."],t.s)
B.akQ=new A.a8("Relational Memory","MEMORY","Remember the specific pairings or relationships between different items presented.","Tap the correct item that completes the pair when prompted.",B.aTA,B.aDA)
B.aO4=s(["Step 1: A color word (e.g., 'BLUE') appears on screen in a different ink color (e.g., red ink).","Step 2: Suppress the urge to select the ink color.","Step 3: Read the text of the word.","Step 4: Tap the option that matches the written text."],t.s)
B.ax1=s(["Focus slightly off-center or squint to blur the color while reading.","Silently sound out the letters to reinforce reading over color perception.","Maintain a steady pace to avoid falling into the color-matching trap."],t.s)
B.agJ=new A.a8("Reverse Stroop","ATTENTION","Identify the written word itself while ignoring the contradictory ink color it is printed in.","Tap the button that corresponds to the text of the word, not the color.",B.aO4,B.ax1)
B.aUX=s(["Step 1: Read the target word at the top of the screen.","Step 2: Read through the provided options.","Step 3: Sound out the words to find the matching ending phonetic sound.","Step 4: Select the correct rhyming word to score."],t.s)
B.atA=s(["Ignore spelling; focus purely on the phonetic sound (e.g., 'weight' and 'late').","Say the target word and options aloud in your head.","Look out for near-rhymes designed to trick you."],t.s)
B.akc=new A.a8("Rhyme Master","WORD","Identify words that rhyme with a given target word from a selection of options.","Tap the word that rhymes with the target.",B.aUX,B.atA)
B.auX=s(["Step 1: Listen closely to the auditory rhythm played.","Step 2: Watch visual indicators if available to grasp the timing.","Step 3: When prompted, tap the screen to replicate the beat.","Step 4: Maintain the exact tempo and pauses of the original sequence."],t.s)
B.aRV=s(["Tap your foot or nod your head to internalize the beat while listening.","Subdivide the beat in your head to handle off-beat taps.","Don't rush; keeping a steady internal metronome is key."],t.s)
B.ah2=new A.a8("Rhythm Master","MEMORY","Listen to a rhythm sequence and tap it back with accurate timing.","Tap the designated button in sync with the memorized rhythm.",B.auX,B.aRV)
B.aS2=s(["Step 1: Read the mathematical equation in Roman numerals.","Step 2: Convert the numerals into standard numbers in your head.","Step 3: Perform the addition, subtraction, or multiplication.","Step 4: Convert the result back to Roman numerals and select it."],t.s)
B.avX=s(["Memorize key values: I=1, V=5, X=10, L=50, C=100.","Watch out for subtractive notation (e.g., IV = 4, IX = 9).","Do the math in base-10 first to avoid errors."],t.s)
B.ai9=new A.a8("Roman Arithmetic","MATH","Solve arithmetic problems presented entirely in Roman numerals.","Tap the correct Roman numeral answer from the choices provided.",B.aS2,B.avX)
B.aKP=s(["Step 1: Scan the room carefully during the observation phase.","Step 2: Memorize object positions, colors, and presence.","Step 3: Wait for the screen to blink or transition.","Step 4: Inspect the new room state and tap the discrepancy."],t.s)
B.aNQ=s(["Scan the room systematically (e.g., left to right, top to bottom).","Count the number of items on shelves or tables.","Focus on prominent objects that are likely candidates for change."],t.s)
B.ahM=new A.a8("Room Inspector","ATTENTION","Memorize the layout and objects in a room, then identify what changed after a brief transition.","Tap the objects that were added, removed, or altered.",B.aKP,B.aNQ)
B.aRS=s(["Step 1: Observe the ball's current position and the location of the exit.","Step 2: Plan a path through the corridors.","Step 3: Rotate the maze so gravity pulls the ball along your planned route.","Step 4: Catch the ball on walls to prevent it falling into traps or dead ends."],t.s)
B.aTg=s(["Think one step ahead about where the ball will land after rotation.","Use small, controlled rotations rather than spinning wildly.","Use corners to stall the ball while you reorient the maze."],t.s)
B.ake=new A.a8("Rotating Maze","SPATIAL","Navigate a ball through a maze to the exit by rotating the entire maze structure.","Tap the left or right rotation buttons (or drag) to tilt the maze.",B.aRS,B.aTg)
B.aKp=s(["Step 1: Look at the active sorting rule displayed on screen.","Step 2: Examine the current item to be sorted.","Step 3: Tap the corresponding pile that matches the rule.","Step 4: Pay close attention as the rule changes randomly and adapt immediately."],t.s)
B.aH4=s(["Continuously repeat the active rule in your head (e.g., 'Color, Color, Color').","When the rule switches, pause for a split second to reset your mental state.","Don't rely on muscle memory; evaluate each item deliberately."],t.s)
B.ai0=new A.a8("Rule Switcher","ATTENTION","Sort items based on a rule that dynamically changes (e.g., sorting by color, then switching to shape).","Tap the correct target pile based on the currently active rule.",B.aKp,B.aH4)
B.aKy=s(["Step 1: Watch the sequence of items presented one by one.","Step 2: Note that the sequence may stop at any time.","Step 3: When the sequence ends, tap the items corresponding to the last N items.","Step 4: Recall them in the exact order they appeared."],t.s)
B.aSe=s(["Continuously update your memory with the most recent items.","Rehearse the current target items in your mind as new ones appear.","Focus intensely on the sequence, as you won't know when it ends."],t.s)
B.ahV=new A.a8("Running Memory Span","MEMORY","Recall the last N items of a sequence after the presentation stops.","Tap the items in the order they were presented at the end of the sequence.",B.aKy,B.aSe)
B.aNz=s(["Step 1: A 5x5 grid of randomly placed numbers (1-25) is presented.","Step 2: Find and tap the number 1.","Step 3: Continue finding and tapping the numbers in ascending order (2, 3, 4...).","Step 4: Complete the grid in the shortest time possible."],t.s)
B.aQA=s(["Keep your eyes focused on the center of the grid.","Use your peripheral vision to locate the next numbers.","Try to spot the next number while moving your finger to the current one."],t.s)
B.ajV=new A.a8("Schulte Table","ATTENTION","Find and tap all the numbers in the grid in ascending order as fast as possible.","Tap the numbers on the grid in order, starting from 1.",B.aNz,B.aQA)
B.aEZ=s(["Step 1: Review the key at the top pairing symbols with digits 1-9.","Step 2: Look at the large target symbol presented in the center.","Step 3: Find its corresponding digit in the key.","Step 4: Tap the matching digit on the keypad as quickly as possible."],t.s)
B.axR=s(["Memorize the most frequent symbol-digit pairs to save time.","Keep your eyes on the target symbol and key, and rely on muscle memory for the keypad.","Maintain a steady rhythm to maximize your score."],t.s)
B.akq=new A.a8("Symbol Digit Modalities","ATTENTION","Match the correct digit to the presented symbol based on the provided key within the time limit.","Tap the number on the numpad that corresponds to the displayed symbol.",B.aEZ,B.axR)
B.aWN=s(["Step 1: Read the provided target words or concepts.","Step 2: Evaluate the given options for semantic relevance.","Step 3: Select the option that best connects to the targets.","Step 4: Answer as many correctly as possible within the limit."],t.s)
B.atu=s(["Look for shared categories or functional relationships.","Eliminate clearly unrelated options first.","Trust your immediate associations."],t.s)
B.aki=new A.a8("Semantic Association","WORD","Identify the word that is most closely related to the given target words.","Tap the word option that forms the strongest semantic connection.",B.aWN,B.atu)
B.aUy=s(["Step 1: Type any guess word into the text field and submit.","Step 2: Review the semantic distance score returned for your guess.","Step 3: A lower score means you are conceptually closer to the secret word.","Step 4: Hone in on synonyms and related concepts until you find the secret word (distance 0.0) before time expires."],t.s)
B.aVD=s(["Start with broad domain words (nature, food, space, items) to identify the category.","When a guess gives a low score (< 25), test specific parts, functions, and close synonyms.","A distance score of 0.0 indicates you have successfully discovered the secret word."],t.s)
B.ail=new A.a8("Semantic Distance","WORD","Uncover the secret target word by guessing related words and tracking their semantic distance.","Type your word guess in the input box and tap send or press enter.",B.aUy,B.aVD)
B.azP=s(["Step 1: Start with the initial target word.","Step 2: Select a word from the options that is semantically linked to it.","Step 3: The selected word becomes the new target.","Step 4: Continue building the chain until it is complete."],t.s)
B.aQX=s(["Think a step ahead to ensure you don't paint yourself into a corner.","Associations can be categorical, synonymous, or functional.","If stuck, look at the remaining options to reverse-engineer the path."],t.s)
B.aho=new A.a8("Semantic Link","WORD","Form a chain of words where each word shares a meaningful connection with the preceding one.","Tap the next logical word in the sequence from the available options.",B.azP,B.aQX)
B.aKU=s(["Step 1: Read all the jumbled words provided on the screen.","Step 2: Identify the subject, verb, and object of the sentence.","Step 3: Arrange the words in proper syntactic order.","Step 4: Submit the completed sentence to verify correctness."],t.s)
B.azH=s(["Look for capitalized words to start the sentence and punctuation to end it.","Group common phrases or compound nouns together first.","Read your formed sentence aloud in your head to check for natural flow."],t.s)
B.agW=new A.a8("Sentence Unscramble","WORD","Rearrange the jumbled words to form a grammatically correct and meaningful sentence.","Drag and drop the words into the correct order, or tap them sequentially.",B.aKU,B.azH)
B.avk=s(["Step 1: Examine the provided sequence of items.","Step 2: Determine the rule governing the progression (e.g., +2, x3, alternating shapes).","Step 3: Calculate the missing value based on this rule.","Step 4: Input the correct answer to solve the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aDM=s(["Check the differences between adjacent numbers first.","If simple addition doesn't work, try multiplication or alternating patterns.","Verify your hypothesized rule against all given parts of the sequence."],t.s)
B.al8=new A.a8("Sequence Sleuth","LOGIC","Identify the underlying pattern in a sequence of numbers or symbols and determine the missing element.","Tap or enter the correct missing element to complete the sequence.",B.avk,B.aDM)
B.aTz=s(["Step 1: Watch the initial sequence of items.","Step 2: Reproduce the sequence by tapping the items.","Step 3: A new item is added to the end of the sequence.","Step 4: Reproduce the newly lengthened sequence from the beginning."],t.s)
B.aGV=s(["Group the items into small chunks (e.g., groups of 3 or 4).","Create a mnemonic or a spatial path in your mind.","Say the sequence out loud or in your head as it plays."],t.s)
B.ak0=new A.a8("Sequence Stack","MEMORY","Memorize and reproduce an ever-growing sequence of items.","Tap the items in the exact order they were shown.",B.aTz,B.aGV)
B.awz=s(["Step 1: Observe the 2D shadow cast on the wall.","Step 2: Examine the 3D objects available.","Step 3: Visualize how each object would cast a shadow from different angles.","Step 4: Select the object that matches the shadow perfectly."],t.s)
B.aKt=s(["Focus on distinct edges and asymmetric features of the shadow.","Mentally rotate the objects on the X, Y, and Z axes.","Eliminate options that have features completely missing in the shadow."],t.s)
B.akz=new A.a8("Shadow Pivot","SPATIAL","Identify the correct 3D object or orientation based on its projected 2D shadow.","Swipe to rotate the object or tap to select the matching shadow.",B.awz,B.aKt)
B.aRN=s(["Step 1: Memorize the initial shape, color, and orientation.","Step 2: Watch the sequence of transformation rules applied (e.g., rotate 90\xb0, invert color).","Step 3: Mentally apply these transformations step-by-step.","Step 4: Select the final outcome from the choices."],t.s)
B.aWP=s(["Update your mental image of the shape after every single transformation.","Pay attention to the order of operations, as it affects the final state.","Use your fingers to trace the rotation if visualization gets difficult."],t.s)
B.agn=new A.a8("Shape Shifter","SPATIAL","Track a shape as it undergoes various transformations and identify the final result.","Tap the correct final shape from the given options.",B.aRN,B.aWP)
B.aTu=s(["Step 1: Note which container holds the target object before they cover it.","Step 2: Follow that specific container with your eyes as they shuffle around.","Step 3: Do not let distractor containers break your focus.","Step 4: Tap the correct container when the shuffling stops."],t.s)
B.aNG=s(["Fixate your eyes between the target container and the center of the screen.","Avoid blinking during fast shuffles.","If tracking multiple targets, expand your visual focus rather than darting your eyes."],t.s)
B.akK=new A.a8("Shell Game","ATTENTION","Keep your eye on the container hiding the target object as they are rapidly shuffled.","Tap the container you believe holds the target object once they stop moving.",B.aTu,B.aNG)
B.aJs=s(["Step 1: Look at the numbers scattered across the grid.","Step 2: Drag to create a rectangle around a number.","Step 3: Ensure the area of the rectangle matches the number exactly.","Step 4: Fill the entire grid with non-overlapping rectangles."],t.s)
B.aSz=s(["Start with large prime numbers, as they can only form 1xN or Nx1 rectangles.","Look for numbers trapped in corners or along the edges.","Use deduction: if a cell can only be reached by one specific number, include it in that rectangle."],t.s)
B.agA=new A.a8("Shikaku","LOGIC","Divide the grid into rectangles such that each contains exactly one number, and its area equals that number.","Drag across the grid cells to draw rectangles.",B.aJs,B.aSz)
B.aJj=s(["Step 1: Analyze the presented word or list of words.","Step 2: Pronounce the words in your head to check phonetic spelling.","Step 3: Identify the letter that is written but not pronounced.","Step 4: Make your selection before the time runs out."],t.s)
B.aFU=s(["Watch out for common silent letter combinations like 'kn', 'wr', 'mb', and 'gh'.","Remember that 'e' at the end of a word is often silent and changes the vowel sound.","Sound out the word carefully to ensure every letter is accounted for."],t.s)
B.ako=new A.a8("Silent Letter Search","WORD","Identify words containing silent letters or pinpoint the specific silent letter within a word.","Tap the word with a silent letter, or tap the specific letter itself.",B.aJj,B.aFU)
B.aPB=s(["Step 1: Observe the detailed reference image carefully.","Step 2: Look at the provided silhouette options.","Step 3: Notice subtle differences in posture, edges, or negative space.","Step 4: Select the silhouette that is an exact outline of the reference."],t.s)
B.aXg=s(["Focus on the edges and negative spaces rather than the center.","Look for small, distinctive features like a raised finger, hair strand, or uneven edge.","Eliminate silhouettes that clearly lack a prominent feature of the original."],t.s)
B.ahX=new A.a8("Silhouette Match","SPATIAL","Find the exact silhouette that matches the detailed image.","Tap the correct silhouette from the available options.",B.aPB,B.aXg)
B.aL_=s(["Step 1: Examine the 3D object and the requested view direction (e.g., 'Top View').","Step 2: Mentally flatten the object along that specific axis.","Step 3: Compare your mental image to the 2D options.","Step 4: Select the correct matching projection."],t.s)
B.aT1=s(["Ignore depth entirely; imagine looking at the object from infinitely far away.","Count the number of visible blocks or segments on the outer edges.","Watch out for hidden geometry that might be blocked by foreground elements."],t.s)
B.aid=new A.a8("Ortho Silhouette","SPATIAL","Match the correct orthographic projection (top, front, side view) to the 3D object.","Tap the correct 2D projection from the choices.",B.aL_,B.aT1)
B.aW9=s(["Step 1: Read or listen to the command given on screen.","Step 2: Check if the command starts with 'Simon says'.","Step 3: If it does, perform the requested action quickly.","Step 4: If it does not, do absolutely nothing and wait."],t.s)
B.aAS=s(["Train yourself to look for the cue phrase first, before processing the action.","Keep your finger ready but resist the urge to act immediately.","Stay focused, as the pace will gradually increase."],t.s)
B.ah4=new A.a8("Simon Command","MEMORY","Follow the instructions only when preceded by 'Simon says'.","Tap the correct action button, or refrain from tapping if it's a trick.",B.aW9,B.aAS)
B.aVn=s(["Step 1: Watch the buttons flash in a specific sequence.","Step 2: Wait for the sequence to finish playing.","Step 3: Repeat the sequence by tapping the buttons in the exact same order.","Step 4: With each round, a new step is added to the sequence."],t.s)
B.ayU=s(["Use both visual and auditory memory; hum the tune while visualizing the colors.","Assign numbers or words to the colors and repeat them in your head.","Group the sequence into chunks of 3 or 4 to make it easier to remember."],t.s)
B.agw=new A.a8("Simon Sequence","MEMORY","MEMORY","Tap the colored buttons in the correct order.",B.aVn,B.ayU)
B.at3=s(["Step 1: Look at the clues on the edges of the grid indicating how many 'skyscrapers' are visible.","Step 2: Taller numbers block smaller numbers behind them.","Step 3: Fill the grid such that each row and column has numbers 1-N without repeating.","Step 4: Ensure all edge clues are satisfied by the placed heights."],t.s)
B.avd=s(["A clue of '1' means the tallest building (N) must be placed right next to it.","A clue of 'N' means the buildings must be in ascending order from that edge.","Use elimination similar to Sudoku for rows and columns."],t.s)
B.ai4=new A.a8("Skyscrapers","LOGIC","Place numbers 1 to N in the grid so no number repeats in any row or column, while satisfying the visibility clues.","Tap a cell and select a number from the dial or pad.",B.at3,B.avd)
B.aLp=s(["Step 1: Examine the scrambled grid and locate the single empty space.","Step 2: Slide tiles into the empty space to move them around.","Step 3: Try to solve the puzzle row by row, starting from the top.","Step 4: Position the final pieces in the bottom right corner to complete the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aHh=s(["Solve the top row and left column first to reduce the puzzle size.","To swap two adjacent pieces, you must rotate them in a loop with the empty space.","Plan your moves ahead to avoid messing up already solved sections."],t.s)
B.akC=new A.a8("Slide Puzzle","SPATIAL","Rearrange the scrambled tiles to form the complete picture or numerical order.","Tap or swipe a tile adjacent to the empty space to slide it.",B.aLp,B.aHh)
B.aLx=s(["Step 1: Look at the numbers inside the cells.","Step 2: The number indicates exactly how many of its 4 edges are part of the loop.","Step 3: Draw lines to satisfy all numbers.","Step 4: Ensure the lines form exactly one closed loop."],t.s)
B.aWC=s(["A '0' means no lines can surround it; mark them with 'x' to visually eliminate them.","Adjacent '3's always have parallel lines on their outer edges and a line between them.","The loop cannot branch or intersect itself, which helps logically force paths."],t.s)
B.ahe=new A.a8("Slitherlink","LOGIC","Connect adjacent dots to form a single continuous loop without crossings or branches.","Tap the edges between dots to draw or remove a line.",B.aLx,B.aWC)
B.aPX=s(["Step 1: A grid of objects is displayed.","Step 2: Tap any object you want.","Step 3: The objects shuffle their positions completely.","Step 4: Tap an object you have NOT tapped yet. Repeat until all objects are selected."],t.s)
B.aPq=s(["Pick a specific spatial order (e.g., top-left to bottom-right) or categorical order.","Memorize the items you have already clicked by creating a mental story.","Don't rely on spatial memory, as the items will shuffle every time."],t.s)
B.al6=new A.a8("Subject-Ordered Pointing","MEMORY","Select a different item on every trial until all items have been chosen once.","Tap an item from the grid.",B.aPX,B.aPq)
B.aXB=s(["Step 1: During the learning phase, observe items and note their source (e.g., red box vs blue box).","Step 2: During the testing phase, an item is presented.","Step 3: Recall the source associated with that item.","Step 4: Select the correct source to score points."],t.s)
B.aPH=s(["Create a strong associative link between the item and its source during encoding.","Pay equal attention to the context as you do to the item itself.","Use visualization to picture the item in its original context."],t.s)
B.ajy=new A.a8("Source Monitoring","MEMORY","Recall not just the information, but the exact source (who, where, or how it was presented).","Tap the correct source corresponding to the presented item.",B.aXB,B.aPH)
B.aWj=s(["Step 1: Observe the cabinet as doors open to reveal objects inside.","Step 2: Memorize which object belongs in which compartment.","Step 3: When the doors close, you will be prompted to find specific objects.","Step 4: Tap the correct compartment to reveal the requested object."],t.s)
B.aUW=s(["Group objects together by rows or columns in your mind.","Create a mental map or a story connecting adjacent items.","Focus on the general layout rather than staring at one single item."],t.s)
B.agF=new A.a8("Spatial Cabinet","MEMORY","Memorize the locations of various objects within a grid or cabinet and recall them accurately.","Tap the compartments to reveal or place objects based on your memory.",B.aWj,B.aUW)
B.aS6=s(["Step 1: An arrow will appear on the screen.","Step 2: Note the direction the arrow is pointing (Left or Right).","Step 3: Ignore which side of the screen the arrow appears on.","Step 4: Quickly tap the button matching the direction the arrow points."],t.s)
B.aKs=s(["Focus your vision on the arrowhead to quickly determine direction.","Actively suppress your urge to tap the side where the stimulus appears.","Stay calm and prioritize accuracy over extreme speed to avoid errors."],t.s)
B.aku=new A.a8("Spatial Conflict","SPATIAL","Respond to the direction of an arrow while ignoring its conflicting spatial position.","Tap the button corresponding to the arrow's direction.",B.aS6,B.aKs)
B.at9=s(["Step 1: A word flashes on the screen.","Step 2: Quickly analyze its spelling.","Step 3: Decide if it is a valid spelling or contains a typo.","Step 4: Make your choice before the timer runs out."],t.s)
B.aQH=s(["Trust your immediate visual recognition; correctly spelled words often 'look' right.","Watch out for common tricky pairs like 'ie' vs 'ei' and double consonants.","Don't overthink it, as the time limit is strict."],t.s)
B.ajs=new A.a8("Spelling Sprint","WORD","Rapidly identify whether the presented word is spelled correctly or incorrectly.","Swipe or tap the appropriate button for 'Correct' or 'Incorrect'.",B.at9,B.aQH)
B.aFf=s(["Step 1: Read the clue provided on screen.","Step 2: The answer is a pair of words that are a spoonerism of another common phrase.","Step 3: Determine the target phrase and swap the first letters/sounds.","Step 4: Input the resulting two words to solve the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aKr=s(["Sound the words out loud, as spoonerisms rely on phonetics, not just spelling.","Look for common idioms or well-known pairs as the base phrase.","Work backwards from the clue to find the modified words."],t.s)
B.aht=new A.a8("Spoonerism Solver","WORD","Swap the initial sounds of two words to solve the clue.","Type or select the correct words formed by the spoonerism.",B.aFf,B.aKr)
B.ax7=s(["Step 1: The targets are highlighted at the beginning.","Step 2: The lights go out, and all items begin to move.","Step 3: A spotlight briefly reveals their positions as they move.","Step 4: When they stop, tap on all the items that were the original targets."],t.s)
B.aPT=s(["Do not focus on a single target; keep a wide, relaxed gaze.","Use the spotlight flashes to update your mental map of the targets' trajectories.","Predict where they will be based on their speed and direction."],t.s)
B.aj2=new A.a8("Spotlight Track","ATTENTION","Keep track of multiple moving targets in the dark as they are briefly illuminated.","Tap the locations of the targets after they stop moving.",B.ax7,B.aPT)
B.axf=s(["Step 1: Watch the sequence of icons being highlighted.","Step 2: Look at the grid of icon options provided.","Step 3: Tap all the icons that were part of the highlighted sequence.","Step 4: Successfully select all correct icons to progress to a longer sequence."],t.s)
B.aBU=s(["Group icons by color or category to remember them easier.","Create a short story in your head using the icons as they appear."],t.s)
B.ajK=new A.a8("Staircase Memory","MEMORY","Memorize the sequence of highlighted icons on a grid, then correctly select those exact icons from a grid of options in any order to reconstruct the set.","Tap the icons in the bottom grid that were shown in the top sequence.",B.axf,B.aBU)
B.aPI=s(["Step 1: Memorize the set of letters displayed on the screen.","Step 2: Wait for the sequence to disappear and a single probe letter to appear.","Step 3: Recall if the probe letter was part of the original set.","Step 4: Tap YES or NO before the time runs out."],t.s)
B.aUl=s(["Say the letters out loud or silently in your head as they appear.","Group the letters into chunks or pronounceable syllables if possible."],t.s)
B.aiW=new A.a8("Sternberg Task","MEMORY","Memorize a short sequence of letters shown briefly, then determine if a single probe letter appeared in that sequence.","Tap the YES button if the probe letter was in the sequence, or the NO button if it was not.",B.aPI,B.aUl)
B.aWp=s(["Step 1: Wait for a large green arrow to appear on the screen.","Step 2: Quickly tap the corresponding left or right button.","Step 3: If the arrow suddenly turns red (the stop signal), withhold your tap and wait for the next trial.","Step 4: Maintain high accuracy and speed across multiple trials."],t.s)
B.aDH=s(["Keep your thumbs hovering near the buttons to minimize reaction time.","Don't anticipate the direction; wait for the visual cue before moving."],t.s)
B.ajI=new A.a8("Stop Signal","ATTENTION","Quickly tap the arrow button that matches the direction of the large green arrow, UNLESS the arrow turns red, in which case you must do nothing and wait.","Tap the left arrow button if the green arrow points left, or the right arrow button if it points right. Do not tap anything if the arrow is red.",B.aWp,B.aDH)
B.ay_=s(["Step 1: Read all the scattered sentence fragments carefully.","Step 2: Identify the sentence that logically starts the story and tap it.","Step 3: Find the next logical sentence that follows and tap it.","Step 4: Continue selecting sentences until the story is completely reconstructed in order."],t.s)
B.axT=s(["Look for transition words like 'First', 'Then', or 'Finally' to deduce order.","Identify cause-and-effect relationships between the sentences."],t.s)
B.akA=new A.a8("Story Builder","MEMORY","Reconstruct a scrambled story by selecting the sentences in their correct chronological order.","Tap the sentence cards in the order they should appear to build the story.",B.ay_,B.axT)
B.ayf=s(["Step 1: Look at the colored word displayed in the center of the screen.","Step 2: Ignore what the word says, and identify the actual ink color it is drawn in.","Step 3: Find the button that has the text of that ink color.","Step 4: Tap the correct button as quickly as possible before the timer runs out."],t.s)
B.aSw=s(["Try squinting your eyes slightly to blur the word and focus only on the color.","Mentally repeat the color you see before looking at the options."],t.s)
B.ahO=new A.a8("Stroop Test","ATTENTION","Identify the ink color of the text displayed, ignoring the actual word written (which may spell a conflicting color).","Tap the button containing the name of the ink color, ignoring the word itself.",B.ayf,B.aSw)
B.aXI=s(["Step 1: Scan the grid for rows, columns, or 3x3 boxes that are almost full.","Step 2: Tap an empty cell in one of those areas.","Step 3: Determine the missing number and select it from the keypad.","Step 4: Repeat this process, using logic to deduce missing numbers until the entire grid is filled correctly."],t.s)
B.azs=s(["Start with the 3x3 boxes that have the most given numbers.","Look for naked singles where only one specific number can possibly fit in a cell based on its row, column, and box."],t.s)
B.ahK=new A.a8("Sudoku","LOGIC","Fill the 9x9 grid so that every row, column, and 3x3 box contains the digits 1 through 9 exactly once without any duplicates.","Tap an empty cell on the grid to select it, then tap a number from the bottom keypad to fill it. Tap the selected cell again or the clear button to erase a number.",B.aXI,B.azs)
B.aws=s(["Step 1: Look for an empty block that has both blocks beneath it filled, or a filled block with one empty block beneath it.","Step 2: Tap the empty block to select it.","Step 3: Calculate the sum or difference and enter the number using the keypad.","Step 4: Submit your answer to check if the pyramid is correctly solved."],t.s)
B.aFc=s(["Work from the bottom up when you have adjacent base numbers.","Work top-down using subtraction when you have a top block and one of its base blocks."],t.s)
B.alf=new A.a8("Sum Pyramid","MATH","Fill in the empty blocks of the pyramid such that every block's number is the exact sum of the two blocks directly beneath it.","Tap an empty block in the pyramid to select it, then use the number pad to enter the correct value. Tap the backspace button to clear a mistake.",B.aws,B.aFc)
B.aDj=s(["Step 1: Note the target sum required at the top of the screen.",u.aq,"Step 3: Drag your finger across adjacent numbers, keeping track of the running sum.","Step 4: Release your finger once the sum of the highlighted path matches the target exactly."],t.s)
B.aWR=s(["If the target is large, look for paths containing high numbers.","If you overshoot the target, retrace your path backwards to deselect cells."],t.s)
B.aiQ=new A.a8("Sum Snake","MATH","Trace a continuous, non-overlapping path through the grid of numbers so that the sum of the numbers on the path exactly equals the target value.","Tap and drag across adjacent grid cells (horizontally, vertically, or diagonally) to draw your path. Release to submit.",B.aDj,B.aWR)
B.aHB=s(["Step 1: Read the current rule at the top of the screen (MATCH COLOR or MATCH SHAPE).","Step 2: Observe the central symbol and its properties.","Step 3: Compare it to the two options provided.","Step 4: Tap the option that matches based on the active rule before time runs out."],t.s)
B.aAg=s(["Always read the rule first before looking at the symbols, as it changes frequently.","Verbally repeat the rule to yourself to maintain focus."],t.s)
B.ajj=new A.a8("Switch Task","ATTENTION","Match the central symbol to one of the options based on the current active rule (either matching by COLOR or matching by SHAPE), which changes dynamically.","Tap the option button (left or right) that matches the central symbol according to the current rule displayed at the top.",B.aHB,B.aAg)
B.aPK=s(["Step 1: Look at the available syllables scattered on the screen.","Step 2: Try to identify familiar word beginnings or endings.","Step 3: Tap the syllables in order to construct a word in the active slots.","Step 4: Once a valid word is formed, it will lock in; continue until all syllables are used."],t.s)
B.aBY=s(["Look for common prefixes (like 're-' or 'un-') or suffixes (like '-tion' or '-ing').","Sound out combinations in your head before selecting them."],t.s)
B.aie=new A.a8("Syllable Stack","WORD","Combine the scattered syllables in the correct order to form complete, valid words.","Tap the syllable blocks in the correct sequence to build a word. Tap the undo button to remove the last selected syllable.",B.aPK,B.aBY)
B.azl=s(["Step 1: Study the association key showing which symbol equals which digit.","Step 2: Tap Start Translating to hide the key and begin the test.","Step 3: Look at the challenge symbols provided.","Step 4: Use the keypad to enter the correct digit for each symbol from memory and submit."],t.s)
B.aNH=s(["Create visual stories linking the shape of the symbol to the number.","Focus on memorizing 3 or 4 pairs at a time rather than all 9 at once."],t.s)
B.ais=new A.a8("Symbol Digit Assoc","MEMORY","Memorize the association between 9 unique symbols and the digits 1-9, then correctly translate a sequence of challenge symbols into their corresponding digits using a keypad.","During the recall phase, tap a symbol box to select it, then tap the number pad to input the corresponding digit. Tap the clear button to erase an entry, and submit when finished.",B.azl,B.aNH)
B.aKw=s(["Step 1: A row of five symbols will appear on the screen.","Step 2: Focus entirely on the center symbol, ignoring the two on the left and two on the right.","Step 3: Identify the center symbol.","Step 4: Quickly tap the matching symbol button at the bottom of the screen."],t.s)
B.aPD=s(["Try to fix your gaze on the exact center of the screen before the symbols appear.","Consciously force yourself to ignore the outer edges of the symbol row."],t.s)
B.akN=new A.a8("Symbolic Flanker","ATTENTION","Identify the center symbol in a row of five symbols, ignoring the flanking symbols on either side, which may be the same or different.","Tap the button corresponding to the center symbol.",B.aKw,B.aPD)
B.aK_=s(["Step 1: Look at the first equation to determine the value of the first symbol (e.g., A + A = X).","Step 2: Use that value in the next equation to solve for the second symbol.","Step 3: Continue substituting known values to find the value of all symbols.","Step 4: Calculate the sum of the symbols in the final equation and enter the answer."],t.s)
B.aA2=s(["Always start with the equation that has two identical symbols.","Write down the values of the symbols if you have trouble keeping them in memory."],t.s)
B.ahq=new A.a8("Symbol Logic","LOGIC","Deduce the numerical value of different symbols based on a series of visual equations, then calculate and input the answer for the final question.","Use the number pad to type your answer for the final equation. Tap the clear button to erase, and the checkmark button to submit your guess.",B.aK_,B.aA2)
B.aBk=s(["Step 1: Observe the pattern of filled cells on the left side of the grid.","Step 2: Imagine a vertical mirror line down the center of the grid.","Step 3: Tap the cells on the right side to fill them in the mirrored positions.","Step 4: Ensure the right side is an exact reflection of the left side to complete the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aym=s(["Work column by column, starting from the center mirror line and moving outwards.","Count the empty spaces from the center line to accurately place mirrored cells."],t.s)
B.ak8=new A.a8("Symmetry","SPATIAL","Complete the symmetrical pattern by toggling cells on the right half of the grid so that it perfectly mirrors the pre-filled left half.","Tap or drag across the empty cells on the right side of the grid to toggle them on or off to match the reflection.",B.aBk,B.aym)
B.aTG=s(["Step 1: Memorize the position of the red cell on the grid.","Step 2: Judge whether the next displayed matrix is symmetrical by tapping YES or NO.","Step 3: Memorize the next red cell position.","Step 4: Once the recall phase begins, tap the grid cells in the exact sequence the red cells appeared."],t.s)
B.auW=s(["Try to visualize a line connecting the red cells to remember their sequence as a path.","Focus on accuracy during the symmetry judgment, but don't let it distract you from repeating the sequence in your head."],t.s)
B.alp=new A.a8("Symmetry Span","MEMORY","Alternate between judging whether patterns are symmetrical and memorizing the location of red cells in a 4x4 grid, then recall the entire sequence of red cell locations in order.","Tap YES or NO to judge symmetry. During recall, tap the cells on the 4x4 grid in the exact order the red cells appeared.",B.aTG,B.auW)
B.axP=s(["Step 1: Look at the tangled web of nodes and intersecting lines.","Step 2: Identify lines that are crossing (highlighted in red).","Step 3: Drag the nodes connected to those lines to new positions.","Step 4: Continue repositioning nodes until all lines are clear and no longer intersect (turn green)."],t.s)
B.aFa=s(["Try pulling nodes that have many connections towards the center, and nodes with few connections to the outside.","Look for triangles or loops of connected nodes and untangle them as a group."],t.s)
B.aiF=new A.a8("Tangle Fix","LOGIC","Untangle the graph by moving the nodes so that none of the connecting lines cross each other.","Tap and hold a node, then drag it around the screen to reposition it and untangle the connected lines.",B.axP,B.aFa)
B.aOf=s(["Step 1: Observe the target outline on the main grid.","Step 2: Tap a piece in the dock to select it.","Step 3: Double-tap the piece if you need to rotate it to fit.","Step 4: Tap on the grid to place the piece, and repeat until the target shape is perfectly filled."],t.s)
B.aDE=s(["Start by placing the largest pieces or those with unique shapes that only fit in specific corners.","If you get stuck, remove pieces and try a different rotation for the first piece."],t.s)
B.agY=new A.a8("Tangram","SPATIAL","Completely fill the target outline on the grid by placing and rotating all the provided tangram pieces without any overlap.","Tap a piece in the dock to select it, double-tap to rotate it, and tap a cell on the grid to place the piece's pivot point.",B.aOf,B.aDE)
B.aV0=s(["Step 1: Look at the numbers available on the 5x5 grid.","Step 2: Tap a number to start your selection.","Step 3: Tap additional numbers, keeping an eye on the Selection Sum indicator.","Step 4: Select a combination that adds up to exactly 10 to clear those tiles and score points."],t.s)
B.auL=s(["Look for obvious pairs that make 10, like 9+1 or 8+2.","You can use three or more numbers (e.g., 5+3+2) if simple pairs are not available."],t.s)
B.ahv=new A.a8("Target 10","MATH","Select a combination of number tiles from the 5x5 grid whose sum equals exactly 10.","Tap the tiles on the grid to select or deselect them and add their values to your current selection sum.",B.aV0,B.auL)
B.azq=s(["Step 1: Note the target number at the top of the screen.","Step 2: Look at the available number tiles.","Step 3: Tap numbers and operators to construct a mathematical equation.","Step 4: Use all the numbers to reach the exact target value to win the round."],t.s)
B.awH=s(["Think backwards from the target number to see if a multiplication or division step can get you close.","Use brackets to control the order of operations when adding or subtracting before multiplying."],t.s)
B.aje=new A.a8("Target Number","MATH","Use the provided numbers and mathematical operators to construct an expression that evaluates exactly to the target number.","Tap the number tiles and operator buttons to build your expression. Tap the undo button to remove the last input, or refresh to clear entirely.",B.azq,B.awH)
B.aUQ=s(["Step 1: Watch carefully as a series of icons is shown one at a time.","Step 2: Read the query to see if you need to identify the EARLIER or LATER item.","Step 3: Look at the two icon options provided.","Step 4: Tap the icon that correctly matches the temporal order requested."],t.s)
B.aIG=s(["Create a story linking the icons together in the order they appear to solidify the sequence in your memory.","Mentally recite the list of items each time a new one is added."],t.s)
B.ajE=new A.a8("Temporal Order","MEMORY","Memorize a sequence of icons presented one by one, then answer queries about which of two given icons appeared earlier or later in the sequence.","Tap the button corresponding to the icon that answers the query.",B.aUQ,B.aIG)
B.at4=s(["Step 1: Tap an empty cell in the grid.","Step 2: Look at the column sum target and the other numbers in that column.","Step 3: Select a digit from the keypad that helps reach the sum without duplicating a number in the row or placing it next to an identical number.","Step 4: Fill the entire grid following all rules to win."],t.s)
B.aQP=s(["Start with columns that have high or low target sums, as they have fewer possible combinations.","Pay close attention to the rule that same numbers cannot touch diagonally."],t.s)
B.agS=new A.a8("Tenner Grid","LOGIC","Fill the grid so that each row contains the digits 0-9 exactly once, each column's sum matches the target number below it, and no adjacent cells (even diagonally) contain the same digit.","Tap an empty cell on the grid to select it, then tap a number from the keypad below to fill it in.",B.at4,B.aQP)
B.avT=s(["Step 1: Read one row's clue as four digits in alphabet order. On a five-cell row, `2111` means two As, one B, one C and one D.","Step 2: When a clue digit is met, that letter cannot appear again in the line. When the cells left in a line equal the counts still owed, those cells are fixed.","Step 3: Two identical letters may not share an edge, so a letter in a cell rules itself out of the cells above, below, left and right.","Step 4: Work the tightest line first: a line with a 0 or a line whose counts are almost used up is where the next certain letter is.","Step 5: The grid is finished when every cell holds a letter and every clue digit is met; a letter touching its twin is shown in red."],t.s)
B.aAR=s(["A row whose clue has a 0 removes that letter from the whole row at once.","If a letter's count in a line equals the number of free cells, every free cell of that line is that letter.","Alternate thinking: a run of cells that can hold a letter at most every other cell bounds that letter's count. When the bound equals the clue, the alternation is forced.","Column and row clues cross, so a letter forced in a row very often fixes a cell in a column too. Sweep both directions each time you place one."],t.s)
B.ajh=new A.a8("ABCD","LOGIC","Write one letter in every cell so that each row and column holds exactly the number of each letter printed beside it, and no two identical letters touch along an edge.","Tap a cell to cycle its letter: empty, then A, B, C, D, and back to empty. The hint button fills one cell the counts prove.",B.avT,B.aAR)
B.aSQ=s(["Step 1: Read the numbers along the top and the left. A 0 empties that whole row or column, so tap every cell in it to water.","Step 2: Mark boat cells with the longest boat first. A run of four needs four cells in a line, so a line that cannot hold four anywhere is not part of it.","Step 3: Once a row or column has all the boat cells its count asks for, tap the rest of that line to water.","Step 4: Two boat cells that touch at a corner are a mistake even when both runs have the right length. Water one of them.","Step 5: The strip under the board crosses a boat off when you have marked a complete one. The board is finished when every boat is crossed off and the counts are met."],t.s)
B.aS8=s(["Whenever a cell has boat cells on both a row neighbour and a column neighbour, it cannot be a boat: a boat is a straight run, so it would have to bend.","A boat cell rules out all four cells diagonally beside it, not just the four it touches.","If a line's count is only just satisfied by the cells still open, every one of them is a boat.","Count the fleet, not just the lines: when the remaining lengths cannot fit in a gap, that gap is water."],t.s)
B.aiv=new A.a8("Boats","LOGIC","Place the whole fleet: every boat is a straight run of boat cells, no two boats touch even at a corner, and the counts outside the grid say how many boat cells each row and column holds.","Tap a cell to cycle it through boat cell, water, and untouched. No dragging is needed.",B.aSQ,B.aS8)
B.aU9=s(["Step 1: Find the 1. The cell that holds it touches the 2, so an isolated corner with one way in usually fixes its neighbour.","Step 2: Work from both ends. The lowest and highest printed numbers fix their own neighbours, and the walk closes in from the middle.","Step 3: A number only ever moves one cell, so a cell with eight neighbours can hold anything, and a corner cell can only hold numbers whose neighbours are near.","Step 4: When a printed number has only one free cell beside it, the number after it goes there. Write it; that closes one more door.","Step 5: The board is finished when every number is on it and every step touches the step before. A number out of reach shows in red."],t.s)
B.aDZ=s(["Count room, not hope: if the next number has nowhere to go from a cell, that cell cannot hold this one.","A cell that touches only one empty cell is the end of the path from that side, which pins both of its neighbours.","Long printed runs already laid out are free deductions: every gap between two printed numbers is a mini path with fixed ends.","When the grid fills up, the last few numbers place themselves: the cells left are the numbers left, in order."],t.s)
B.ajL=new A.a8("Number Path","LOGIC","Place 1 to the last number on the grid, once each, so that every number touches the one before it and the one after it, along an edge or a corner.","Tap an empty cell to write the next number. Tap a number you wrote to clear it. The hint button writes one number the printed clues prove.",B.aU9,B.aDZ)
B.aEo=s(["Step 1: Read a dot as a small puzzle of its own. The dot already shows the colour of its cell, so that cell is done, and exactly one of its neighbours shares it.","Step 2: A corner cell without a dot has only two neighbours, so both of them must be its colour. That is the strongest start on the board.","Step 3: Count neighbours, not patterns. A cell needs two of its colour, so when one neighbour is the other colour and one is empty, the empty one is decided.","Step 4: A dotted cell with no same-coloured neighbour yet needs its one from the cells still open. When only one is open, that one takes the colour.","Step 5: The board is finished when every cell is coloured, every dot has exactly one neighbour of its colour, and every plain cell has two. A cell that cannot reach its count shows in red."],t.s)
B.aTb=s(["Work from the corners inward: a corner without a dot forces both of its neighbours, which then forces the next ring.","A dot with one neighbour already its colour rules out that colour for every other neighbour, which is often the fastest way to place an edge.","Two colours are symmetrical, so a mistake is not local: a cell that cannot reach two neighbours of its colour usually means the cell two steps away is wrong.","An edge cell has three neighbours, so it needs two of its own colour: one of the three is the odd one out, and the dot tells you which."],t.s)
B.ajG=new A.a8("Clusters","LOGIC","Colour every cell one of two colours, so that a dotted cell has exactly one neighbour of its colour and a cell without a dot has at least two.","Tap a cell to cycle it: empty, then one colour, then the other, then empty again. A dotted cell is fixed and does not change.",B.aEo,B.aTb)
B.aNa=s(["Step 1: Look at the shapes, not at the numbers. A shape with four cells holds 1, 2, 3 and 4 exactly once.","Step 2: Read the ripple rule as a no-entry zone as wide as the number: a 1 keeps another 1 out of the four cells beside it, a 3 keeps another 3 out of the three cells either side, because two 3s need three cells between them.","Step 3: Count the room a number needs, not just the cells next to it. On a line of six cells a 3 in the second cell can only meet another 3 in the last, because it needs three cells of gap.","Step 4: When a shape has only one cell left that can hold a number, that cell is it. Write it and the ripple clears its neighbours.","Step 5: The board is finished when every cell holds a number and no digit sits too close to its twin. A number that breaks the ripple shows in red."],t.s)
B.aAa=s(["A 1 is the most useful clue on the board: it rules out its four orthogonal neighbours everywhere, and a shape of size one is simply that number.","Count the room a digit has along a line, not just beside it: two equal digits need one more cell of gap than the digit itself, so a 2 needs two cells between it and its twin and a 4 needs four.","Cross off by shape and by line at once: a digit placed in a shape is gone from that shape everywhere, even in cells far away.","The largest region's size is the highest digit on the board. Nothing above it exists, so a cell in a smaller shape can never take it."],t.s)
B.ajv=new A.a8("Ripple Effect","LOGIC","Fill every shape with the numbers 1 to its size, once each, so that two equal numbers in a line have at least that many cells between them.","Tap a cell to select it, then tap a number to write it. Tap the same number again, or the eraser, to clear the cell. The hint button writes one number the clues prove.",B.aNa,B.aAa)
B.at_=s(["Step 1: The board is a Latin square before it is arithmetic. A number written in a cell is gone from the rest of its row and its column, and that alone fills a lot of a five by five.","Step 2: Read a corner clue as two separate questions. A +7 between four cells says the top left and the bottom right add to seven AND the top right and the bottom left add to seven. Either one failing breaks the clue.","Step 3: Use the small numbers first. A \xd72 forces a 1 and a 2, a \u22121 forces two neighbours, and an E or an O decides the parity of four cells at once.","Step 4: When a row has only one cell left for a number, that cell is it, even if you have not looked at the corners yet.","Step 5: The board is finished when every row and column holds each number once and no corner is red. A number that repeats or a corner that fails shows in red."],t.s)
B.ax6=s(["Count the parity first: an E corner needs four even numbers, and on a five board that is 2 and 4 with one of them twice, so the corner immediately says which cells cannot hold 1, 3 or 5.","For a product clue, list the pairs that multiply to it before touching the board. A \xd712 on a six board is 2 and 6 or 3 and 4, and which pair it is usually falls out of the row.","A \xd7 with the biggest number is the strongest clue on the board: it pairs the largest digit with a 1 or a 2, and there are very few places for either.","Division is the weakest of the four operations: a \xf72 means one number is twice the other, which is 1 and 2, 2 and 4, or 3 and 6 on a six board. List the pairs before you eliminate anything, and prefer a product clue when both are on the same corner.","Work from the corners inward. The four corner cells of the grid touch only one clue each, so they have the least to satisfy, and they feed the row and column rules for everything else."],t.s)
B.agH=new A.a8("Mathrax","LOGIC","Fill every row and column with the numbers 1 to the side of the board, once each. The clue on each corner binds the four cells around it along both diagonals: E means all four are even, O means all odd, = means each diagonal pair is equal, and a number is the result of its operation on each diagonal pair.","Tap a cell to write the next number, and keep tapping to cycle back to empty. The hint button writes one number the clues prove.",B.at_,B.ax6)
B.aH6=s(["Step 1: Look at the row and column clues indicating how many tents belong in each line.","Step 2: Find trees and tap adjacent empty cells to place tents next to them.","Step 3: Ensure no two tents touch each other, even diagonally.","Step 4: Complete the grid so all trees have a tent and all clues are satisfied."],t.s)
B.aED=s(["Fill rows or columns with a '0' clue entirely with grass.","If a tree only has one valid empty space next to it, a tent must go there."],t.s)
B.ajF=new A.a8("Tents And Trees","LOGIC","Place tents in the grid so that every tree is paired with exactly one adjacent tent, no two tents touch each other (even diagonally), and the tent counts match the row and column clues.","Tap an empty cell to place a tent, tap again to cycle to grass (empty), or tap again to clear.",B.aH6,B.aED)
B.aTX=s(["Step 1: Look at the two shapes or characters presented on the screen.","Step 2: Count the number of holes (closed loops) in each shape.","Step 3: Consider the number of endpoints or intersections.","Step 4: Tap YES if they have the same topological properties, or NO if they differ."],t.s)
B.avZ=s(["The most important feature is the number of holes; an 'O' and a 'D' are equivalent (1 hole), but an 'O' and an '8' are not (1 vs 2 holes).","Imagine the shape is made of rubber and see if you can bend one into the other."],t.s)
B.ahs=new A.a8("Topology","SPATIAL","Determine if two displayed characters or shapes are topologically equivalent, meaning one can be stretched or deformed into the other without tearing or merging holes.","Tap the YES button if they are topologically equivalent, or the NO button if they are not.",B.aTX,B.avZ)
B.aL5=s(["Step 1: Compare the current layout of beads on the bottom pegs to the target configuration on the top pegs.","Step 2: Tap the peg holding the bead you want to move.","Step 3: Tap the destination peg to drop the bead, keeping in mind that the pegs can only hold 3, 2, and 1 beads respectively.","Step 4: Match the target configuration before running out of allowed moves."],t.s)
B.aBp=s(["Plan your moves backwards from the target configuration to figure out which bead needs to be placed first.","Use the smallest peg (capacity 1) as a temporary holding spot to access beads underneath."],t.s)
B.ajN=new A.a8("Tower Of London","LOGIC","Move the colored beads between the three pegs to match the target configuration in the minimum number of moves, adhering to the height capacity of each peg.","Tap a peg to select the top bead, then tap another peg to move the bead there.",B.aL5,B.aBp)
B.aTs=s(["Step 1: Locate the starting marker of the target path.","Step 2: Press and hold your finger on the start marker.","Step 3: Drag your finger along the curve of the path, trying to stay exactly on the line.","Step 4: Release your finger when you reach the end marker to get your accuracy score."],t.s)
B.ax8=s(["Move at a steady, moderate pace; moving too fast reduces accuracy, but moving too slow makes it hard to draw smooth curves.","Look slightly ahead of your finger to anticipate the curves."],t.s)
B.akS=new A.a8("Trace Path","SPATIAL","Carefully trace the drawn path from the start point to the end point, staying as close to the line as possible to achieve high accuracy.","Tap and hold on the starting marker, then drag your finger along the path to the ending marker.",B.aTs,B.ax8)
B.aNU=s(["Step 1: Find the first circle in the sequence and tap it.","Step 2: Quickly scan the screen for the next logical item in the sequence.","Step 3: Tap the next circle to connect them.","Step 4: Continue connecting the circles in the correct order until the trail is complete."],t.s)
B.aMa=s(["While moving your finger to the next circle, actively scan the rest of the screen for the one after that.","Keep your finger close to the screen to minimize travel time."],t.s)
B.agx=new A.a8("Trail Making","ATTENTION","Connect the numbered or lettered circles in the correct sequential order as quickly as possible.","Tap the circles in the correct sequence.",B.aNU,B.aMa)
B.aCa=s(["Step 1: Select a shape from the tool menu below the grid.","Step 2: Tap an empty cell to place the selected shape.","Step 3: Use logic to ensure no three identical shapes are adjacent vertically or horizontally.","Step 4: Ensure every row and column contains exactly two of each shape to complete the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aUf=s(["If you see two identical shapes next to each other, the spaces on either side MUST be different shapes.","If a row already has two of a certain shape, fill the remaining empty cells with the other shapes."],t.s)
B.ahN=new A.a8("Triplets Logic","LOGIC","Fill a 6x6 grid with three types of shapes so that every row and column has exactly two of each shape, and no three identical shapes appear consecutively in any row or column.","Tap a shape tool to select it, then tap an empty cell on the grid to paint that shape. Tap a filled cell with the same tool to clear it.",B.aCa,B.aUf)
B.ayH=s(["Step 1: Read the target phrase displayed in the center of the screen.","Step 2: Tap the text input field to bring up the keyboard.","Step 3: Type the phrase exactly as shown, paying attention to matching characters.","Step 4: Complete the phrase before the timer expires to see your WPM score."],t.s)
B.atI=s(["Focus on accuracy first; fixing mistakes takes more time than typing slightly slower but correctly.","Try to read a few words ahead of what you are currently typing."],t.s)
B.aiZ=new A.a8("Typing Speed","WORD","Type the displayed phrase exactly as it appears as quickly and accurately as possible to test your Words Per Minute (WPM).","Use the on-screen keyboard to type the target phrase into the text field.",B.ayH,B.atI)
B.aGs=s(["Step 1: A word is displayed with scrambled inner letters (e.g. 'Tpyolgcyemia').","Step 2: Look at the first and last letters to grasp the word skeleton.","Step 3: Decipher the original word structure.","Step 4: Type or select the correct word to proceed."],t.s)
B.aDG=s(["Read the word as a single entity rather than analyzing individual letter positions.","Focus on context if the word is part of a full sentence.","Your brain naturally recognizes words if the outer boundaries are correctly placed."],t.s)
B.akE=new A.a8("Typoglycemia","WORD","Decipher and read words whose inner letters are scrambled, keeping only the first and last letters correct.","Type the correct unscrambled word or select it from multiple choices.",B.aGs,B.aDG)
B.aWV=s(["Step 1: Note the starting value, its unit, and the target unit of measurement.","Step 2: Calculate the converted value using the appropriate conversion multiplier or formula.","Step 3: Input the calculated target value on the numpad.","Step 4: Submit to verify your answer."],t.s)
B.aMk=s(["Memorize basic conversion benchmarks (e.g. 1 inch = 2.54 cm, 0\xb0C = 32\xb0F).","Estimate calculations if exact values are complex.","Pay attention to units to avoid division vs multiplication swaps."],t.s)
B.ait=new A.a8("Unit Converter Pro","MATH","Convert values between different units of measurement (e.g. Celsius to Fahrenheit, meters to feet).","Enter the converted value on the number pad and submit.",B.aWV,B.aMk)
B.aHH=s(["Step 1: Observe the target direction or pattern required.","Step 2: Select individual vectors that are misaligned.","Step 3: Rotate them until they match the target direction flow.","Step 4: Correct all vectors to complete the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aE3=s(["Start by aligning vectors adjacent to the boundaries.","Look for group rotations if available.","Check the flow field overall to catch single misalignments."],t.s)
B.ajM=new A.a8("Vector Grid Alignment","SPATIAL","Align the vectors on the grid to point in the same direction or create a specific vector flow field.","Tap or drag vectors to rotate and change their direction.",B.aHH,B.aE3)
B.aOa=s(["Step 1: Note the mathematical vector equation (e.g. A + B or 2A).","Step 2: Add or multiply components of the starting vectors.","Step 3: Drag the result vector head to the correct calculated coordinate.","Step 4: Submit to confirm alignment."],t.s)
B.aua=s(["Calculate components individually (X component first, then Y).","For vector addition, imagine stacking arrows tip-to-tail.","Double check negative component coordinates carefully."],t.s)
B.alo=new A.a8("Vector Vektor","MATH","Perform vector operations (addition, subtraction, scaling) on the coordinate plane.","Drag the vector arrow ends to match the resulting calculated vector.",B.aOa,B.aua)
B.aVA=s(["Step 1: Read the property tags for each circle (e.g. 'Prime', 'Even', 'Multiple of 3').","Step 2: Analyze the properties of the given number token.","Step 3: Drag the number into the intersection where it satisfies all matching circle properties.","Step 4: Place all numbers correctly to win."],t.s)
B.aXm=s(["Check if the number fits none of the categories and belongs on the outer boundary.","Take your time validating overlapping circle criteria.","Find numbers that fit the central intersection of all circles first."],t.s)
B.ahY=new A.a8("Venn Numbers","LOGIC","Place numbers into the correct intersections of a Venn diagram according to numerical properties.","Drag and drop the number tokens into the Venn diagram sections.",B.aVA,B.aXm)
B.aBs=s(["Step 1: Read the starting analogy relationship (A is to B).","Step 2: Identify the logic of the relationship (e.g. opposites, synonyms, tool/user).","Step 3: Apply the same logic to the target word (C is to ...).","Step 4: Tap the word option that fits this logic."],t.s)
B.avP=s(["Define the exact relationship between the first pair of words in a simple sentence.","Ensure the word order matches (e.g. if A is the action and B is the noun, C must be action and D must be noun).","Eliminate options that belong to unrelated word groups."],t.s)
B.ajA=new A.a8("Verbal Analogies","WORD","Complete the word relationship analogy (e.g. Hot is to Cold as Up is to ...).","Tap the correct word option to complete the analogy.",B.aBs,B.avP)
B.aCG=s(["Step 1: Observe the frequent distractor signals flashing.","Step 2: Maintain focus and ignore distractor variations.","Step 3: React immediately when the specific rare target signal is shown.","Step 4: Continue monitoring for the duration of the task."],t.s)
B.aGX=s(["Keep a steady breathing rhythm to avoid fatigue.","Do not tap reactively to every flash; wait to confirm the target shape/color.","Maintain strict visual focus on the stimulus zone."],t.s)
B.al7=new A.a8("Vigilance Task","ATTENTION","Maintain attention over a long duration and react only to rare target signals while ignoring frequent distractors.","Tap the screen only when the rare target signal appears.",B.aCG,B.aGX)
B.aRD=s(["Step 1: Read the target description or symbol layout to look for.","Step 2: Scan the grid of distractors rapidly.","Step 3: Locate the unique target item.","Step 4: Tap it to score and advance."],t.s)
B.ay2=s(["Scan in a systematic grid path (e.g. left-to-right rows) instead of random looking.","Look for features that stand out (such as line orientation or color).","If the target has a distinct feature, look for that specific difference."],t.s)
B.ahU=new A.a8("Visual Search","ATTENTION","Find the unique target symbol among a dense array of similar distractors.","Tap the target symbol in the grid.",B.aRD,B.ay2)
B.aTD=s(["Step 1: Watch the stream of shapes appear sequentially on screen.","Step 2: Inner-logical shapes always appear together in pairs or triplets.","Step 3: During the test phase, select which pair of shapes felt more familiar.","Step 4: Submit your familiarity choices."],t.s)
B.aHb=s(["Let your brain pick up the sequences passively without overanalyzing individual items.","Trust your gut feeling of familiarity during testing.","Observe shape transition flows closely."],t.s)
B.ahP=new A.a8("Visual Statistical Learning","MEMORY","Identify patterns and statistical pairings in a stream of visual shapes.","Tap the options that represent matching sequences or pairs that appeared together.",B.aTD,B.aHb)
B.atn=s(["Step 1: Read the target word and the requested relation (synonym or antonym).","Step 2: Analyze the meanings of the multiple choice options.","Step 3: Select the word that correctly matches the relation.","Step 4: Submit to advance."],t.s)
B.ayw=s(["Eliminate options that have matching parts of speech but unrelated definitions.","Think of the target word in a sentence to recall its context.","Prefixes and suffixes can give clues to overall positive or negative word meanings."],t.s)
B.ai_=new A.a8("Vocabulary Builder","WORD","Select the correct synonym or antonym for the given vocabulary word.","Tap the correct word option from the list.",B.atn,B.ayw)
B.aEq=s(["Step 1: Note the category clue at the top.","Step 2: Examine the consonants and empty spaces.","Step 3: Deduce the word that fits the consonants and category.","Step 4: Submit to verify."],t.s)
B.aH0=s(["Think of words in the given category that start with the first consonant.","Place common vowel pairings (like 'ou', 'ee', 'ea') in the blanks to test them.","Say the consonant skeleton out loud to hear potential word fits."],t.s)
B.aj7=new A.a8("Vowel Reconstruct","WORD","Fill in the missing vowels of a word based on the remaining consonants and a semantic category.","Tap the vowels in the correct sequence to complete the word.",B.aEq,B.aH0)
B.aNN=s(["Step 1: Look at the mixed color layers in the tubes.","Step 2: Tap a tube with the top color you want to pour.","Step 3: Tap a destination tube that is either empty or has the same matching top color layer.","Step 4: Continue sorting until all colors are separated into individual tubes."],t.s)
B.aA4=s(["Keep at least one tube empty as a temporary transition space.","Solve tubes containing colors that are already near the top first.","Plan your moves ahead to avoid locking yourself out of empty slots."],t.s)
B.aiB=new A.a8("Water Sort","LOGIC","Sort the colored water in the test tubes until each tube contains only one color.","Tap a tube to select it, then tap another tube to pour the top layer of water.",B.aNN,B.aA4)
B.aDm=s(["Step 1: Look at the card to be sorted at the bottom.","Step 2: Place it on one of the four reference piles.","Step 3: Receive correctness feedback. Use this to identify if the current sorting rule is shape, color, or number.","Step 4: Adapt your sorting to follow this rule until it changes again."],t.s)
B.awl=s(["Do not panic when a correct rule starts returning 'Incorrect' - it means the rule has shifted.","Always test rules systematically: color first, then shape, then number.","Remember the last correct rule to avoid repeating it immediately after a shift."],t.s)
B.ajH=new A.a8("Wisconsin Card Sorting","LOGIC","Deduce the hidden rule for sorting cards (by color, shape, or number) based on correctness feedback, and adapt when the rule changes.","Tap one of the four piles to place your card.",B.aDm,B.awl)
B.aMz=s(["Step 1: In the study phase, look at the two words presented side-by-side and memorize their pairing.","Step 2: Tap 'NEXT PAIR' to view the next set, until you finish all 5 pairs and tap 'START RECALL'.","Step 3: In the recall phase, a target word is shown. Select the word that was paired with it from the multiple choices.","Step 4: Correctly identify all 5 pairings to win the game. If you make a mistake, you must restart the study phase."],t.s)
B.aOm=s(["Create a vivid, bizarre mental image combining the two words (e.g., for 'Apple - Ocean', imagine a giant apple floating in the sea).","Say the pair aloud as you study them to reinforce memory through auditory learning."],t.s)
B.akG=new A.a8("Word Association Recall","MEMORY","The objective is to memorize pairs of associated words and later correctly recall which word was paired with a given target word.","In the study phase, tap 'NEXT PAIR' or 'START RECALL' to proceed. In the recall phase, tap the correct word from the multiple-choice list.",B.aMz,B.aOm)
B.aTl=s(["Step 1: Scan the 16 scrambled words in the grid to find potential connections or themes.","Step 2: Tap on exactly 4 words that you believe belong to the same category.","Step 3: Tap the 'Submit Group' button that appears at the bottom.","Step 4: If correct, the category is solved and removed from the grid. If incorrect, you lose a try. Solve all 4 categories before running out of tries to win."],t.s)
B.aTO=s(["Don't submit immediately if you see a connection; make sure there aren't 5 or 6 words that fit the category, which means you need to solve another overlapping category first.","If you're stuck, try finding the most unique or specific word on the board and figure out what it must connect to."],t.s)
B.akt=new A.a8("Word Grid Connection","WORD","The objective is to group a 16-word grid into four categories of four related words each, within a limited number of tries.","Tap to select or deselect exactly 4 words from the grid. Once 4 are selected, tap the 'Submit Group' button that appears at the bottom.",B.aTl,B.aTO)
B.aRQ=s(["Step 1: Look at the START word and END word displayed at the top.","Step 2: Use the keyboard to enter a new valid word that differs from the current bottom word of the ladder by exactly one letter.","Step 3: Tap ENTER to submit the word. If valid, it is added to the ladder.","Step 4: Continue chaining words until you successfully enter the END word to complete the ladder."],t.s)
B.atP=s(["Work backward from the END word in your mind to see what words can connect to it.","Change vowels first if you are stuck, as they offer the most flexibility for forming new words."],t.s)
B.akL=new A.a8("Word Ladder","WORD","The objective is to transform the start word into the end word by changing only one letter at a time, where each intermediate step must be a valid word.","Use the on-screen keyboard to type a word that changes exactly one letter from the previous word. Press ENTER to submit or DEL to correct mistakes.",B.aRQ,B.atP)
B.aV3=s(["Step 1: Enter a 4-letter starting word using the keyboard and press ENTER.","Step 2: Review the feedback provided next to your guess: 'B' indicates a Bull (correct letter in the correct position), and 'C' indicates a Cow (correct letter but in the wrong position).","Step 3: Use this logic to refine your next guess.","Step 4: Keep guessing until you get 4 Bulls, revealing the target word before you run out of attempts."],t.s)
B.aXD=s(["Use a starting word with 4 unique common letters (like 'TEAR' or 'LION') to maximize initial information.","If you get a 'Cow', try moving that letter to a different position in your next guess."],t.s)
B.akg=new A.a8("Word Mastermind","WORD","The objective is to guess the hidden 4-letter target word by entering guesses and using the Bulls (B) and Cows (C) feedback.","Use the on-screen keyboard to type a 4-letter guess and press ENTER to submit.",B.aV3,B.aXD)
B.aVf=s(["Step 1: Look at the scrambled letters displayed at the top of the screen.","Step 2: Mentally rearrange the letters to figure out the original word.","Step 3: Tap the letter buttons one by one to spell out your guess in the input boxes.","Step 4: Tap the SUBMIT button to check your guess. If correct, you win!"],t.s)
B.aBT=s(["Look for common prefixes (like 're-', 'un-') or suffixes (like '-ing', '-ed', '-tion') among the letters.","Try mentally pairing consonants and vowels that often go together (e.g., 'th', 'ch', 'ea')."],t.s)
B.agR=new A.a8("Word Scramble","WORD","The objective is to unscramble the letters to find the correct target word.","Tap the scrambled letter buttons to spell the word. Use the backspace button to correct mistakes, the refresh button to clear, and SUBMIT to check your answer.",B.aVf,B.aBT)
B.aTi=s(["Step 1: Review the 'WORDS TO FIND' list at the bottom of the screen.","Step 2: Scan the letter grid above to locate the first letter of one of the words.","Step 3: Once found, press and drag your finger from the first letter to the last letter of the word, then release.","Step 4: Find and highlight all the words in the list to complete the puzzle."],t.s)
B.aT8=s(["Search for the least common letters in a word (like Q, X, Z, K, or V) rather than starting with the first letter.","Scan row by row or column by column systematically if you're stuck."],t.s)
B.ahT=new A.a8("Word Search","WORD","The objective is to find all the listed words hidden within the grid of letters.","Drag your finger across the letters in the grid (horizontally, vertically, or diagonally) to highlight and select a word.",B.aTi,B.aT8)
B.au_=s(["Step 1: Read the TARGET WORD displayed at the top of the screen.","Step 2: Locate the starting letter of the word in the 4x4 grid.","Step 3: Tap the starting letter, then sequentially tap adjacent letters to trace the full word.","Step 4: Successfully trace the target number of words to win the game. If you make a wrong tap, the trail resets."],t.s)
B.aPR=s(["Before tapping the first letter, visually trace the whole path in your head to ensure it leads to the final letter.","Remember that the path can snake in any adjacent direction (up, down, left, right) but cannot revisit a cell it has already used."],t.s)
B.ajQ=new A.a8("Word Snake Trail","WORD","The objective is to trace the continuous path of a hidden word within a grid of letters.","Tap the adjacent letter cells one by one starting from the first letter to trace the complete word path.",B.au_,B.aPR)
B.aPY=s(["Step 1: Look at the prompt to see if you need a SYNONYM or ANTONYM.","Step 2: Read the large target word in the center of the screen.","Step 3: Quickly evaluate the four options and tap the correct one.","Step 4: Repeat the process as fast as possible to fill the score progress bar before the time expires."],t.s)
B.aJT=s(["Check the prompt carefully for each new word; it can switch between SYNONYM and ANTONYM.","Act fast but avoid impulsive guessing, as errors cost precious time."],t.s)
B.ajo=new A.a8("Word Surge","WORD","The objective is to rapidly identify synonyms or antonyms for the given target words to reach the target score before the timer runs out.","Tap the correct option button from the four choices displayed in the grid.",B.aPY,B.aJT)
B.aKe=s(["Step 1: Look at the letter wheel, paying special attention to the central letter.","Step 2: Spell out a word using the provided letters (minimum 3 letters) by tapping the letter buttons. The word MUST contain the central letter.","Step 3: Tap SUBMIT to check your word. If it's valid, it will be added to your found words list.","Step 4: Find the required target number of words to win the game."],t.s)
B.awE=s(["Try finding prefixes and suffixes you can make with the outer letters to attach to the central letter.","Look for the 'Pangram' - a word that uses all 7 letters provided in the wheel."],t.s)
B.aif=new A.a8("Word Wheel","WORD","The objective is to find valid words using the provided letters, where each word must include the central letter.","Tap the letter buttons to spell a word, use the backspace button to correct mistakes, and tap the SUBMIT button to enter your guess.",B.aKe,B.awE)
B.ati=s(["Step 1: Select a difficulty level (Easy, Medium, or Hard) to start the game.","Step 2: Pay close attention to the screen and count the sheep emojis as they move across from left to right.","Step 3: When all the sheep have finished passing and the input screen appears, type the total number you counted into the text field.","Step 4: Tap the 'SUBMIT ANSWER' button to verify your count."],t.s)
B.aW1=s(["Keep your eyes focused slightly off-center to see the whole screen and avoid missing fast-moving sheep.","If sheep appear in clusters, try grouping them in small sets (like 2s or 3s) mentally instead of counting by ones."],t.s)
B.ahk=new A.a8("Counting Sheep","ATTENTION","The objective is to accurately count the number of sheep that move across the screen and submit the correct total.","Tap a difficulty level to start. Watch the sheep pass, then use the keyboard to type the number and tap 'SUBMIT ANSWER'.",B.ati,B.aW1)
B.auj=s(["Step 1: During the counting phase, look at the screen and count ONLY the specified target objects.","Step 2: Tap the correct number button from the options at the bottom of the screen.","Step 3: Repeat this process for a sequence of multiple screens, remembering the correct count from each screen in order.","Step 4: During the recall phase, use the number pad to input the exact sequence of numbers you counted across all the screens."],t.s)
B.aUU=s(["Visualize the sequence of numbers as a single larger number (e.g., 3, 5, 2 becomes 'Three-Fifty-Two') to make it easier to remember.","Quickly scan for the targets rather than counting every single shape, and don't let the distractors break your concentration."],t.s)
B.akf=new A.a8("Counting Span","MEMORY","The objective is to correctly count the target items in each sequence of screens and then recall all those counts in the exact order they appeared.","Tap the number button corresponding to your count during the counting phase. Later, use the number pad to enter the sequence of counts during the recall phase.",B.auj,B.aUU)
B.atx=s(["Step 1: Observe the 3D solid and the highlighted plane slicing through it in the main view area.","Step 2: Mentally visualize the 2D cross-section shape created exactly where the plane intersects the solid.","Step 3: Look at the 2D shape options at the bottom of the screen.","Step 4: Tap the option that matches your visualized shape. Correctly identify the target number of cross-sections to win."],t.s)
B.aIY=s(["Pay close attention to the angle of the slicing plane; a diagonal cut through a cylinder makes an ellipse, not a circle.","Imagine looking directly 'down' the slicing plane perpendicular to its surface to 'see' the true 2D shape."],t.s)
B.ah1=new A.a8("Cross Section Slice","SPATIAL","The objective is to correctly identify the 2D shape that results from slicing a 3D solid with a plane.","Tap the button corresponding to the correct 2D shape at the bottom of the screen.",B.atx,B.aIY)
B.aDh=s(["Step 1: Tap on an empty square in the crossword grid. This highlights the word (Across or Down) and displays its corresponding clue below the grid.","Step 2: Read the clue and use the on-screen keyboard to type the answer. The selection will automatically advance to the next letter.","Step 3: Tap a cell again if you need to switch between the intersecting 'Across' and 'Down' clues.","Step 4: Continue solving clues until the entire grid is correctly filled."],t.s)
B.aAj=s(["Start with the shortest words or fill-in-the-blank clues, as they are usually the easiest to solve and provide crossing letters for harder words.","If you're stuck on a word, switch to the intersecting words to get more letters."],t.s)
B.ahn=new A.a8("Crossword","WORD","The objective is to fill the entire grid with the correct words based on the provided clues.","Tap a cell in the grid to select it and view its clue. Use the on-screen keyboard to enter letters. Tap the cell again to switch between Across and Down clues.",B.aDh,B.aAj)
B.aUa=s(["Step 1: Tap a dot to pick it up. The dot you picked is ringed.","Step 2: Tap a cell near that dot. Its mirror image about the dot is painted at the same time, so the region stays symmetric.","Step 3: Keep painting outward until the region is as big as it can be without touching another dot's cells.","Step 4: Move to the next dot and repeat. The board is solved when every cell belongs to exactly one dot."],t.s)
B.ay6=s(["Start with the dots closest to an edge. Their regions have the fewest places to go, so they decide themselves quickly.","A cell whose mirror image is already another dot's cannot belong to this dot. That single fact usually settles the cells around a crowded corner.","Watch for cells that would be cut off. If painting a cell would leave a gap no region can reach, that cell belongs to the dot on the other side of the gap.","When two dots are close together, one of them usually has only one way out. Find it before painting anything else."],t.s)
B.agC=new A.a8("Galaxies","LOGIC","Split the board into regions, one per dot. Every region must be symmetric about its own dot, and no region may hold two dots.","Tap a dot to pick it up, then tap the cells that belong to it. Or drag the dot onto a cell. Painting a cell also paints the cell it reflects onto. Tap a painted cell with no dot picked to clear it. The hint button shows one cell the rules can prove.",B.aUa,B.ay6)
B.aAl=s(["Step 1: Look for a peg with an empty square exactly two cells away and a peg between them. That is a jump.","Step 2: Drag that peg onto the empty square. The peg it jumped over is removed.","Step 3: Keep jumping toward the edges. A peg stranded in a corner with no partner can never be captured.","Step 4: Finish when one peg remains."],t.s)
B.at5=s(["Work from the outside in. The middle of the board is where you want your last peg, not where you want to start clearing.","Before a jump, check whether it leaves a peg isolated with no neighbour to jump over. That peg is dead weight you can never remove.","If two jumps look equally good, take the one that keeps the remaining pegs close together."],t.s)
B.ah5=new A.a8("Pegs","LOGIC","Clear the board until a single peg is left. Every jump captures the peg it hops over.","Drag a peg onto the square it should land on. Or tap a peg to pick it up and tap the landing square. The hint button shows one jump.",B.aAl,B.at5)
B.aXO=s(["Step 1: Find the tile numbered 1 and turn the block that contains it until it sits in the top left corner.","Step 2: Do the same for 2, then 3, working along the top row without disturbing what you have already placed.","Step 3: Move down a row at a time. Tiles already in place are tinted, so you can see your progress.","Step 4: Finish when every number is in its home square."],t.s)
B.aXE=s(["Solve the top row first, then the left column, then the remaining block. Each step shrinks the area you still have to turn.","A quarter turn moves four tiles at once, so prefer turns that fix two numbers rather than one.","If a turn breaks a tile you already placed, undo it: every turn has an exact opposite."],t.s)
B.ahZ=new A.a8("Twiddle","LOGIC","Turn blocks of tiles until the numbers run in order from the top left.","Drag a tile onto the square the turn would move it to. Or tap a tile to turn the block around it clockwise. The hint button outlines a block worth turning.",B.aXO,B.aXE)
B.aMg=s(["Step 1: Read the board first. A blue square paints the face the cube lands on; a white square unpaints one.","Step 2: Roll onto blue squares early, while most faces are still white.","Step 3: Watch the bottom face as you roll: it is the one that changes, and the other four edges rotate around it.","Step 4: Finish when all six faces are blue. The faces counter tracks how many are done."],t.s)
B.aXw=s(["Every roll swaps the bottom face with the square you land on, so a roll is its own inverse. If a roll makes things worse, roll back.","Plan a route that visits each blue square once rather than crossing the same square twice.","Work from a corner: a corner only has two exits, so it is the cheapest place to fix a face."],t.s)
B.aju=new A.a8("Cube","LOGIC","Roll the cube over the board until all six of its faces are blue.","Drag the cube onto a neighbouring square, or tap that square. There is no undo, but every roll can be rolled back by rolling again.",B.aMg,B.aXw)
B.aWA=s(["Step 1: Find the gems first and the mines second. A route between them is the puzzle.","Step 2: Move along one direction at a time. Each move ends against a wall, so it always changes your row or your column completely.","Step 3: Collect the gems one at a time, checking that the stop square is not a mine.","Step 4: The board is won when the last gem is collected."],t.s)
B.aIS=s(["A move always ends at a wall, so think in terms of which wall you want to end against.","Mines are only dangerous where you stop, not where you pass. Crossing a mine's row is safe.","Leave a gem near a dead end for last, so you always have somewhere to go."],t.s)
B.aj6=new A.a8("Inertia","LOGIC","Collect every gem on the board without touching a mine.","Drag the ball onto the square it would land on, or tap any square in line with it. The ball slides until a wall stops it and cannot stop halfway.",B.aWA,B.aIS)
B.aw5=s(["Step 1: Start with the region that has the most neighbours, and give it a colour.","Step 2: Colour its neighbours with the other colours, one at a time.","Step 3: Continue outward. A clash is shown immediately, so you can always see what is wrong.","Step 4: The board is done when every region has a colour and nothing glows."],t.s)
B.atL=s(["Unlike the other puzzles here, this one has many answers on purpose: any valid four-colouring is correct.","Regions that touch at a corner are not neighbours. Only a shared border constrains the colour.","If you get stuck, pick the region with the fewest remaining colours and change it first."],t.s)
B.agX=new A.a8("Map","LOGIC","Colour every region with four colours so that no two regions that share a border share a colour. Any valid colouring wins.","Tap a region to cycle its colour. A region that clashes with a neighbour glows red.",B.aw5,B.atL)
B.aJ7=s(["Step 1: Find the lines that cannot move. A wall stops its line, so those tiles are already where they will be.","Step 2: Slide a line that a misplaced tile sits in, and watch where the tile goes.","Step 3: Work pipe by pipe: join one pair, then keep that join out of the line you slide next.","Step 4: The board is won when every pipe meets a pipe."],t.s)
B.aIP=s(["A slide moves a whole line, so every tile in that line changes place at once. Count what moves with it.","Slides come in pairs: sliding the same line back restores the board.","Leave the line with the fewest tiles until last; it has the least room for mistakes."],t.s)
B.aks=new A.a8("Netslide","LOGIC","Slide rows and columns until every pipe is joined to a pipe.","Drag a tile one square along its row or column: the whole line slides round one step. Tiles never rotate. A wall across a line blocks it.",B.aJ7,B.aIP)
B.aBl=s(["Step 1: Look for the colour that covers the most board and start there.","Step 2: Remove groups that join two other groups of the same colour once they fall together.","Step 3: Keep the small groups for last; they are the ones that strand single squares.","Step 4: The board is cleared when no group of two or more is left."],t.s)
B.azS=s(["A single square can never be removed, so avoid cutting a group down to one.","Removing a tall group collapses the columns and can merge two groups that were apart.","Play from the bottom where you can: a collapse changes more of the board than a removal at the top."],t.s)
B.ahu=new A.a8("Same Game","LOGIC","Clear the board by removing groups of two or more squares of the same colour.","Tap a group of two or more connected squares of the same colour to remove it. The squares above fall and the columns close up.",B.aBl,B.azS)
B.aXv=s(["Step 1: Start from the given numbers. A given pins down the cell it sits in, and often the arrow into it.","Step 2: Follow each arrow as far as it can go along its line. The arrow runs along the whole ray, so the cell it means can be any distance away.","Step 3: An arrow that has only one cell left in its ray is decided for you: link it.","Step 4: Finish when one chain runs from 1 to the last number with every arrow pointing the way."],t.s)
B.aLG=s(["An arrow never points at a neighbour by default: it points at whatever lies along its line, so look to the end of the ray first.","Work backwards from the highest given number as well as forwards; both ends are constrained.","Every cell is used exactly once, so a number you cannot place in one ray is a reason to re-read the others."],t.s)
B.agQ=new A.a8("Signpost","LOGIC","Number every cell from 1 to the last so that each cell points at the cell holding the next number.","Drag a cell onto the cell it points at, or tap one cell and then the other. An arrow turns solid once its cell points somewhere; tapping that cell again takes the link back.",B.aXv,B.aLG)
B.ri=new A.an(B.b3Y,[B.aj0,B.alk,B.ajm,B.aiX,B.aiV,B.aiE,B.ald,B.agB,B.aj9,B.aj8,B.ahf,B.alm,B.ags,B.alj,B.ajk,B.aj3,B.agv,B.agr,B.aik,B.ajB,B.aih,B.akZ,B.agN,B.akr,B.ahB,B.ah6,B.agy,B.agu,B.akM,B.ak9,B.aj1,B.ak1,B.agz,B.ahJ,B.ahg,B.ajd,B.aiR,B.ajJ,B.akh,B.agZ,B.ak5,B.ahi,B.ajD,B.agK,B.agL,B.aib,B.ahl,B.aln,B.ali,B.akY,B.ak_,B.al9,B.ahc,B.aka,B.ahj,B.ahH,B.ahF,B.agq,B.ahI,B.ahG,B.aiG,B.ahC,B.aha,B.akW,B.ak4,B.ahd,B.akF,B.ajq,B.akn,B.aiK,B.ain,B.akx,B.agG,B.akI,B.akR,B.agO,B.ajZ,B.akb,B.aiO,B.akD,B.ahR,B.agT,B.aky,B.ahE,B.aip,B.all,B.agm,B.aja,B.ahx,B.alg,B.aiU,B.air,B.ai5,B.agI,B.al5,B.agt,B.agV,B.ahm,B.ah7,B.ahb,B.akU,B.aiz,B.aiJ,B.aiy,B.akH,B.ajl,B.agD,B.aia,B.ahw,B.ahS,B.agE,B.al0,B.ahL,B.ajn,B.aig,B.akm,B.ahA,B.ajT,B.ajc,B.ajb,B.akk,B.ai1,B.aio,B.aii,B.ahQ,B.aiw,B.akl,B.ajp,B.akJ,B.aiM,B.al4,B.ai6,B.aiu,B.ajU,B.ajS,B.aj4,B.ajC,B.aiL,B.ajr,B.akv,B.ah_,B.aiq,B.ajX,B.ajx,B.aiS,B.akV,B.al_,B.ajw,B.aiD,B.ala,B.ai7,B.aiN,B.ahD,B.akO,B.akX,B.aiI,B.ajR,B.ale,B.ahr,B.aiA,B.ahp,B.aij,B.aiY,B.aim,B.akP,B.ajO,B.aji,B.al3,B.al1,B.aiT,B.ai8,B.akj,B.aj5,B.agP,B.aj_,B.ajP,B.ak2,B.akT,B.ak7,B.ah9,B.akp,B.al2,B.aic,B.agp,B.ai2,B.ajW,B.ak6,B.ajz,B.ajY,B.aiH,B.ahW,B.agU,B.akd,B.alh,B.aiP,B.ahz,B.ah3,B.ai3,B.aix,B.ajf,B.akw,B.ah8,B.agM,B.aiC,B.ah0,B.alc,B.alb,B.ak3,B.ahh,B.ajg,B.ajt,B.ago,B.akB,B.ahy,B.akQ,B.agJ,B.akc,B.ah2,B.ai9,B.ahM,B.ake,B.ai0,B.ahV,B.ajV,B.akq,B.aki,B.ail,B.aho,B.agW,B.al8,B.ak0,B.akz,B.agn,B.akK,B.agA,B.ako,B.ahX,B.aid,B.ah4,B.agw,B.ai4,B.akC,B.ahe,B.al6,B.ajy,B.agF,B.aku,B.ajs,B.aht,B.aj2,B.ajK,B.aiW,B.ajI,B.akA,B.ahO,B.ahK,B.alf,B.aiQ,B.ajj,B.aie,B.ais,B.akN,B.ahq,B.ak8,B.alp,B.aiF,B.agY,B.ahv,B.aje,B.ajE,B.agS,B.ajh,B.aiv,B.ajL,B.ajG,B.ajv,B.agH,B.ajF,B.ahs,B.ajN,B.akS,B.agx,B.ahN,B.aiZ,B.akE,B.ait,B.ajM,B.alo,B.ahY,B.ajA,B.al7,B.ahU,B.ahP,B.ai_,B.aj7,B.aiB,B.ajH,B.akG,B.akt,B.akL,B.akg,B.agR,B.ahT,B.ajQ,B.ajo,B.aif,B.ahk,B.akf,B.ah1,B.ahn,B.agC,B.ah5,B.ahZ,B.aju,B.aj6,B.agX,B.aks,B.ahu,B.agQ],A.aM("an<x,a8>"))
B.ba_=new A.by(B.yG,!1,!1,!1,!1,B.ap)
B.Z5=new A.by(B.kv,!1,!1,!1,!1,B.ap)
